TURATH_CHUNK(31,[{"num":6200,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَرَأَيْتَ لَوْ نَزَلْتَ وَادِيًا وَفِيهِ شَجَرَةٌ قَدْ أُكِلَ مِنْهَا، وَوَجَدْتَ شَجَرًا لَمْ يُؤْكَلْ مِنْهَا، فِي أَيِّهَا كُنْتَ تُرْتِعُ بَعِيرَكَ؟ قَالَ: فِي الَّذِي لَمْ يُرْتَعْ مِنْهَا. تَعْنِي أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمْ يَتَزَوَّجْ بِكْرًا غَيْرَهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5077) عن إسماعيل بن عبد الله، قال: حدثني أخي، عن سليمان ( هو ابن بلال )، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تفضيل نكاح الأبكار على الثيبات إلا للمصلحة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5077).","chapter_en":"Chapter on preferring marriage to virgins over previously married women, except when there is a benefit in doing otherwise","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, if you were to camp in a valley in which there was a tree that had already been grazed from, and you found trees that had not been grazed from, which would you let your camel graze from?” He said, “From the one that has not been grazed from.” Meaning that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not marry any virgin besides her."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10393],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5077)."},{"num":6201,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: تُنْكَحُ الْمَرْأَةُ لأَرْبَعٍ: لِمَالِهَا، وَلِحَسَبِهَا، وَجَمَالِهَا، وَلِدِينِهَا، فَاظْفَرْ بِذَاتِ الدِّينِ تَرِبَتْ يَدَاكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5090)، ومسلم في الرضاع (1466: 53) كلاهما من طريق يحيى بن سعيد (وهو القطان)، عن عبيد الله، حدثني سعيد بن أبي سعيد، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الكفاءة هي الدين وحده، والترغيب في اختيار الزوجة الصالحة ذات الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5090) and Muslim (1466:53).","chapter_en":"Chapter on what has been reported that compatibility is in religion alone, and encouraging the choice of a righteous, religious wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “A woman is married for four things: for her wealth, her lineage, her beauty, and her religion. So attain the one with religion, may your hands be covered with dust.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى: (وَالَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا هَبْ لَنَا مِنْ أَزْوَاجِنَا وَذُرِّيَّاتِنَا قُرَّةَ أَعْيُنٍ) [الفرقان: ٧٤]"],"en":["Allah Most High said:","“And those who say: Our Lord, grant us from our spouses and our offspring comfort to our eyes.” [Al-Furqan: 74]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5090)، ومسلم (1466: 53)."},{"num":6202,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ:  تَزَوَّجْتُ امْرَأَةً. فَقَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هَلْ تَزَوَّجْتَ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: أَبِكْرًا أَمْ ثَيِّبًا؟ قُلْتُ: ثَيِّبًا. قَالَ: فَأَيْنَ أَنْتَ مِنَ الْعَذَارَى وَلِعَابِهَا؟","قَالَ شُعْبَةُ: فَذَكَرْتُهُ لِعَمْرِو بْنِ دِينَارٍ. فَقَالَ: قَدْ سَمِعْتَهُ مِنْ جَابِرٍ. وَإِنَّمَا قَالَ: فَهَلَّا جَارِيَةً تُلَاعِبُهَا وَتُلَاعِبُكَ؟."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح ( 5080) ومسلم في الرضاع (715: 55) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، حدّثنا محارب قال: سمعت جابر بن عبد الله يقول: فذكره. واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الكفاءة هي الدين وحده، والترغيب في اختيار الزوجة الصالحة ذات الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5080) and Muslim (715:55).","chapter_en":"Chapter on what has been reported that compatibility is in religion alone, and encouraging the choice of a righteous, religious wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: I married a woman, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Have you married?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “A virgin or a previously married woman?” I said, “A previously married woman.” He said, “Then where are you with young virgins and their playfulness?” Shu‘bah said: I mentioned it to ‘Amr ibn Dinar, and he said: I heard it from Jabir, and he only said: “Why not a young girl that you may play with her and she may play with you?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6199,6331],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5080)، ومسلم (715: 55)."},{"num":6203,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَطَاءٍ، أَخْبَرَنِي جَابِرُ بْنُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ:  تَزَوَّجْتُ امْرَأَةً فِي عَهْدِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَقِيتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا جَابِرُ تَزَوَّجْتَ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: بِكْرٌ أَمْ ثَيِّبٌ؟ قُلْتُ: ثَيِّبٌ. قَالَ: فَهَلَّا بِكْرًا تُلَاعِبُهَا؟ قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ لِي أَخَوَاتٍ فَخَشِيتُ أَنْ تَدْخُلَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَهُنَّ. قَالَ: فَذَاكَ إِذَنْ، إِنَّ الْمَرْأَةَ تُنْكَحُ عَلَى دِينِهَا، وَمَالِهَا، وَجَمَالِهَا، فَعَلَيْكَ بِذَاتِ الدِّينِ تَرِبَتْ يَدَاكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الرضاع (54:715) عن محمد بن عبد الله بن نُمير، حدثنا أبي، حدثنا عبد الملك بن أبي سليمان، عن عطاء، أخبرني جابر بن عبد الله، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الكفاءة هي الدين وحده، والترغيب في اختيار الزوجة الصالحة ذات الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (715:54).","chapter_en":"Chapter on what has been reported that compatibility is in religion alone, and encouraging the choice of a righteous, religious wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: I married a woman during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ met me and said, “O Jabir, have you married?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “A virgin or a previously married woman?” I said, “A previously married woman.” He said, “Why not a virgin, so that you may play with her?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have sisters, and I feared that she would come between me and them.” He said, “Then that is fine. A woman is married for her religion, her wealth, and her beauty, so hold fast to the one with religion, may your hands be covered with dust.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (54:715)."},{"num":6204,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: تُنْكَحُ الْمَرْأَةُ عَلَى إِحْدَى خِصَالٍ ثَلَاثٍ: تُنْكَحُ الْمَرْأَةُ عَلَى مَالِهَا، وَتُنْكَحُ الْمَرْأَةُ عَلَى جَمَالِهَا، وَتُنْكَحُ الْمَرْأَةُ عَلَى دِينِهَا، فَخُذْ ذَاتَ الدِّينِ وَالْخُلُقِ تَرِبَتْ يَمِينُكَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد ( 11765) وأبو يعلى (1012) والبزار – كشف الأستار (1403) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4037) والحاكم (2680) كلهم من طريق محمد بن موسى الفطري المدني، عن سعد بن إسحاق، عن عمته، عن أبي سعيد الخدري فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الكفاءة هي الدين وحده، والترغيب في اختيار الزوجة الصالحة ذات الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (11765), Abu Ya‘la (1012), al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1403), and authenticated by Ibn Hibban (4037).","chapter_en":"Chapter on what has been reported that compatibility is in religion alone, and encouraging the choice of a righteous, religious wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A woman is married for one of three qualities: she is married for her wealth, she is married for her beauty, and she is married for her religion. So take the one with religion and good character, may your right hand be covered with dust.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (11765)، وأبو يعلى (1012)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (1403)، وصححه ابن حبان (4037)."},{"num":6205,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرٍو، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ:  الدُّنْيَا مَتَاعٌ، وَخَيْرُ مَتَاعِ الدُّنْيَا الْمَرْأَةُ الصَّالِحَةُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الرضاع (1467) عن محمد بن عبد الله بن نُمير الهَمْدانيّ، حدّثنا حَيْوة، أخبرني شرحبيل بن شريك، أنه سمع أبا عبد الرحمن الحبليّ يحدّث عن عبدالله بن عمروبن العاص فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الكفاءة هي الدين وحده، والترغيب في اختيار الزوجة الصالحة ذات الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1467).","chapter_en":"Chapter on what has been reported that compatibility is in religion alone, and encouraging the choice of a righteous, religious wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This world is a temporary enjoyment, and the best enjoyment of this world is a righteous woman.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1467)."},{"num":6206,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَهْلٍ، قَالَ: مَرَّ رَجُلٌ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: مَا تَقُولُونَ فِي هَذَا. قَالُوا: حَرِيٌّ إِنْ خَطَبَ أَنْ يُنْكَحَ، وَإِنْ شَفَعَ أَنْ يُشَفَّعَ، وَإِنْ قَالَ أَنْ يُسْتَمَعَ. قَالَ: ثُمَّ سَكَتَ. فَمَرَّ رَجُلٌ مِنَ فُقَرَاءِ الْمُسْلِمِينَ، فَقَالَ: مَا تَقُولُونَ فِي هَذَا. قَالُوا: حَرِيٌّ إِنْ خَطَبَ أَنْ لاَ يُنْكَحَ، وَإِنْ شَفَعَ أَنْ لاَ يُشَفَّعَ، وَإِنْ قَالَ أَنْ لاَ يُسْتَمَعَ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هَذَا خَيْرٌ مِنْ مِلْءِ الأَرْضِ مِثْلَ هَذَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5091) عن إبراهيم بن حمزة، حدثنا ابن أبي حازم، عن أبيه، عن سهل، قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الكفاءة هي الدين وحده، والترغيب في اختيار الزوجة الصالحة ذات الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5091).","chapter_en":"Chapter on what has been reported that compatibility is in religion alone, and encouraging the choice of a righteous, religious wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Sa‘d said: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “What do you say about this one?” They said: He is deserving, if he proposes, to be married to; if he intercedes, to have his intercession accepted; and if he speaks, to be listened to. Then he remained silent. Then a poor man from among the Muslims passed by, and he said, “What do you say about this one?” They said: He is deserving, if he proposes, not to be married to; if he intercedes, not to have his intercession accepted; and if he speaks, not to be listened to. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “This one is better than the whole earth filled with the likes of that one.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5091)."},{"num":6207,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَرْبَعٌ مِنَ السَّعَادَةِ! الْمَرْأَةُ الصَّالِحَةُ، وَالْمَسْكَنُ الْوَاسِعُ، وَالْجَارُ الصَّالِحُ، وَالْمَرْكَبُ الْهَنِيءُ، وَأَرْبَعٌ مِنَ الشَّقَاوَةِ: الْجَارُ السُّوءُ، وَالْمَرْأَةُ السُّوءُ، وَالْمَسْكَنُ الضِّيقُ، وَالْمَرْكَبُ السُّوءُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (4032) عن محمد بن إسحاق بن إبراهيم مولى ثقيف، قال: حدثنا محمد بن عبد العزيز بن أبي رِزقة، قال: حدثنا الفضل بن موسى، عن عبد الله بن سعيد بن أبي هند، عن إسماعيل بن محمد بن سعد، عن أبيه، عن جده فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الكفاءة هي الدين وحده، والترغيب في اختيار الزوجة الصالحة ذات الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Hibban in his Sahih (4032).","chapter_en":"Chapter on what has been reported that compatibility is in religion alone, and encouraging the choice of a righteous, religious wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sa‘d ibn Abi Waqqas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Four things are from happiness: a righteous wife, a spacious home, a good neighbor, and a comfortable mount. And four things are from misery: a bad neighbor, a bad wife, a cramped home, and a bad mount.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14182],"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (4032)."},{"num":6208,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ رَجُلٍ من أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: تَبًّا لِلذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقْتُ مَعَ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! قَوْلُكَ: تَبًّا لِلذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ مَاذَا؟ فَقَالَ: لِسَانًا ذَاكِرًا وَقَلْبًا شَاكِرًا، زوجة تُعِينُ عَلَى الْآخِرَةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23101) عن محمد بن جعفر، حدثنا شعبة، حدثنا سَلْم قـال: سمعت عبد الله بن أبي الهذيل قـال: حدثني صاحب لي أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الكفاءة هي الدين وحده، والترغيب في اختيار الزوجة الصالحة ذات الدين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (23101).","chapter_en":"Chapter on what has been reported that compatibility is in religion alone, and encouraging the choice of a righteous, religious wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["A man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Woe to gold and silver.” He said: So I went with ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, your statement, “Woe to gold and silver” - then what should one have? He said: “A tongue that remembers Allah, a grateful heart, a wife who helps one toward the Hereafter.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “Woe to gold and silver,” means destruction for the one who hoards them and does not pay their due alms.","His statement, “then what?” means: then what should we acquire, as in the narration of Thawban that comes later."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23101)."},{"num":6209,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن فَاطِمَةَ بنت قَيْسٍ أَنَّ أَبَا عمرو بْنِ حفص طلقها البتة فذكرت الْحَدِيثَ. قَالَتْ: فَلَمَّا حَلَلْتُ ذَكَرْتُ لَهُ أَنَّ مُعَاوِيَةَ بْنَ أَبِي سُفْيَانَ، وَأَبَا جَهْمِ بْنَ هِشَامٍ خَطَبَانِي. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَمَّا أَبُو جَهْمٍ فَلاَ يَضَعُ عَصَاهُ عَنْ عَاتِقِهِ، وَأَمَّا مُعَاوِيَةُ فَصُعْلُوكٌ لاَ مَالَ لَهُ، انْكِحِي أُسَامَةَ بْنَ زَيْدٍ. قَالَتْ: فَكَرِهْتُهُ ثُمَّ قَالَ: انْكِحِي أُسَامَةَ بْنَ زَيْدٍ. فَنَكَحْتُهُ. فَجَعَلَ اللَّهُ فِي ذَلِكَ خَيْرًا، وَاغْتَبَطْتُ بِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في الطلاق (73) عن عبد الله بن يزيد مولى الأسود بن سفيان، عن أبي سلمة، بن عبد الرحمن بن عوف، عن فاطمة بنت قيس فذكرته. ومن طريق مالك رواه مسلم في الطلاق (1480)","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تزوج المولى العربية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Malik (73) and Muslim (1480).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a freedman marrying an Arab woman","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Fatimah bint Qays reported that Abu ‘Amr ibn Hafs divorced her irrevocably. She mentioned the rest of the narration and said: When my waiting period ended, I mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ that Mu‘awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm ibn Hisham had proposed to me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “As for Abu Jahm, he does not put down his staff from his shoulder; and as for Mu‘awiyah, he is poor and has no wealth. Marry Usamah ibn Zayd.” She said: I disliked him. Then he said: “Marry Usamah ibn Zayd.” So I married him, and Allah placed much good in that, and I was pleased with it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (73)، ومسلم (1480)."},{"num":6210,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا أَنَّ أَبَا حُذَيْفَةَ بْنَ عُتْبَةَ بْنِ رَبِيعَةَ بْنِ عَبْدِ شَمْسٍ،، وَكَانَ، مِمَّنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَبَنَّى سَالِمًا، وَأَنْكَحَهُ بِنْتَ أَخِيهِ هِنْدَ بِنْتَ الْوَلِيدِ بْنِ عُتْبَةَ بْنِ رَبِيعَةَ، وَهْوَ مَوْلًى لاِمْرَأَةٍ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في النكاح ( 5088) عن أبي اليمان، أخبرنا شُعيب عن الزهري، قال: أخبرني عروة بن الزبير، عن عائشة فذكرته مثله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تزوج المولى العربية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5088).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a freedman marrying an Arab woman","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah reported that Abu Hudhayfah ibn ‘Utbah ibn Rabi‘ah ibn ‘Abd Shams - and he was among those who witnessed Badr with the Prophet ﷺ - had adopted Salim and married him to the daughter of his brother, Hind bint al-Walid ibn ‘Utbah ibn Rabi‘ah, and he was the freedman of a woman from the Ansar."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5088)."},{"num":6211,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، أَنَّ أَبَا هِنْدٍ، حَجَمَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي الْيَافُوخِ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَا بَنِي بَيَاضَةَ، أَنْكِحُوا أَبَا هِنْدٍ، وَانْكِحُوا إِلَيْهِ. قَالَ وَإِنْ كَانَ فِي شَىْءٍ مِمَّا تَدَاوَوْنَ بِهِ خَيْرٌ فَالْحِجَامَةُ.","وفي رواية: كان حجاماً."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2102) عن عبد الواحد بن غياث، حدثنا حماد، حدثنا محمد بن عمرو، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب لا يرد نكاح غير الكفء إذا رضيت المرأة ووليها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2102), al-Daraqutni (3/300–301), Ibn Hibban (4067), and al-Hakim (2/164).","chapter_en":"Chapter on not rejecting the marriage of one who is not socially equal if the woman and her guardian are pleased","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported that Abu Hind cupped the Prophet ﷺ on the crown of his head, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “O Banu Bayadah, marry Abu Hind [to your women], and seek his daughters in marriage.” And he said: “If there is any good in what you use for treatment, then it is cupping.” And in one narration: “He was a cupper.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “and seek marriage from him,” means: ask for his daughters in marriage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2102)، والدارقطني (3794)، وابن حبان (4067)، والحاكم (2/164)."},{"num":6212,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ أَنَّهَا قَالَتْ: كَانَ فِي بَرِيرَةَ ثَلاَثُ سُنن، فَكَانَتْ إِحْدَى السُّنَنِ الثلاث أَنَّهَا أُعْتِقَتْ فخُيِّرتْ فِي زَوْجِهَا. وَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْوَلاَءُ لِمَنْ أَعْتَقَ وَدَخَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَالْبُرْمَةُ تَفُورُ بِلَحْمٍ فقُرّب إِلَيْهِ خُبْزٌ وَأُدْمٌ مِنْ أُدْمِ الْبَيْتِ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَلَمْ أَرَ الْبُرْمَةَ فِيهَا لَحْمٌ؟ فقالو: بَلَى. يَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ. وَلَكِنْ لَحْمٌ تُصُدِّقَ بِهِ عَلَى بَرِيرَةَ، وَأَنْتَ لاَ تَأْكُلُ الصَّدَقَةَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ هُوَ عَلَيْهَا صَدَقَةٌ، وهو لَنَا هَدِيَّةٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الطلاق (29) عن ربيعة بن أبي عبد الرحمن، عن القاسم بن محمد، عن عائشة فذكرته. ورواه البخاري في الطلاق (5279)، ومسلم في الطلاق (1504: 14) كلاهما من طريق مالك، به.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب اعتبار الحرية في الكفاءة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (29), al-Bukhari (5279), and Muslim (1504:14).","chapter_en":"Chapter on considering freedom in compatibility","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: There were three legal rulings connected to Barirah. One of those three rulings was that when she was freed, she was given the choice regarding her husband. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The right of patronage belongs to the one who frees.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while a cooking pot was boiling with meat, and bread and ordinary household seasoning were brought near to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Did I not see the pot with meat in it?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but it is meat that was given in charity to Barirah, and you do not eat charity. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “For her it is charity, and for us it is a gift.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (29)، والبخاري (5279)، ومسلم (1504: 14)."},{"num":6213,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، فِي قِصَّةِ بَرِيرَةَ قَالَتْ: كَانَ زَوْجُهَا عَبْدًا، فَخَيَّرَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  فَاخْتَارَتْ نَفْسَهَا، وَلَوْ كَانَ حُرًّا لَمْ يُخَيِّرْهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الطلاق (1504: 9) من طرق عن جرير بن عبد الحميد، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اعتبار الحرية في الكفاءة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1504:9).","chapter_en":"Chapter on considering freedom in compatibility","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: The husband of Barirah was a slave, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice, and she chose herself. If he had been a free man, he would not have given her that choice."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1504: 9)."},{"num":6214,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، أَنَّ زَوْجَ، بَرِيرَةَ كَانَ عَبْدًا يُقَالُ لَهُ مُغِيثٌ، كَأَنِّي أَنْظُرُ إِلَيْهِ يَطُوفُ خَلْفَهَا يَبْكِي، وَدُمُوعُهُ تَسِيلُ عَلَى لِحْيَتِهِ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِعَبَّاسٍ: يَا عَبَّاسُ، أَلاَ تَعْجَبُ مِنْ حُبِّ مُغِيثٍ بَرِيرَةَ، وَمِنْ بُغْضِ بَرِيرَةَ مُغِيثًا. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَوْ رَاجَعْتِهِ. قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ تَأْمُرُنِي؟ قَالَ: إِنَّمَا أَنَا أَشْفَعُ. قَالَتْ: لاَ حَاجَةَ لِي فِيهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الطلاق (5283) عن محمد، أخبرنا عبدالوهاب حدثنا خالد، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اعتبار الحرية في الكفاءة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5283).","chapter_en":"Chapter on considering freedom in compatibility","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas reported that the husband of Barirah was a slave named Mughith. It is as if I can still see him going around behind her, weeping, with tears flowing down his beard. Then the Prophet ﷺ said to al-‘Abbas: “O ‘Abbas, are you not amazed at the love of Mughith for Barirah, and the dislike of Barirah for Mughith?” Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “Why do you not return to him?” She said: O Messenger of Allah, are you commanding me? He said: “I am only interceding.” She said: I have no need of him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[6735],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5283)."},{"num":6215,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: ذَاكَ مُغِيثٌ عَبْدُ بَنِي فُلاَنٍ ـ يَعْنِي زَوْجَ بَرِيرَةَ، ـ كَأَنِّي أَنْظُرُ إِلَيْهِ يَتْبَعُهَا فِي سِكَكِ الْمَدِينَةِ، يَبْكِي عَلَيْهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الطلاق (5281) عن عبد الأعلى بن حماد، حدثنا وُهيب، حدثنا أيوب، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اعتبار الحرية في الكفاءة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5281).","chapter_en":"Chapter on considering freedom in compatibility","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: That was Mughith, the slave of such-and-such people - meaning the husband of Barirah. It is as though I can still see him following her through the streets of Madinah, weeping over her."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5281)."},{"num":6216,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، أَنَّ زَوْجَ بَرِيرَةَ كَانَ عَبْدًا أَسْوَدَ يُسَمَّى مُغِيثًا، قَالَ: فَكُنْتُ أَرَاهُ يَتْبَعُهَا فِي سِكَكِ الْمَدِينَةِ، يَعْصِرُ عَيْنَيْهِ عَلَيْهَا، قَالَ: وَقَضَى فِيهَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَرْبَعَ قَضِيَّاتٍ: إِنَّ مَوَالِيَهَا اشْتَرَطُوا الْوَلاءَ، فَقَضَى النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْوَلاءَ لِمَنْ أَعْتَقَ وَخَيَّرَهَا، فَاخْتَارَتْ نَفْسَهَا، فَأَمَرَهَا أَنْ تَعْتَدَّ، قَالَ: وَتُصُدِّقَ عَلَيْهَا بِصَدَقَةٍ، فَأَهْدَتْ مِنْهَا إِلَى عَائِشَةَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا، فَذَكَرَتْ ذَلِكَ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: هُوَ عَلَيْهَا صَدَقَةٌ، وَإِلَيْنَا هَدِيَّةٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (2542) والطبراني (11826) والبيهقي (14264) كلهم من حديث همام قال: أخبرنا قتادة، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره. وإسناده صحيح، وهو من هذا الوجه في صحيح البخاري (5280) مختصرا بقول ابن عباس: رأيته عبداً- يعني زوج بريرة.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اعتبار الحرية في الكفاءة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ahmad (2542), al-Tabarani (11826), and al-Bayhaqi (7/221–222).","chapter_en":"Chapter on considering freedom in compatibility","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas reported that the husband of Barirah was a black slave named Mughith. He said: I used to see him following her through the streets of Madinah, crying over her. He said: The Prophet ﷺ gave four rulings regarding her case: her masters had stipulated that the right of patronage would remain with them, so the Prophet ﷺ ruled, “The right of patronage belongs to the one who frees.” He gave her the choice, and she chose herself. He ordered her to observe her waiting period. And charity was given to her, then she gifted some of it to ‘A’ishah, and when that was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ he said, “For her it is charity, and for us it is a gift.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (2542)، والطبراني (11826)، والبيهقي (14264)."},{"num":6217,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَيَّرَ بَرِيرَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجة (2078) عن إسماعيل بن ثوبة، حدثنا عباد بن العوّام، عن يحيى بن أبي إسحاق، عن عبدالرحمن بن أُذَينة، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اعتبار الحرية في الكفاءة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Majah (2078).","chapter_en":"Chapter on considering freedom in compatibility","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Barirah the choice."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (2078)."},{"num":6218,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لاَ عَدْوَى، وَلاَ طِيَرَةَ، وَلاَ هَامَةَ، وَلاَ صَفَرَ، وَفِرَّ مِنَ الْمَجْذُومِ كَمَا تَفِرُّ مِنَ الأَسَدِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الطب (5807) قال: وقال عفان، حدثنا سليم بن حيان، حدثنا سعيد بن ميناء قال: سمعت أبا هريرة يقول: فذكره","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اعتبار السلامة من العيوب في الكفاءة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5707).","chapter_en":"Chapter on considering freedom from defects in suitability","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no contagious transmission by itself, no evil omen, no owl-omen, and no bad luck in Safar; and flee from the leper as you would flee from a lion.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[11635,11651],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5807)."},{"num":6219,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يُورِد مُمرِض عَلَى مُصحّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الطب (5774) ومسلم في السلام، كلاهما من حديث ابن شهاب، عن أبي سلمة بن عبدالله بن عوف، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب اعتبار السلامة من العيوب في الكفاءة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5774) and Muslim (2221) in the Book of Greetings.","chapter_en":"Chapter on considering freedom from defects in suitability","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A diseased animal should not be brought to one that is healthy.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11650],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5774)، ومسلم (2221) في السلام."},{"num":6220,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن فَاطِمَةَ بنت قَيْسٍ تَقُولُ:  إِنَّ زَوْجَهَا طَلَّقَهَا ثَلَاثًا، فَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ لَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سُكْنَى وَلَا نَفَقَةً. قَالَتْ: قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا حَلَلْتِ فَآذِنِينِي، فَآذَنْتُهُ، فَخَطَبَهَا مُعَاوِيَةُ، وَأَبُو جَهْمٍ، وَأُسَامَةُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَمَّا مُعَاوِيَةُ فَرَجُلٌ تَرِبٌ لَا مَالَ لَهُ، وَأَمَّا أَبُو جَهْمٍ فَرَجُلٌ ضَرَّابٌ، لِلنِّسَاءِ، وَلَكِنْ أُسَامَةُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الطلاق (1480: 47) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا وكيع، حدثنا سفيان، عن أبي بكر بن الجهم بن صُخير العدوى قـال: سمعت فاطمة بنت قيس تقول: فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الترغيب في اختيار الزوج الصالح سواء كان له مال أم لا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1480:47).","chapter_en":"Chapter on encouraging the choice of a righteous husband whether he has wealth or not","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Fatimah bint Qays said: Her husband divorced her with a final triple divorce, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not assign for her housing or maintenance. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “When your waiting period ends, inform me.” So I informed him. Then Mu‘awiyah, Abu Jahm, and Usamah ibn Zayd proposed to her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “As for Mu‘awiyah, he is a poor man with no wealth. As for Abu Jahm, he is a man who beats women. But Usamah ibn Zayd…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1480: 47)."},{"num":6221,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِيهِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ أَحْسَابَ أَهْلِ الدُّنْيَا الَّذِي يَذْهَبُونَ إِلَيْهِ، هَذَا الْمَالُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3225) وأحمد (22990) والقضاعي في مسند الشهاب (982) وصحّحه ابن حبان (699، 700) والحاكم (2689) والبيهقي (7/135) كلهم من حديث حسين بن واقد قال: حدثني عبد الله بن بريدة، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الترغيب في اختيار الزوج الصالح سواء كان له مال أم لا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3225), Ahmad (22990), and authenticated by Ibn Hibban (699).","chapter_en":"Chapter on encouraging the choice of a righteous husband whether he has wealth or not","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What the people of this world regard as status is this wealth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[15243],"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3225)، وأحمد (22990)، وصححه ابن حبان (699)."},{"num":6222,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مَسْرُوقٍ، وَعَمْرِو بْنِ عُتْبَةَ، أَنَّهُمَا كَتَبَا إِلَى سُبَيْعَةَ بِنْتِ الْحَارِثِ يَسْأَلاَنِهَا عَنْ أَمْرِهَا، فَكَتَبَتْ إِلَيْهِمَا....-الْحَدِيثَ مُطَوَّلًا كَمَا سَيَأْتِي-، وَفِي آخِرِهِ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنْ وَجَدْتِ زَوْجًا صَالِحًا فَتَزَوَّجِي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (2028) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا علي بن مسهر، عن داود بن أبي هند، عن الشعبي، عن مسروق وعمرو بن عتبة فذكراه. وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الترغيب في اختيار الزوج الصالح سواء كان له مال أم لا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Majah (2028).","chapter_en":"Chapter on encouraging the choice of a righteous husband whether he has wealth or not","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Masruq and ‘Amr ibn ‘Utbah wrote to Subay‘ah bint al-Harith asking her about her case - and she wrote back to them the full narration, which will come later - and at its end the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you find a righteous husband, then marry.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (2028).","voc":["ibnmajah",2028]},{"num":6223,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: خَيْرُ نِسَاءٍ رَكِبْنَ الإِبِلَ صَالِحُو نِسَاءِ قُرَيْشٍ، أَحْنَاهُ عَلَى وَلَدٍ فِي صِغَرِهِ، وَأَرْعَاهُ عَلَى زَوْجٍ فِي ذَاتِ يَدِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5082) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2527) كلاهما من حديث أبي الزناد، عن الأعرج، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر صفات خير النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5082) and Muslim (2527).","chapter_en":"Chapter on mentioning the qualities of the best women","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The best women who have ridden camels are the righteous women of Quraysh: the most compassionate toward a child in his young age, and the most careful regarding her husband’s wealth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[6325],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5082)، ومسلم (2527)."},{"num":6224,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَطَبَ أُمَّ هَانِئٍ بِنْتَ أَبِي طَالِبٍ. فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنِّي قَدْ كَبِرْتُ وَلِي عِيَالٌ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: خَيْرُ نِسَاءٍ رَكِبْنَ الإبل، نِسَاءٍ قُرَيْشٍ، أَحْنَاهُ عَلَى وَلَدٍ فِي صِغَرِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2527: 201) من طريق عبد الرزاق، أخبرنا معمر، عن الزهري، عن ابن المسيب، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر صفات خير النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2527:201).","chapter_en":"Chapter on mentioning the qualities of the best women","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ proposed to Umm Hani’ bint Abi Talib. She said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have grown old and I have dependents.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The best women who have ridden camels are the women of Quraysh, the most compassionate toward a child in his young age.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10462],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2527: 201)."},{"num":6225,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قِيلَ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ! صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَىُّ النِّسَاءِ خَيْرٌ؟ قَالَ: الَّتِي تَسُرُّهُ إِذَا نَظَرَ، وَتُطِيعُهُ إِذَا أَمَرَ، وَلاَ تُخَالِفُهُ فِي نَفْسِهَا وَمَالِهَا بِمَا يَكْرَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3231) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا الليث، عن ابن عجلان، عن سعيد بن أبي سعيد المقبري، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر صفات خير النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3231), Ahmad (7421), and al-Bayhaqi (7/82).","chapter_en":"Chapter on mentioning the qualities of the best women","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, which women are best?” He said, “The one who pleases him when he looks at her, obeys him when he commands her, and does not oppose him concerning herself or his wealth in a way he dislikes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3231)، وأحمد (7421)، والبيهقي (13477)."},{"num":6226,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن سلاّم أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: خَيْرُ النِّسَاءِ تَسُرُّكَ إِذَا أَبْصَرْتَ، وَتُطِيعُكَ إِذَا أَمَرْتَ، وَتَحْفَظُ غَيْبَتَكَ فِي نَفْسِهَا وَمَالِكَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (14/ح 386) عن العباس بن الفضل الأسفاطي، حدثنا موسى بن إسماعيل، حدثنا زُريك بن أبي زُريك، عن معاوية بن قُرّة، عن عبدالله بن سلاّم قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر صفات خير النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Mu‘jam al-Kabir (14/338, no. 14969).","chapter_en":"Chapter on mentioning the qualities of the best women","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn Salam reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of women is the one who pleases you when you see her, obeys you when you command her, and guards your absence regarding herself and your wealth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (338/14 رقم 14969)."},{"num":6227,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: قَالَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: أيهما امْرَأَةٍ تزوجتْ بِغَيْرِ إِذْنِ وَلِيِّهَا فَنِكَاحُهَا بَاطِلٌ، فَإِنْ دَخَلَ بِهَا فَلَهَا الْمَهْرُ بِمَا اسْتَحَلَّ مِنْ فَرْجِهَا، وَإِنْ اشْتَجَرُوا فَالسُّلْطَانُ وَلِيُّ مَنْ لاَ وَلِيَّ لَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2083) والترمذي (1102) وابن ماجة (1879) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4074) والحاكم (2/168) والبيهقي (13655) كلهم من حديث ابن جريج، قال: أخبرني سليمان بن موسى أن ابن شهاب أخبره، أن عروة أخبره أن عائشة أخبرته أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب لا نكاح إلا بولي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2083), al-Tirmidhi (1102), Ibn Majah (1879), and authenticated by Ibn Hibban (4074).","chapter_en":"There is no marriage except with a guardian","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, then her marriage is invalid. If he has consummated the marriage with her, then she is entitled to the dowry because he made her private part lawful for himself. And if they dispute, then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2083)، والترمذي (1102)، وابن ماجه (1879)، وصححه ابن حبان (4074)."},{"num":6228,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى الأشعري قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لاَ نِكَاحَ إِلاَّ بِوَلِيٍّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2085) والترمذي (1101) وابن ماجة (1881) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4077، 4078) والحاكم (3543) والبيهقي (7/107) كلهم من طريق أبي إسحاق الهمداني، عن أبي بردة، عن أبي موسى فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا نكاح إلا بولي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2085), al-Tirmidhi (1101), Ibn Majah (1881), and authenticated by Ibn Hibban (4078, 4077).","chapter_en":"There is no marriage except with a guardian","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Musa al-Ash‘ari said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no marriage except with a guardian.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2085)، والترمذي (1101)، وابن ماجه (1881)، وصححه ابن حبان (4078، 4077)."},{"num":6229,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ حَبِيبَةَ، أَنَّهَا كَانَتْ عِنْدَ ابْنِ جَحْشٍ، فَهَلَكَ عَنْهَا. - وَكَانَ فِيمَنْ هَاجَرَ إِلَى أَرْضِ الْحَبَشَةِ، - فَزَوَّجَهَا النَّجَاشِيُّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهِيَ عِنْدَهُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2086) عن محمد بن يحيى بن فارس، حدثنا عبد الرزاق، عن معمر، عن الزهري، عن عروة بن الزبير، عن أم حبيبة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا نكاح إلا بولي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2086).","chapter_en":"There is no marriage except with a guardian","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Habibah reported that she had been married to Ibn Jahsh, then he died while they were among those who had migrated to Abyssinia. Then the Negus married her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was there with them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2086)."},{"num":6230,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قَالَ: لَا نِكَاحَ إِلَاّ بِوَلِيٍّ، وَشَاهِدَيْ عَدْلٍ، وَمَا كَانَ مِنْ نِكَاحٍ عَلَى غَيْرِ ذَلِكَ، فَهُوَ بَاطِلٌ، فَإِنْ تَشَاجَرُوا فَالسُّلْطَانُ وَلِيُّ مَنْ لَا وَلِيَّ لَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (4075) عن عمر بن محمد الهمداني من أصل كتابه، حدثنا سعيد بن يحيى بن سعيد الأموي، حدثنا حفص بن غياث، عن ابن جريج، عن سليمان بن موسى، عن الزهري، عن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب لا نكاح إلا بشاهدين عدلين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Hibban (4075).","chapter_en":"There is no marriage except with two just witnesses","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses. Any marriage other than that is invalid. If they dispute, then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (4075)."},{"num":6231,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَمُرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: أَيُّمَا امْرَأَةٍ زَوَّجَهَا وَلِيَّانِ فَهِيَ لِلأَوَّلِ مِنْهُمَا، وَأَيُّمَا رَجُلٍ بَاعَ بَيْعًا مِنْ رَجُلَيْنِ فَهُوَ لِلأَوَّلِ مِنْهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2088) والترمذي (1110) وابن ماجة (2190) وأحمد (20085) والحاكم (2/174-175) والبيهقي (7/139-141) كلهم من طرق عن قتادة، عن الحسن، عن سمرة، عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إذا نكح وليّان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2088), al-Tirmidhi (1110), Ibn Majah (2190), and Ahmad (20085).","chapter_en":"If two guardians marry off the same woman","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Samurah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Any woman whom two guardians marry off, then she belongs to the first of them. And any man who sells one sale to two men, it belongs to the first of them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2088)، والترمذي (1110)، وابن ماجه (2190)، وأحمد (20085)."},{"num":6232,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سالم بن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ أَنَّهُ سَمِعَ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا يُحَدِّثُ أَنَّ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ حِينَ تَأَيَّمَتْ حَفْصَةُ بِنْتُ عُمَرَ مِنْ خُنَيْسِ بْنِ حُذَافَةَ السَّهْمِيِّ ـ وَكَانَ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَتُوُفِّيَ بِالْمَدِينَةِ ـ فَقَالَ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ: أَتَيْتُ عُثْمَانَ بْنَ عَفَّانَ فَعَرَضْتُ عَلَيْهِ حَفْصَةَ فَقَالَ: سَأَنْظُرُ فِي أَمْرِي. فَلَبِثْتُ لَيَالِيَ ثُمَّ لَقِيَنِي فَقَالَ: قَدْ بَدَا لِي أَنْ لاَ أَتَزَوَّجَ يَوْمِي هَذَا. قَالَ عُمَرُ: فَلَقِيتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ الصِّدِّيقَ فَقُلْتُ: إِنْ شِئْتَ زَوَّجْتُكَ حَفْصَةَ بِنْتَ عُمَرَ. فَصَمَتَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَلَمْ يَرْجِعْ إِلَىَّ شَيْئًا، وَكُنْتُ أَوْجَدَ عَلَيْهِ مِنِّي عَلَى عُثْمَانَ، فَلَبِثْتُ لَيَالِيَ ثُمَّ خَطَبَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَنْكَحْتُهَا إِيَّاهُ، فَلَقِيَنِي أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَقَالَ: لَعَلَّكَ وَجَدْتَ عَلَىَّ حِينَ عَرَضْتَ عَلَىَّ حَفْصَةَ فَلَمْ أَرْجِعْ إِلَيْكَ شَيْئًا. قَالَ عُمَرُ: قُلْتُ نَعَمْ. قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: فَإِنَّهُ لَمْ يَمْنَعْنِي أَنْ أَرْجِعَ إِلَيْكَ فِيمَا عَرَضْتَ عَلَىَّ إِلاَّ أَنِّي كُنْتُ عَلِمْتُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَدْ ذَكَرَهَا، فَلَمْ أَكُنْ لأُفْشِيَ سِرَّ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَلَوْ تَرَكَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَبِلْتُهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5122) عن عبد العزيز بن عبد الله، حدّثنا إبراهيم بن سعد، عن صالح بن كيسان، عن ابن شهاب قال: أخبرني سالم بن عبد الله، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عرض الإنسان ابنته أو أخته على أهل الصلاح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5122).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a man offering his daughter or sister to righteous people","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salim ibn ‘Abd Allah reported that he heard ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar narrating: When Hafsah bint ‘Umar became widowed after Khunays ibn Hudhafah al-Sahmi - who had been one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and had died in Madinah - ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I went to ‘Uthman ibn ‘Affan and offered Hafsah to him, and he said: “I will consider my matter.” A few nights passed, then he met me and said: “It seems to me that I should not marry at this time.” ‘Umar said: Then I met Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and said: “If you wish, I will marry Hafsah bint ‘Umar to you.” Abu Bakr remained silent and gave me no reply, and I was more upset with him than with ‘Uthman. Then a few nights passed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her, so I married her to him. Then Abu Bakr met me and said: “Perhaps you were upset with me when you offered Hafsah to me and I gave you no response?” ‘Umar said: I said, “Yes.” Abu Bakr said: “Nothing prevented me from replying to you except that I knew the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had mentioned her, and I would never disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Had the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left her, I would have accepted her.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[9412],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5122)."},{"num":6233,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ حَبِيبَةَ بِنْتِ أَبِي سُفْيَانَ، قَالَتْ:  دَخَلَ عَلَيَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: هَلْ لَكَ فِي أُخْتِي بِنْتِ أَبِي سُفْيَانَ؟ فَقَالَ: أَفْعَلُ مَاذَا؟ قُلْتُ: تَنْكِحُهَا. قَالَ: أَوَتُحِبِّينَ ذَلِكِ؟ قُلْتُ: لَسْتُ لَكَ بِمُخْلِيَةٍ وَأَحَبُّ مَنْ شَرِكَنِي فِي الْخَيْرِ أُخْتِي. قَالَ:"],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5101) من طريق الزهري، ومسلم في الرضاع (1449: 15) من طريق هشام ( هو ابن عروة)- كلاهما عن عروة بن الزبير، عن زينب بنت أم سلمة، عن أم حبيبة بنت أبي سفيان، قالت فذكرته، واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب عرض الإنسان ابنته أو أخته على أهل الصلاح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5101) and Muslim (1449:15), and this wording is that of Muslim.","chapter_en":"Chapter on a man offering his daughter or sister to righteous people","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and I said to him, “Would you like my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan?” He said, “What would I do?” I said, “Marry her.” He said, “Would you like that?” I said, “I am not the only one for you, and the one I would most love to share in good with me is my sister…”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Her saying, “I am not the only one for you,” means: I am not alone with you and not free from having a co-wife."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5101)، ومسلم (1449: 15)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":6234,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَهْلٍ، أَنَّ امْرَأَةً، عَرَضَتْ نَفْسَهَا عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَجُلٌ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، زَوِّجْنِيهَا. فَقَالَ: مَا عِنْدَكَ. قَالَ مَا عِنْدِي شَىْءٌ. قَالَ: اذْهَبْ فَالْتَمِسْ وَلَوْ خَاتَمًا مِنْ حَدِيدٍ. فَذَهَبَ ثُمَّ رَجَعَ فَقَالَ: لاَ وَاللَّهِ مَا وَجَدْتُ شَيْئًا، وَلاَ خَاتَمًا مِنْ حَدِيدٍ، وَلَكِنْ هَذَا إِزَارِي وَلَهَا نِصْفُهُ. ـ قَالَ سَهْلٌ: وَمَا لَهُ رِدَاءٌ. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَا تَصْنَعُ بِإِزَارِكَ؟ إِنْ لَبِسْتَهُ لَمْ يَكُنْ عَلَيْهَا مِنْهُ شَىْءٌ، وَإِنْ لَبِسَتْهُ لَمْ يَكُنْ عَلَيْكَ مِنْهُ شَىْءٌ. فَجَلَسَ الرَّجُلُ حَتَّى إِذَا طَالَ مَجْلَسُهُ قَامَ، فَرَآهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَدَعَاهُ أَوْ دُعِي لَهُ فَقَالَ مَاذَا مَعَكَ مِنَ الْقُرْآنِ. فَقَالَ مَعِي سُورَةُ كَذَا وَسُورَةُ كَذَا لِسُوَرٍ يُعَدِّدُهَا. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمْلَكْنَاكَهَا بِمَا مَعَكَ مِنَ الْقُرْآنِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5121)، ومسلم في النكاح (1425) من طريق أبي حازم، عن سهل بن سعد، فذكره. واللفظ للبخاريّ.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب عرض المرأة نفسها على النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5121) and Muslim (1425). The wording here is that of al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman offering herself to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Sa‘d reported that a woman offered herself to the Prophet ﷺ. Then a man said to him: “O Messenger of Allah, marry her to me.” He said, “What do you have?” He said, “I have nothing.” He said, “Go and look, even if only for an iron ring.” So he went and returned and said, “No, by Allah, I found nothing, not even an iron ring. But this is my waist-wrapper, and she may have half of it.” Sahl said: He did not even have an upper garment. So the Prophet ﷺ said, “What would she do with your waist-wrapper? If you wear it, she will have nothing of it, and if she wears it, you will have nothing of it.” The man sat until his sitting became long, then he stood up. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and called him - or he was called for. He said to him, “What do you have from the Qur’an?” He said, “I have such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah,” listing several surahs. Then the Prophet ﷺ said, “We have married her to you in exchange for what you have of the Qur’an.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[13085],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5121)، ومسلم (1425). واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":6235,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أنس بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: جَاءَتِ امْرَأَةٌ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَعْرِضُ عَلَيْهِ نَفْسَهَا قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَلَكَ بِي حَاجَةٌ؟ فَقَالَتْ بِنْتُ أَنَسٍ: مَا أقلّ حَيَاءَهَا وَاسَوْأَتَاهْ. قَالَ: هِيَ خَيْرٌ مِنْكِ. رَغِبَتْ فِي النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَعَرَضَتْ عَلَيْهِ نَفْسَهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5120) عن علي بن عبدالله، حدّثنا مرحوم، قال سمعت ثابتاً البناني قال: كنتُ عند أنسٍ وعنده ابنة له، قال أنس: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب عرض المرأة نفسها على النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5120).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman offering herself to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offering herself to him. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, do you have any need of me?” The daughter of Anas said, “How little modesty she had! What a shame!” He said: She was better than you; she desired the Prophet ﷺ, so she offered herself to him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5120)."},{"num":6236,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: كُنْتُ أَغَارُ عَلَى اللَّاتِي وهَبْن أَنْفُسَهُنَّ لِرَسُولِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَقُولُ: تهب الْمَرْأَةُ نَفْسَهَا؟ فَلَمَّا نَزَلَ قوله تَعَالَى: ﴿تُرْجِي مَنْ تَشَاءُ مِنْهُنَّ وَتُؤْوِي إِلَيْكَ مَنْ تَشَاءُ وَمَنِ ابْتَغَيْتَ مِمَّنْ عَزَلْتَ﴾ [ الأحزاب: ٥١] قَالَتْ: قُلْتُ: وَاللهِ مَا أَرَى رَبَّكَ إِلَّا يُسَارِعُ لَكَ فِي هَوَاكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4788) ومسلم في الرضاع (1463) كلاهما من حديث أبي أسامة، عن هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب عرض المرأة نفسها على النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (4788) and Muslim (1463).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman offering herself to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: I used to feel jealous of those women who offered themselves to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I would say, “Does a woman offer herself?” Then when the saying of Allah Most High was revealed: “You may defer whom you will of them and take to yourself whom you will, and whomever you desire of those you had set aside - there is no blame upon you.” [Al-Ahzab: 51] she said: I said, “By Allah, I see that your Lord hastens to fulfill what pleases you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4788)، ومسلم (1463)."},{"num":6237,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: كَانَتْ خَوْلَةُ بِنْتُ حَكِيمٍ مِنَ اللاَّئِي وَهَبْنَ أَنْفُسَهُنَّ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: أَمَا تَسْتَحِي الْمَرْأَةُ أَنْ تَهَبَ نَفْسَهَا لِلرَّجُلِ؟ فَلَمَّا نَزَلَتْ {تُرْجِئُ مَنْ تَشَاءُ مِنْهُنَّ} قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! مَا أَرَى رَبَّكَ إِلاَّ يُسَارِعُ فِي هَوَاكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5113) عن محمد بن سلام، حدثنا ابن فُضيل، حدثنا هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب عرض المرأة نفسها على النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5113) and Muslim (1464/50).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman offering herself to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUrwah reported: Khawlah bint Ḥakīm was among the women who offered themselves in marriage to the Prophet ﷺ. ʿĀʾishah said: “Does a woman not feel shy to offer herself to a man?” Then when the verse was revealed: “You may defer whom you wish of them…” [al-Aḥzāb: 51] I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I see that your Lord hastens to fulfill what pleases you.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word “turjī” means: you may defer whichever of the women who offered themselves you wish.","“And you may take in” means: you may accept whichever of them you wish and put aside whichever you wish; and even one whom you previously put aside remains subject to your choice afterward—if you wish, you may return to her and accept her.","Her expression “what you desire” means what pleases you. Jealousy caused her to phrase it in that manner; attributing mere personal whim to the Prophet ﷺ is not intended literally, because he does not speak from whim nor act from whim."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13089],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5113)، ومسلم (1464/50)."},{"num":6238,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ بُرَيْدَةَ قَالَ: خَطَبَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ فَاطِمَةَ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّهَا صَغِيرَةٌ فَخَطَبَهَا عليٌّ، فَزَوَّجَهَا مِنْهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3221) عن الحسين بن حريث، قال: ثنا الفضل بن موسى، عن الحسين بن واقد، عن عبد الله بن بريدة، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب تزوج المرأة مثلها في السن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3221).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the recommendation of marrying a woman near one’s age","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah said: Abu Bakr and ‘Umar proposed marriage to Fatimah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “She is young.” Then ‘Ali proposed to her, and he married her to him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9424],"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3221)."},{"num":6239,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: تَزَوَّجَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَنَا بِنْتُ ست سِنِينَ، وَبَنَى بِي وَأَنَا بِنْتُ تِسْعِ سِنِينَ، قَالَتْ: فَقَدِمْنَا الْمَدِينَةَ، فَنَزَلْنَا فِي بَنِي الْحَارِثِ بْنُ خزرج، فَوُعِكْتُ فتمزّق شَعْرِي، فَوَفَى جُمَيْمَةً، فَأَتَتْنِي أُمِّي أُمُّ رُومَانَ، وَأَنَا عَلَى أُرْجُوحَةٍ، وَمَعِي صَوَاحِبِي، فَصَرَخَتْ بِي فَأَتَيْتُهَا، لا أَدْرِي مَا تُرِيدُ بِي، فَأَخَذَتْ بِيَدِي حَتَّى أوقفتني عَلَى الْبَابِ. فَقُلْتُ: هَهْ هَهْ، حَتَّى ذَهَبَ نَفَسي فَأَدْخَلَتْنِي بَيْتًا، فَإِذَا نِسْوَةٌ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ، فَقُلْنَ: عَلَى الْخَيْرِ وَالْبَرَكَةِ، وَعَلَى خَيْرِ طَائِرٍ، فَأَسْلَمَتْنِي إِلَيْهِنَّ، فَغَسَلْنَ رَأْسِي وأصْلَحْنَني، فَلَمْ يَرُعْني إِلَّا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ضحىً. فَأَسْلَمَتْنِي إِلَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المناقب (3894) ومسلم في النكاح (1422) كلاهما عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في نكاح الصغيرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (3894) and Muslim (1422).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the Marriage of a Young Girl","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAʾishah reported: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was six years old and consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old. We then came to Madinah and stayed among Banu al-Harith ibn Khazraj. I fell ill and my hair fell out, then it grew back to around ear-length. My mother, Umm Ruman, came to me while I was on a swing with some girl companions. She called me, so I went to her without knowing what she wanted. She took me by the hand until she made me stand at the door. I said, ‘Hah, hah,’ until my breath settled, then she brought me into a house. There were women from the Ansar inside, and they said: ‘With goodness and blessing, and with good fortune.’ She handed me over to them, and they washed my head and prepared me. Nothing startled me except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming in the forenoon. Then she handed me over to him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Her saying, “Jamima,” is the diminutive of “jamma,” which refers to hair that falls to the ears and the like—meaning it had grown to this length after having","fallen out due to illness."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3894) ومسلم (1422)."},{"num":6240,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ  أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَزَوَّجَهَا وَهِْيَ بِنْتُ سَبْعِ سِنِينَ، وَزُفَّتْ إِلَيْهِ وَهِيَ بِنْتُ تِسْعِ سِنِينَ، وَلُعَبُهَا مَعَهَا، وَمَاتَ عَنْهَا وَهِيَ بِنْتُ ثَمَانَ عَشْرَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في النكاح (1422: 71) عن عبد بن حميد، أخبرنا عبد الرزاق، أخبرنا معمر، عن الزهري، عن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في نكاح الصغيرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (71:1422).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the Marriage of a Young Girl","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported that the Prophet ﷺ married her when she was seven years old, and she was brought to him as a bride when she was nine years old, with her playthings with her, and he died when she was eighteen years old."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1422: 71)."},{"num":6241,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي سَلَمَةَ ويحيى قالا: لَمَّا هلكت خديجة، جاءت خولة بنت حكيم امرأة عُثْمَانَ بن مَظْعُونٍ قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَلَا تَزَوَّجُ؟ قَالَ: مَنْ؟ قَالَتْ: إِنْ شِئْتَ بِكْرًا، وَإِنْ شِئْتَ ثَيِّبًا؟ قَالَ: فَمَنِ الْبِكْرُ؟ قَالَتْ: ابْنَةُ أَحَبِّ خَلْقِ اللهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ إِلَيْكَ: عَائِشَةُ بِنْتُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، قَالَ: وَمَنِ الثَّيِّبُ؟ قَالَتْ: سَوْدَةُ بِنْتُ زَمْعَةَ، آَمَنَتْ بِكَ، وَاتَّبَعَتْكَ عَلَى مَا تَقُولُ، ، قَالَ: فَاذْهَبِي فَاذْكُرِيهِمَا عَلَيَّ ، فَدَخَلَتْ بَيْتَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، فَقَالَتْ: يَا أُمَّ رُومَانَ، مَاذَا أَدْخَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنَ الْخَيْرِ وَالْبَرَكَةِ؟ قَالَتْ: وَمَا ذَاكَ؟ قَالَتْ: أَرْسَلَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَخْطُبُ عَلَيْهِ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: انْتَظِرِي أَبَا بَكْرٍ حَتَّى يَأْتِيَ، فَجَاءَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَقَالَتْ: يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ، مَاذَا أَدْخَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنَ الْخَيْرِ وَالْبَرَكَةِ؟ قَالَ: وَمَا ذَاكَ؟ قَالَتْ: أَرْسَلَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَخْطُبُ عَلَيْهِ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَ: وَهَلْ تَصْلُحُ لَهُ؟ إِنَّمَا هِيَ ابْنَةُ أَخِيهِ، فَرَجَعَتْ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَذَكَرَتْ ذَلِكَ لَهُ، قَالَ: ارْجِعِي إِلَيْهِ فَقُولِي لَهُ: أَنَا أَخُوكَ، وَأَنْتَ أَخِي فِي الْإِسْلَامِ، وَابْنَتُكَ تَصْلُحُ لِي، فَرَجَعَتْ، فَذَكَرَتْ ذَلِكَ لَهُ، قَالَ: انْتَظِرِي، وَخَرَجَ، قَالَتْ أُمُّ رُومَانَ: إِنَّ مُطْعِمَ بْنَ عَدِيٍّ قَدْ كَانَ ذَكَرَهَا عَلَى ابْنِهِ، فَوَاللهِ مَا وَعَدَ وَعْدًا قَطُّ، فَأَخْلَفَهُ لِأَبِي بَكْرٍ، فَدَخَلَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ عَلَى مُطْعِمِ بْنِ عَدِيٍّ، وَعِنْدَهُ امْرَأَتُهُ أُمُّ الْفَتَى، فَقَالَتْ: يَا ابْنَ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ، لَعَلَّكَ مُصْبِئُ صَاحِبَنَا، مُدْخِلُهُ فِي دِينِكَ الَّذِي أَنْتَ عَلَيْهِ، إِنْ تَزَوَّجَ إِلَيْكَ، قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ لِلْمُطْعِمِ بْنِ عَدِيٍّ: أَقَوْلُ هَذِهِ تَقُولُ، قَالَ: إِنَّهَا تَقُولُ ذَلِكَ، فَخَرَجَ مِنْ عِنْدِهِ، وَقَدْ أَذْهَبَ اللهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ مَا كَانَ فِي نَفْسِهِ مِنْ عِدَتِهِ الَّتِي وَعَدَهُ، فَرَجَعَ، فَقَالَ لِخَوْلَةَ: ادْعِي لِي رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَدَعَتْهُ، فَزَوَّجَهَا إِيَّاهُ، وَعَائِشَةُ يَوْمَئِذٍ بِنْتُ سِتِّ سِنِينَ، ثُمَّ خَرَجَتْ فَدَخَلَتْ عَلَى سَوْدَةَ بِنْتِ زَمْعَةَ، فَقَالَتْ: مَاذَا أَدْخَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ عَلَيْكِ مِنَ الْخَيْرِ وَالْبَرَكَةِ؟ قَالَتْ: مَا ذَاكَ؟ قَالَتْ: أَرْسَلَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَخْطُبُكِ عَلَيْهِ، قَالَتْ: وَدِدْتُ ادْخُلِي إِلَى أَبِي فَاذْكُرِي ذَاكَ لَهُ، وَكَانَ شَيْخًا كَبِيرًا، قَدْ أَدْرَكَتْهُ السِّنُّ، قَدْ تَخَلَّفَ عَنِ الْحَجِّ، فَدَخَلَتْ عَلَيْهِ، فَحَيَّتْهُ بِتَحِيَّةِ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَذِهِ؟ فَقَالَتْ: خَوْلَةُ بِنْتُ حَكِيمٍ، قَالَ: فَمَا شَأْنُكِ؟ قَالَتْ: أَرْسَلَنِي مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ أَخْطُبُ عَلَيْهِ سَوْدَةَ، قَالَ: كُفْءٌ كَرِيمٌ، مَاذَا تَقُولُ صَاحِبَتُكِ؟ قَالَتْ: تُحِبُّ ذَاكَ، قَالَ: ادْعُهَا لِي فَدَعَتْهَا، فَقَالَ: أَيْ بُنَيَّةُ إِنَّ هَذِهِ تَزْعُمْ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ قَدْ أَرْسَلَ يَخْطُبُكِ، وَهُوَ كُفْءٌ كَرِيمٌ، أَتُحِبِّينَ أَنْ أُزَوِّجَكِ بِهِ، قَالَتْ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: ادْعِيهِ لِي، فَجَاءَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَيْهِ فَزَوَّجَهَا إِيَّاهُ، فَجَاءَهَا أَخُوهَا عَبْدُ بْنُ زَمْعَةَ مِنَ الْحَجِّ، فَجَعَلَ يَحْثِي عَلَى رَأْسِهِ التُّرَابَ، فَقَالَ بَعْدَ أَنْ أَسْلَمَ: لَعَمْرُكَ إِنِّي لَسَفِيهٌ يَوْمَ أَحْثِي فِي رَأْسِي التُّرَابَ أَنْ تَزَوَّجَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سَوْدَةَ بِنْتَ زَمْعَةَ.","قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: فَقَدِمْنَا الْمَدِينَةَ، فَنَزَلْنَا فِي بَنِي الْحَارِثِ مِنَ الْخَزْرَجِ فِي السُّنْحِ، قَالَتْ: فَجَاءَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَدَخَلَ بَيْتَنَا، وَاجْتَمَعَ إِلَيْهِ رِجَالٌ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ وَنِسَاءٌ، فَجَاءَتْ بِي أُمِّي، وَإِنِّي لَفِي أرجوجة بَيْنَ عَذْقَيْنِ تَرْجَحُ بِي، فَأَنْزَلَتْنِي مِنَ الْأُرْجُوحَةِ، وَلِي جُمَيْمَةٌ، فَفَرَقَتْهَا، وَمَسَحَتْ وَجْهِي بِشَيْءٍ مِنْ مَاءٍ، ثُمَّ أَقْبَلَتْ تَقُودُنِي حَتَّى وَقَفَتْ بِي عِنْدَ الْبَابِ، وَإِنِّي لَأَنْهَجُ، حَتَّى سَكَنَ مِنْ نَفْسِي، ثُمَّ دَخَلَتْ بِي، فَإِذَا رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم جَالِسٌ عَلَى سَرِيرٍ فِي بَيْتِنَا، وَعِنْدَهُ رِجَالٌ وَنِسَاءٌ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ، فَأَجْلَسَتْنِي فِي حِجْرِهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَتْ: هَؤُلَاءِ أَهْلُكِ، فَبَارَكَ اللهُ لَكِ فِيهِمْ، وَبَارَكَ لَهُمْ فِيكِ، فَوَثَبَ الرِّجَالُ وَالنِّسَاءُ، فَخَرَجُوا وَبَنَى بِي رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم فِي بَيْتِنَا، مَا نُحِرَتْ عَلَيَّ جَزُورٌ، وَلَا ذُبِحَتْ عَلَيَّ شَاةٌ حَتَّى أَرْسَلَ إِلَيْنَا سَعْدُ بْنُ عُبَادَةَ بِجَفْنَةٍ كَانَ يُرْسِلُ بِهَا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم إِذَا دَارَ إِلَى نِسَائِهِ، وَأَنَا يَوْمَئِذٍ بِنْتُ تِسْعِ سِنِينَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (25769) عن محمد بن بشر، قال: حدثنا محمد بن عمرو، قال: حدثنا أبو سلمة ويحيى قالا: فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في نكاح الصغيرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (25769).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the Marriage of a Young Girl","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Salamah and Yahya said: When Khadijah died, Khawlah bint Hakim, the wife of ‘Uthman ibn Maz‘un, came and said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry? He said, “Whom?” She said: If you wish, a virgin; and if you wish, a previously married woman. He said, “Who is the virgin?” She said: The daughter of the most beloved of Allah’s creation to you: ‘A’ishah daughter of Abu Bakr. He said, “And who is the previously married woman?” She said: Sawdah bint Zam‘ah. She believed in you and followed what you brought. He said, “Go and mention them to me.” So she entered the house of Abu Bakr and said: O Umm Ruman, what goodness and blessing Allah has brought to your household. She said: And what is that? She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to ask for ‘A’ishah in marriage for him. She said: Wait until Abu Bakr comes. When Abu Bakr came, she said: O Abu Bakr, what goodness and blessing Allah has brought to your household. He said: And what is that? She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to ask for ‘A’ishah in marriage for him. He said: Is she suitable for him? She is the daughter of his brother. So she returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: “Go back to him and say: I am your brother and you are my brother in Islam, and your daughter is lawful for me.” So she went back and mentioned that to him. He said: Wait. Then he went out. Umm Ruman said: Mut‘im ibn ‘Adi had already mentioned her for his son, and by Allah he had never made a promise to Abu Bakr and broken it. So Abu Bakr went to Mut‘im ibn ‘Adi, and with him was the boy’s mother. She said: O son of Abu Quhafah, perhaps you will turn our companion away from his religion and enter him into your religion if he marries into you. Abu Bakr said to Mut‘im ibn ‘Adi: Is this what she is saying? He said: She is saying that. So he left him, and Allah removed from his heart the matter of the promise he had made to him. Then he returned and said to Khawlah: Call the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me. So she called him, and he married her to him, and ‘A’ishah was then six years old. Then she went out and entered upon Sawdah bint Zam‘ah and said: What goodness and blessing Allah has brought to you. She said: And what is that? She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to ask for you in marriage for him. She said: I would like that. Go in to my father and mention it to him. He was a very old man who had advanced in age and had stayed behind from Hajj. She entered upon him and greeted him with the greeting of the pre-Islamic period. He said: Who is this? She said: Khawlah bint Hakim. He said: What is your matter? She said: Muhammad ibn ‘Abdullah has sent me; he is asking for Sawdah in marriage. He said: A noble and suitable match. What does your companion say? She said: She would like that. He said: Call her for me. So she called her. He said: My daughter, this woman claims that Muhammad ibn ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Abd al-Muttalib has sent to ask for your hand, and he is a noble and suitable match. Do you wish that I marry you to him? She said: Yes. He said: Call him for me. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him and he married her to him. Then her brother ‘Abd ibn Zam‘ah came back from Hajj and began throwing dust upon his own head. After he accepted Islam, he said: By your life, I was indeed foolish on the day I threw dust on my head because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Sawdah bint Zam‘ah. ‘A’ishah said: Then we came to Madinah and stayed among Banu al-Harith of al-Khazraj at al-Sunh. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and entered our house, and men and women from the Ansar gathered there. My mother came to me while I was on a swing between two branches, swinging on it. She brought me down from the swing, and my hair had grown to around ear-length. She combed and arranged it and wiped my face with some water. Then she came leading me until she made me stand at the door while I was breathing heavily, until I calmed down. Then she took me in, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated on a bed in our house, with men and women from the Ansar around him. She seated me in his lap, then said: These are your family. May Allah bless you in them, and bless them through you. Then the men and women stood up and left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage with me in our house. No camel was slaughtered for me and no sheep was slaughtered for me, until Sa‘d ibn ‘Ubadah sent us a large bowl which he used to send to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whenever he was with one of his wives. I was nine years old at that time."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (25769)."},{"num":6242,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى الأشعري قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ثَلاَثَةٌ لَهُمْ أَجْرَانِ، رَجُلٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ آمَنَ بِنَبِيِّهِ، وَآمَنَ بِمُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَالْعَبْدُ الْمَمْلُوكُ إِذَا أدّى حَقَّ اللَّهِ وَحَقَّ مَوَالِيهِ، وَرَجُلٌ كَانَتْ عِنْدَهُ أَمَةٌ، فَأَدَّبَهَا فَأَحْسَنَ تَأْدِيبَهَا، وَعَلَّمَهَا فَأَحْسَنَ تَعْلِيمَهَا، ثُمَّ أَعْتَقَهَا فَتَزَوَّجَهَا فَلَهُ أَجْرَانِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في العلم (97) ومسلم في الإيمان (154) كلاهما من حديث صالح بن حيان، قال عامر الشعبي: حدثني أبو بردة، عن أبيه (أبي موسى) فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أجر من أعتق أمته ثم تزوجها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (97) and Muslim (154).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the reward of the one who frees his female slave and then marries her","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Musa al-Ash‘ari said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three people will have a double reward: a man from the People of the Book who believed in his prophet and then believed in Muhammad ﷺ; a slave who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters; and a man who has a slave woman, teaches her manners and does so well, and teaches her knowledge and does so well, then frees her and marries her. For him are two rewards.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12966],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (97) ومسلم (154)."},{"num":6243,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر قال: قال لي رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: تزوجت يا جابر فقلت نعم، وفي آخره فقال: بارك الله لك أو قال: خيراً."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النفقات (5367)، ومسلم في الرضاع (715: 56) كلاهما من طريق حماد بن زيد، عن عمرو بن دينار، عن جابر فذكره في سياق طويل.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صيغ تهنئة النكاح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5367) and Muslim (56:715).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the reported forms of congratulating someone on marriage","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Have you married, O Jabir?” I said: Yes. And at the end of the narration he said: “May Allah bless you,” or he said: “Good.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5367)، ومسلم (715: 56)."},{"num":6244,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: رَأَى النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ عَوْفٍ أَثَرَ صُفْرَةٍ فَقَالَ: مَهْيَمْ. أَوْ مَهْ. قَالَ: تَزَوَّجْتُ امْرَأَةً عَلَى وَزْنِ نَوَاةٍ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ. فَقَالَ: بَارَكَ اللَّهُ لَكَ، أَوْلِمْ وَلَوْ بِشَاةٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الدعوات (6386) ومسلم في النكاح (1427: 79) كلاهما من حديث حماد بن زيد، عن ثابت عن أنس فذكره واللفظ للبخاري، ولفظ مسلم مثله غير أنه لم يذكر مَهْيم أو مه","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صيغ تهنئة النكاح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (6386) and Muslim (79:1427). The wording is that of al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"Chapter on the reported forms of congratulating someone on marriage","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik said: The Prophet ﷺ saw on ‘Abd al-Rahman a trace of yellow perfume and said: “What is this?” or: “What happened?” He said: I married a woman for the weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: “May Allah bless you. Give a wedding feast, even if only with one sheep.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[11155],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6386)، ومسلم (1427: 79). واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":6245,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: تَزَوَّجَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَدْخَلَتْنِي أُمِّي بَيْتًا فَإِذَا نِسْوَةٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ قُلْنَ: عَلَى الْخَيْرِ وَالْبَرَكَةِ، وَعَلَى خَيْرِ طَائِرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المناقب (3894) ومسلم في النكاح (1422) كلاهما عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صيغ تهنئة النكاح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (3894) and Muslim (1422).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the reported forms of congratulating someone on marriage","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me, and my mother brought me into a house where there were women from the Ansar. They said: “With goodness and blessing, and with the best fortune.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Her statement, “with the best fortune,” means: with the best share and good lot."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11160],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3894)، ومسلم (1422). وقولها: (( على خير طائر )) أي على أفضل حظ ونصيب."},{"num":6246,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ إِذَا رَفَّأَ الإِنْسَانَ إِذَا تَزَوَّجَ قَالَ بَارَكَ اللَّهُ لَكَ، وَبَارَكَ عَلَيْكَ، وَجَمَعَ بَيْنَكُمَا فِي خَيْرٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2130) والترمذي (1091) وابن ماجة (1905) وأحمد (8956) والدارمي (2220) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4052) والحاكم (2745) كلهم من حديث عبد العزيز بن محمد الدراوردي ، عن سهيل بن أبي صالح، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صيغ تهنئة النكاح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2130), al-Tirmidhi (1091), and Ahmad (8956). Al-Tirmidhi said: Hasan Sahih.","chapter_en":"Chapter on the reported forms of congratulating someone on marriage","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: When the Prophet ﷺ congratulated a person upon marriage, he would say: “May Allah bless you, and send blessing upon you, and join you both together in goodness.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The phrase meaning “congratulated” refers to the old customary formula used in the pre-Islamic period. It was later discouraged, as in the next narration, because it singled out sons and excluded daughters in line with pre-Islamic dislike of girls."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11157],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2130)، والترمذي (1091)، وأحمد (8956). قال الترمذي: حسن صحيح."},{"num":6247,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْحَسَنِ، قَالَ: تَزَوَّجَ عَقِيلُ بْنُ أَبِي طَالِبٍ امْرَأَةً مِنْ بَنِي جُشَمٍ، فَقِيلَ لَهُ: بِالرِّفَاءِ وَالْبَنِينِ. قَالَ: قُولُوا كَمَا قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بَارَكَ اللَّهُ فِيكُمْ، وَبَارَكَ لَكُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3371) واللفظ له، وابن ماجة (1906) وأحمد (1739) والبيهقي (7/148) والدارمي (2119) كلهم من طرق عن الحسن قال فذكره. ولفظ البيهقي: قدم عقيل بن أبي طالب البصرة","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صيغ تهنئة النكاح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3371), and this is his wording, also Ibn Majah (1906), Ahmad (1739), and al-Bayhaqi (7/148).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the reported forms of congratulating someone on marriage","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Hasan said: ‘Aqil ibn Abi Talib married a woman from Banu Jusham, and people said to him: “May you have harmony and sons.” He said: Say instead what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah bless you, and bless for you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11158],"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3371) واللفظ له، وابن ماجه (1906)، وأحمد (1739)، والبيهقي (7/148)."},{"num":6248,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ بُرَيْدَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ نَفَرٌ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ لِعَلِيٍّ: عِنْدَكَ فَاطِمَةُ. فَأَتَى رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَسَلَّمَ عَلَيْهِ فَقَالَ: مَا حَاجَةُ ابْنِ أَبِي طَالِبٍ؟ قَالَ: ذَكَرْتُ فَاطِمَةَ بِنْتَ مُحَمَّدٍ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَرْحَبًا وَأَهْلًا. لَمْ يَزِدْهُ عَلَيْهِمَا. فَخَرَجَ عَلِيُّ عَلَى أُولَئِكَ الرَّهْطِ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ يَنْتَظِرُونَهُ. قَالُوا: مَا وَرَاءَكَ؟ قَالَ: مَا أَدْرِي غَيْرَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ لِي: مَرْحَبًا وَأَهْلًا. قَالُوا: يَكْفِيكَ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِحْدَاهُمَا. أَعْطَاكَ الْأَهْلَ أَعْطَاكَ المرحب، فَلَمَّا كَانَ بَعْدَمَا زَوَّجَهُ قَالَ: يَا عَلِيُّ إِنَّهُ لَا بُدَّ لِلْعَرُوسِ مِنْ وَلِيمَةٍ فَقَالَ سَعْدٌ: عِنْدِي كَبْشٌ، وَجَمَعَ لَهُ رهط مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ آصعاً مِنْ ذُرَةٍ. فَلَمَّا كَانَ لَيْلَةُ الْبِنَاءِ قَالَ: لَا تُحْدِثْ شَيْئًا حَتَّى تَلْقَانِي. قَالَ: فَدَعَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِإِنَاءٍ فَتَوَضَّأَ مِنْهُ، ثُمَّ أَفْرَغَهُ على علي، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ بَارِكْ فِيهِمَا، وَبَارِكْ عَلَيْهِمَا وَبَارِكْ لَهُمَا فِي نسلهما."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن سعد (6895) والطبراني في الكبير (1153) والطحاوي في مشكله (5947) والنسائي في اليوم والليلة (258) وأحمد (23035) مختصرا كلهم من حديث عبد الكريم بن سليط عن ابن بريدة، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صيغ تهنئة النكاح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Sa‘d (8/21), al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (2/4), and al-Tahawi in Mushkil al-Athar (5947).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the reported forms of congratulating someone on marriage","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah said: Some men from the Ansar said to ‘Ali: You have a chance with Fatimah. So he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him, and he said: “What does the son of Abu Talib seek?” He said: I mentioned Fatimah, the daughter of Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Welcome and greetings,” and said nothing more. Then ‘Ali came out to those men from the Ansar who were waiting for him. They said: What happened? He said: I do not know except that he said to me: “Welcome and greetings.” They said: One of those two from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is enough for you. He gave you family ties and welcome. Then after he married him to her, he said: “O ‘Ali, a bridegroom must have a wedding feast.” Sa‘d said: I have a sheep. And some men from the Ansar gathered several measures of grain for him. When it was the night of the marriage, he said: “Do not do anything until you meet me.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel and performed ablution from it, then poured it over ‘Ali and said: “O Allah, bless them both, send blessing upon them, and bless them in their offspring.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن سعد (6895)، والطبراني في الكبير (1153)، والطحاوي في مشكل الآثار (5947)."},{"num":6249,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ:  تَزَوَّجَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي شَوَّالٍ، وَبَنَى بِي فِي شَوَّالٍ، فَأَيُّ نِسَاءِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ أَحْظَى عِنْدَهُ مِنِّي؟","قَالَ: وَكَانَتْ عَائِشَةُ تَسْتَحِبُّ أَنْ تُدْخِلَ نِسَاءَهَا فِي شَوَّالٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في النكاح (1423) من طريق وكيع، حدثنا سفيان، عن إسماعيل بن أمية، عن عبد الله بن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب التزوج في شوال والدخول فيه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1423).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the recommendation of marrying and consummating the marriage in Shawwal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me in Shawwal and consummated the marriage with me in Shawwal. So which of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more favored by him than me? She said: And ‘A’ishah used to like that the women under her care be brought to their husbands in Shawwal."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1423)."},{"num":6250,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ خَنْسَاءَ بِنْتِ خِذَامٍ الأَنْصَارِيَّةِ، أَنَّ أَبَاهَا، زَوَّجَهَا وَهْىَ ثَيِّبٌ، فَكَرِهَتْ ذَلِكَ. فَأَتَتْ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَرَدَّ نِكَاحَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في النكاح (25) عن عبد الرحمن بن القاسم، عن أبيه، عن عبد الرحمن ومُجمّع ابني يزيد بن جارية الأنصاري، عن خنساء بنت خِدام الأنصارية، فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ردّ زواج الثيب الكارهة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Malik (25) and al-Bukhari (5138).","chapter_en":"Chapter on annulling the marriage of a previously married woman who dislikes it","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khansa’ bint Khidam al-Ansariyyah said that her father married her off while she had previously been married, and she disliked that. So she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he annulled that marriage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (25)، والبخاري (5138)."},{"num":6251,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["أَنَّ امْرَأَةً، مِنْ وَلَدِ جَعْفَرٍ، تَخَوَّفَتْ أَنْ يُزَوِّجَهَا وَلِيُّهَا وَهْىَ كَارِهَةٌ، فَأَرْسَلَتْ إِلَى شَيْخَيْنِ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ: عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ وَمُجَمِّعٍ ابْنَىْ جَارِيَةَ، قَالاَ: فَلاَ تَخْشَيْنَ، فَإِنَّ خَنْسَاءَ بِنْتَ خِذَامٍ أَنْكَحَهَا أَبُوهَا وَهْىَ كَارِهَةٌ، فَرَدَّ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَلِكَ.","قَالَ سُفْيَانُ: وَأَمَّا عبدالرحمن فَسَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ عَنْ أَبِيهِ: إِنَّ خَنْسَاءَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الحيل (6969) عن علي بن عبد الله، حـدثنا","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تخيير البكر البالغ زوجها أبوها وهي كارهة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (6969).","chapter_en":"Chapter on giving an adult virgin the choice if her father marries her off while she dislikes it","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["A woman from the descendants of Ja‘far feared that her guardian would marry her off while she disliked it, so she sent to two elderly men from the Ansar: ‘Abd al-Rahman and Mujamma‘, the two sons of Jariyah. They said: Do not be afraid, for Khansa’ bint Khidam was married off by her father while she disliked it, and the Prophet ﷺ nullified that.","Sufyan said: As for ‘Abd al-Rahman, I heard him say from his father: “Indeed Khansa’…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (6969)."},{"num":6252,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، أَنَّ جَارِيَةً، بِكْرًا أَتَتِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَذَكَرَتْ أَنَّ أَبَاهَا زَوَّجَهَا وَهِيَ كَارِهَةٌ. فَخَيَّرَهَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2096) وابن ماجة (1875) وأحمد (2469) والدارقطني (3566) والبيهقي (13669) كلهم من طريق الحسين بن محمد المروزي، حدثني جرير بن حازم، عن أيوب، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تخيير البكر البالغ زوجها أبوها وهي كارهة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2096), Ibn Majah (1875), Ahmad (2469), and al-Daraqutni (3/234–235).","chapter_en":"Chapter on giving an adult virgin the choice if her father marries her off while she dislikes it","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas narrated that a virgin young woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him that her father had married her off while she disliked it, so the Prophet ﷺ gave her the choice."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2096)، وابن ماجه (1875)، وأحمد (2469)، والدارقطني (3566)."},{"num":6253,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لاَ تُنْكَحُ الأَيِّمُ حَتَّى تُسْتَأْمَرَ، وَلاَ تُنْكَحُ الْبِكْرُ حَتَّى تُسْتَأْذَنَ. قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَكَيْفَ إِذْنُهَا؟ قَالَ: أَنْ تَسْكُتَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5136)، ومسلم في النكاح (1419) كلاهما من طريق هشام، عن يحيى بن أبي كثير، حدّثنا أبو سلمة، حدّثنا أبو هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الأيم أحق بنفسها، والبكر تستأذن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5136) and Muslim (1419).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the previously married woman having more right over herself, and the virgin being asked for permission","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A previously married woman must not be married until she is consulted, and a virgin must not be married until her permission is sought.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, how is her permission given? He said: “By her silence.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Women are of two types: previously married and virgin. Mentioning “the previously married woman” in contrast to the virgin shows that what is meant here by al-ayyim is the previously married woman. The silence of the virgin when asked for permission is taken as a sign of her approval, because she may feel shy about stating it openly and expressing interest in marriage. As for the previously married woman, she may openly express whether she wants marriage or not, since the shyness of a virgin is no longer present, so she speaks and instructs her guardian to marry her as she wishes."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5136)، ومسلم (1419)."},{"num":6254,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَتْ: أَرْسَلَ إِلَيَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَاطِبَ بْنَ أَبِي بَلْتَعَةَ يَخْطُبُنِي لَهُ، فَقُلْتُ: إِنَّ لِي بِنْتًا وَأَنَا غَيُورٌ، فَقَالَ: أَمَّا ابْنَتُهَا فَنَدْعُو اللهَ أَنْ يُغْنِيَهَا عَنْهَا، وَأَدْعُو اللهَ أَنْ يَذْهَبَ بِالْغَيْرَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجنائز (3:918) من طريق إسماعيل بن جعفر، أخبرني سعد بن سعيد، عن عمر بن كثير بن أفلح، عن ابن سفينة، عن أم سلمة، فذكرته بطوله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الأيم أحق بنفسها، والبكر تستأذن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (3:918).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the previously married woman having more right over herself, and the virgin being asked for permission","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Hatib ibn Abi Balta‘ah to propose to me on his behalf. I said: I have a daughter, and I am a jealous woman. He said: “As for her daughter, we ask Allah to make her independent of her mother, and I ask Allah to remove jealousy.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (3:918)."},{"num":6255,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: سَأَلْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَنِ الْجَارِيَةِ يُنْكِحُهَا أَهْلُهَا، أَتُسْتَأْمَرُ أَمْ لَا؟ فَقَالَ لَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : نَعَمْ تُسْتَأْمَرُ فَقَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: فَإِنَّهَا تستحي. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَذَلِكَ إِذْنُهَا إِذَا هِيَ سكتَتْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5137) من طريق الليث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الأيم أحق بنفسها، والبكر تستأذن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5137) and Muslim (1420). The wording is that of Muslim.","chapter_en":"Chapter on the previously married woman having more right over herself, and the virgin being asked for permission","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a young woman whose family wants to marry her off: should her permission be sought or not? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “Yes, her permission should be sought.” ‘A’ishah said: I said to him: But she feels shy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “That is her permission when she remains silent.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The wording in al-Bukhari is: She said, O Messenger of Allah, the virgin feels shy. He said: “Her consent is her silence.”","In other narrations: “Seek the women’s permission concerning their marriage.” Narrated by Ibn Hibban in his Sahih (4080)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5137)، ومسلم (1420). واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":6256,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ عَبَّاسٍ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: الأَيِّمُ أَحَقُّ بِنَفْسِهَا مِنْ وَلِيِّهَا، وَالْبِكْرُ تُسْتَأْذَنُ فِي نَفْسِهَا، وَإِذْنُهَا صُمَاتُهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في النكاح (4) عن عبد الله بن الفضل، عن نافع بن جبير بن مطعم، عن عبد الله بن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الأيم أحق بنفسها، والبكر تستأذن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Malik (4) and Muslim (66:1421).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the previously married woman having more right over herself, and the virgin being asked for permission","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The previously married woman has more right over herself than her guardian, and the virgin is asked for permission regarding herself, and her permission is her silence.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (4)، ومسلم (66:1421)."},{"num":6257,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ العُرس بن عَمِيرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: آمِرُوا النِّسَاءَ لتعرب الثَّيِّبُ عَنْ نَفْسِهَا، وَإِذْنُ الْبِكْرِ صماتها."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (17/ح 342) من طريق سفيان بن عامر، والطحاوي في شرح المعاني (4/368) من طريق يحيى بن أيوب كلاهما عن عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن، عن عدي بن عدي، عن أبيه، عن العرس بن عميرة فذكره واللفظ للطبراني.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الأيم أحق بنفسها، والبكر تستأذن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (17/138), and al-Tahawi in Sharh al-Ma‘ani (4/368). The wording is that of al-Tabarani.","chapter_en":"Chapter on the previously married woman having more right over herself, and the virgin being asked for permission","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-‘Urs ibn ‘Umayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Consult the women, so that the previously married woman may express her own view, and the permission of the virgin is her silence.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The wording of al-Tahawi is: “The previously married woman expresses her own view, and the approval of the virgin is her silence.”","Legal understanding of this chapter: The narrations in this chapter show that marrying off a previously married woman is not permissible except with her permission.","His statement ﷺ, “The previously married woman has more right over herself,” means that she has more right than her guardian in choosing whichever husband she wishes. So she may say, for example: I approve of so-and-so, and I do not approve of so-and-so. The guardian must marry her according to her choice, but she does not personally conduct her own marriage contract.","As for using these narrations as proof that a marriage is valid without a guardian, that is not correct."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (17/ح 342)، والطحاوي في شرح المعاني (4/368) واللفظ للطبراني."},{"num":6258,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ، قَالَ: تُوُفِّيَ عُثْمَانُ بْنُ مَظْعُونٍ، وَتَرَكَ ابْنَةً لَهُ مِنْ خُوَيْلَةَ بِنْتِ حَكِيمِ بْنِ أُمَيَّةَ بْنِ حَارِثَةَ بْنِ الْأَوْقَصِ، قَالَ: وَأَوْصَى إِلَى أَخِيهِ قُدَامَةَ بْنِ مَظْعُونٍ، قَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ: وَهُمَا خَالَايَ، قَالَ: فَخَطَبْتُ إِلَى قُدَامَةَ بْنِ مَظْعُونٍ ابْنَةَ عُثْمَانَ بْنِ مَظْعُونٍ، فَزَوَّجَنِيهَا، وَدَخَلَ الْمُغِيرَةُ بْنُ شُعْبَةَ - يَعْنِي إِلَى أُمِّهَا - فَأَرْغَبَهَا فِي الْمَالِ، فَحَطَّتْ إِلَيْهِ، وَحَطَّتْ الْجَارِيَةُ إِلَى هَوَى أُمِّهَا، فَأَبَيَا، حَتَّى ارْتَفَعَ أَمْرُهُمَا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ قُدَامَةُ بْنُ مَظْعُونٍ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، ابْنَةُ أَخِي، أَوْصَى بِهَا إِلَيَّ، فَزَوَّجْتُهَا ابْنَ عَمَّتِهَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ، فَلَمْ أُقَصِّرْ بِهَا فِي الصَّلَاحِ، وَلَا فِي الْكَفَاءَةِ، وَلَكِنَّهَا امْرَأَةٌ، وَإِنَّمَا حَطَّتْ إِلَى هَوَى أُمِّهَا، قَالَ: فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هِيَ يَتِيمَةٌ، وَلَا تُنْكَحُ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِهَا قَالَ: فَانْتُزِعَتْ وَاللهِ مِنِّي بَعْدَ أَنْ مَلَكْتُهَا، فَزَوَّجُوهَا الْمُغِيرَةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (6136) عن يعقوب، حدثنا أبي، عن ابن إسحاق، حدثني عمر بن حسين بن عبد الله مولى آل حاطب، عن نافع مولى عبد الله بن عمر، عن عبد الله بن عمر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن اليتيمة لا تنكح إلا بإذنها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (6136).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the orphan girl not being married except with her permission","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar said: ‘Uthman ibn Maz‘un died and left behind a daughter from Khawlah bint Hakim ibn Umayyah ibn Harithah ibn al-Awqas. He said: And he entrusted her to his brother Qudamah ibn Maz‘un. ‘Abdullah said: They are both my maternal uncles. He said: So I proposed to Qudamah ibn Maz‘un for the daughter of ‘Uthman ibn Maz‘un, and he married her to me. Then al-Mughirah ibn Shu‘bah approached her mother and encouraged her with wealth, so the mother inclined toward him, and the girl followed the desire of her mother, and they both refused, until their matter was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Qudamah ibn Maz‘un said: O Messenger of Allah, she is my brother’s daughter, and he entrusted her to me. I married her to her cousin ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar, and I was not lacking regarding her in righteousness or suitability, but she is a woman, and she merely followed the preference of her mother. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “She is an orphan girl, and she is not to be married except with her permission.” He said: By Allah, she was taken away from me after I had been given her in marriage, and they married her to al-Mughirah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (6136)."},{"num":6259,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: تُسْتَأْمَرُ الْيَتِيمَةُ فِي نَفْسِهَا، فَإِنْ سَكَتَتْ فَقَدْ أَذِنَتْ، وَإِنْ أَبَتْ لَمْ تُكْرَهْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (9516) والبزار – كشف الأستار (1423) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4085) والحاكم (2702) وعنه البيهقي (13691) كلهم من حديث يونس بن أبي إسحاق، عن أبي بردة، عن أبيه أبي موسى فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن اليتيمة لا تنكح إلا بإذنها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (19516), al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1423), authenticated by Ibn Hibban (4085), and al-Hakim (2702).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the orphan girl not being married except with her permission","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Musa said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The orphan girl is asked for her permission regarding herself. If she remains silent, then she has given permission, and if she refuses, she is not to be forced.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (9516)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (1423)، وصححه ابن حبان (4085)، والحاكم (2702)."},{"num":6260,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : واليتيمة تُسْتَأْمَرُ فِي نَفْسِهَا، فَإِنْ صَمَتَتْ فَهُوَ إِذْنُهَا، وأن أبتْ فَلاَ جَوَازَ عَلَيْهَا يَعْنِي إِذَا أَدْرَكَتْ فردّتْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2093) والترمذي (1109) والنسائي (237) وأحمد (7572) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4086،4079) كلهم رووه عن جماعة عن محمد بن عمرو، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن اليتيمة لا تنكح إلا بإذنها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2093), al-Tirmidhi (1109), al-Nasa’i (3270), and Ahmad (7519).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the orphan girl not being married except with her permission","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The orphan girl is asked for permission regarding herself. If she remains silent, that is her permission, and if she refuses, she is not to be forced.” Meaning: when she reaches maturity and rejects it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2093)، والترمذي (1109)، والنسائي (237)، وأحمد (7572)."},{"num":6261,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["اللهِ بْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: الْأَيِّمُ أَوْلَى بِأَمْرِهَا، وَالْيَتِيمَةُ تُسْتَأْمَرُ فِي نَفْسِهَا، وَإِذْنُهَا صُمَاتُهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3262) عن أحمد بن سعيد الرباطي، قال: حدثنا يعقوب، قال: حدثني أبي، عن ابن إسحاق قال: حدثني صالح بن كيسان، عن عبد الله بن الفضل بن عباس بن ربيعة، عن نافع بن جبير بن مطعم، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن اليتيمة لا تنكح إلا بإذنها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3262), Ahmad (2365), Ibn Abi Shaybah (4/136), and al-Daraqutni (3/238–239).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the orphan girl not being married except with her permission","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The previously married woman has more right concerning her affair, and the orphan girl is asked for permission regarding herself, and her permission is her silence.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3262)، وأحمد (2365)، وابن أبي شيبة (4/136)، والدارقطني (3575)."},{"num":6262,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لاَ تَسْأَلِ الْمَرْأَةُ طَلاَقَ أُخْتِهَا لِتَسْتَفْرِغَ صَحْفَتَهَا، وَلْتَنْكِحْ، فَإِنَّ لَهَا مَا قُدِّرَ لَهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في القدر (7) عن أبي الزّناد، عن الأعرج، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره. ورواه البخاري في القدر (6601) من طريق مالك، به.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب اشتراط المرأة أن يطلق الزوجُ زوجتَه الأولى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (7), al-Bukhari (6601), and Muslim (38:1408).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman stipulating that a husband divorce his first wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman must not ask for her sister to be divorced so that she may empty her bowl. Let her marry, for she will only have what has been decreed for her.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His saying, “her bowl,” refers to a dish from the dishes used for food."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (7)، والبخاري (6601)، ومسلم (38:1408)."},{"num":6263,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: نَهَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَنِ التَّلَقِّي، وَأَنْ يَبْتَاعَ الْمُهَاجِرُ لِلأَعْرَابِيِّ، وَأَنْ تَشْتَرِطَ الْمَرْأَةُ طَلاَقَ أُخْتِهَا، وَأَنْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الشروط (2727) عن محمد بن عرعرة، حدثنا شعبة، عن عدي بن ثابت، عن أبي حازم، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اشتراط المرأة أن يطلق الزوجُ زوجتَه الأولى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (2727).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman stipulating that a husband divorce his first wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade meeting traders before they reached the market, forbade a townsman from buying on behalf of a Bedouin, and forbade a woman from stipulating the divorce of her sister… the rest of the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2727)."},{"num":6264,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتِ: اخْتَصَمَ سَعْدُ بْنُ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ وَعَبْدُ بْنُ زَمْعَةَ فِي غُلاَمٍ. فَقَالَ سَعْدٌ: هَذَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ابْنُ أَخِي عُتْبَةَ بْنِ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ عَهد إليَّ أَنَّهُ ابْنُهُ. انْظُرْ إِلَى شَبَهِهِ، وَقَالَ عَبْدُ بْنُ زَمْعَةَ: هَذَا أَخِي يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وُلِدَ عَلَى فِرَاشِ أَبِي مِنْ وَلِيدَتِهِ. فَنَظَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى شَبَهِهِ فَرَأَى شَبَهًا بَيِّنًا بعُتْبة فَقَالَ: هُوَ لَكَ يَا عَبْدُ بن زَمْعَةَ، الْوَلَدُ لِلْفِرَاشِ، وَلِلْعَاهِرِ الْحَجَرُ وَاحْتَجِبِي مِنْهُ يَا سَوْدَةُ بِنْتَ زَمْعَةَ فَلَمْ تَرَهُ قَطُّ، وَفِي رِوَايَةِ زيادة: هُوَ أَخُوكَ يَا عَبْدُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الأقضية (22) عن ابن شهاب، عن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته. ورواه البخاري في البيوع (2218) ومسلم في الرضاعة (1457) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا الليث، عن ابن شهاب بإسناده مثله.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب اشتراط المرأة أن يطلق الزوجُ زوجتَه الأولى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (22), al-Bukhari (2218), and Muslim (1457).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman stipulating that a husband divorce his first wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: Sa‘d ibn Abi Waqqas and ‘Abdullah ibn Zam‘ah disputed over a boy. Sa‘d said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the son of my brother ‘Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas. He entrusted me that he was his son. Look at his resemblance. ‘Abd ibn Zam‘ah said: This is my brother, O Messenger of Allah. He was born on my father’s bed from his slave-woman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at his resemblance and saw a clear resemblance to ‘Utbah, so he said: “He is yours, O ‘Abd ibn Zam‘ah. The child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone. And veil yourself from him, O Sawdah bint Zam‘ah.” So she never saw him again. In another narration there is the addition: “He is your brother, O ‘Abd.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (22)، والبخاري (2218)، ومسلم (1457)."},{"num":6265,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ،. أَنَّ رَجُلاً، مِنْ أَهْلِ الْبَادِيَةِ أَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! إِنَّ امْرَأَتِي وَلَدَتْ عَلَى فِرَاشِي غُلاَمًا أَسْوَدَ، وَإِنَّا أَهْلُ بَيْتٍ لَمْ يَكُنْ فِينَا أَسْوَدُ قَطُّ. قَالَ: هَلْ لَكَ مِنَ إِبِلٍ. قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَمَا أَلْوَانُهَا. قَالَ: حُمْرٌ. قَالَ: هَلْ فِيهَا أَسْوَدُ. قَالَ: لاَ. قَالَ: فَهَلْ فِيهَا أَوْرَقُ. قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَأَنَّى كَانَ ذَلِكَ. قَالَ: عَسَى أَنْ يَكُونَ نَزَعَهُ عِرْقٌ. قَالَ: فَلَعَلَّ ابْنَكَ هَذَا نَزَعَهُ عِرْقٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (2003) عن أبي كريب، قال: حدثنا عبادة بن كليب الليثي أبو غسان، عن جويرية بن أسماء، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب اشتراط المرأة أن يطلق الزوجُ زوجتَه الأولى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Majah (2003).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman stipulating that a husband divorce his first wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar narrated that a man from the desert came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife has given birth on my bed to a black boy, and we are a household in which there has never been any black person. He said: “Do you have camels?” He said: Yes. He said: “What are their colors?” He said: Red. He said: “Are there any black among them?” He said: No. He said: “Are there any grayish ones among them?” He said: Yes. He said: “How did that happen?” He said: Perhaps some inherited trait drew it out. He said: “Then perhaps this son of yours was likewise drawn out by an inherited trait.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (2003)."},{"num":6266,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قـال: قـال النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْوَلَدُ لِلْفِرَاشِ وَلِلْعَاهِرِ الْحَجَرُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الحدود (6818) عن آدم، حدثنا شعبة، حدثنا محمد بن زياد، قال: سمعت أبا هريرة يقول: فذكره. ورواه مسلم في الرضاع (1458) من أوجه أخرى عن أبي هريرة مثله.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب اشتراط المرأة أن يطلق الزوجُ زوجتَه الأولى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (6818) and Muslim (1458).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman stipulating that a husband divorce his first wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “The child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6818)، ومسلم (1458)."},{"num":6267,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْوَلَدُ لِلْفِرَاشِ، وَلِلْعَاهِرِ الْحَجَرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3486) وابن حبان (4104) كلاهما من حديث جرير، عن مغيرة، عن أبي وائل، عن عبد الله فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اشتراط المرأة أن يطلق الزوجُ زوجتَه الأولى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3486) and Ibn Hibban (4104).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman stipulating that a husband divorce his first wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Mas‘ud said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3486)، وابن حبان (4104)."},{"num":6268,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَضَى بِالْوَلَدِ لِلْفِرَاشِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجة (2005) وأحمد (173) كلاهما من حديث سفيان بن عيينة، عن عبيد الله بن أبي يزيد، عن أبيه، عن عمر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اشتراط المرأة أن يطلق الزوجُ زوجتَه الأولى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Majah (2005) and Ahmad (173).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman stipulating that a husband divorce his first wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the child belongs to the marriage bed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (2005)، وأحمد (173)."},{"num":6269,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَمْرِو بْنِ شُعَيْبٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، عَنْ جَدِّهِ، قَالَ: قَامَ رَجُلٌ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! إِنَّ فُلاَنًا ابْنِي، عَاهَرْتُ بِأُمِّهِ فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لاَ دِعْوَةَ فِي الإِسْلاَمِ، ذَهَبَ أَمْرُ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، الْوَلَدُ لِلْفِرَاشِ، وَلِلْعَاهِرِ الْحَجَرُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2274) عن زهير بن حرب، حدثنا يزيد بن هارون، أخبرنا حسين المعلم، عن عمرو بن شعيب بإسناده فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب اشتراط المرأة أن يطلق الزوجُ زوجتَه الأولى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2274) and Imam Ahmad (6933).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman stipulating that a husband divorce his first wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abdullah ibn ‘Amr ibn al-‘As said: A man stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so is my son; I committed fornication with his mother in the pre-Islamic period. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no such claim in Islam. The matter of the pre-Islamic period has passed. The child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word translated here as “claim” refers to a man attributing himself to someone other than his real father and tribe. They used to do that in the pre-Islamic period. Islam prohibited it and assigned the child to the marriage bed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2274)، والإمام أحمد (6933)."},{"num":6270,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي أمامة الباهلي يقول: سمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول في خطبة عام حجة الواداع: الولد للفراش وللعاهر الحجر."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (2120) وأبو داود (3565) وابن ماجة (2007) وأحمد (22294) كلهم من حديث إسماعيل بن عياش قال:حدثنا شُرحبيل بن مسلم قال: سمعت أبا أمامة الباهلي فذكر الحديث في سياق طويل وفيه هذا الجزء، إلا أن أبا داود لم يذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب اشتراط المرأة أن يطلق الزوجُ زوجتَه الأولى","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (2120), Abu Dawud (3565), Ibn Majah (2007), and Ahmad (22294).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a woman stipulating that a husband divorce his first wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Umamah al-Bahili said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in the sermon of the Farewell Pilgrimage: “The child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Legal understanding of this chapter: It was among the customs of the pre-Islamic period to attach lineage through fornication. They used to hire slave women for intercourse, and if the mother acknowledged that the child belonged to a certain man, they would attach him to him. Islam came and abolished that, and commanded that the child be attributed to the marriage bed. This is what occurred in the dispute between Sa‘d ibn Abi Waqqas and ‘Abd ibn Zam‘ah ibn al-Aswad over a boy. ‘Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas had intercourse with the slave woman of Zam‘ah ibn al-Aswad, so she became pregnant and gave birth to a boy. When ‘Utbah was on his deathbed, he instructed his brother Sa‘d to take this boy and attribute him to him. ‘Utbah then died as a polytheist. After that, Sa‘d and ‘Abd ibn Zam‘ah disputed about the boy. Sa‘d argued for attributing the boy to his brother ‘Utbah according to their old custom of attributing children through fornication, while ‘Abd ibn Zam‘ah relied on his father’s marriage bed. So the Prophet ﷺ ruled: “The child belongs to the marriage bed,” and cut off attribution through fornication by saying: “and the adulterer gets the stone.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (2120)، وأبو داود (3565)، وابن ماجه (2007)، وأحمد (22294)."},{"num":6271,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ دَخَلَ عَلَىَّ مَسْرُورًا تَبْرُقُ أَسَارِيرُ وَجْهِهِ، فَقَالَ: أَلَمْ تَرَىْ أَنَّ مُجَزِّزًا نَظَرَ آنِفًا إِلَى زَيْدِ بْنِ حَارِثَةَ وَأُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ، فَقَالَ: إِنَّ هَذِهِ الأَقْدَامَ بَعْضُهَا مِنْ بَعْضٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الحدود (6770) ومسلم في الرضاع (1459) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا الليث، عن ابن شهاب، عن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ثبوت النسب بالقافة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (6770) and Muslim (1459).","chapter_en":"Chapter on establishing lineage through expert resemblance-tracing","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع أبواب ما جاء في النكاح وشروطه","group_en":"Collected chapters on what has been reported regarding marriage and its conditions","part_no":24,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me happy, with the lines of his face shining, and said: “Did you not see that Mujazziz just now looked at Zayd ibn Harithah and Usamah ibn Zayd and said: These feet belong to one another?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6770)، ومسلم (1459)."},{"num":6272,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ   قَالَ: لاَ يَخْطُبُ أَحَدُكُمْ عَلَى خِطْبَةِ أَخِيهِ.","وزاد في رواية: حَتَّى يَتْرُكَ الْخَاطِبُ قَبْلَهُ، أَوْ يَأْذَنَ لَهُ الْخَاطِبُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في النكاح (2) عن نافع، عن عبد الله بن عمر، فذكره. ورواه البخاري في النكاح (5142) من طريق ابن جريج. والزيادة المذكورة له. ومسلم في النكاح (1412) من طريق الليث (هو ابن سعد)، وعبيد الله ( هو ابن عمر) وأيوب أربعتهم عن نافع، به، نحوه وزاد في أوله النهي عن بيع الرجل عن بيع أخيه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب النهي أن يخطب الرّجل على خِطبة أخيه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (2), al-Bukhari (5142), and Muslim (1412).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the prohibition of a man proposing over his brother’s proposal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should propose over the proposal of his brother.” In another narration there is an addition: “Until the first suitor leaves it or gives him permission.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (2) والبخاري (5142) ومسلم (1412)."},{"num":6273,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  قَالَ: لاَ يَخْطُبْ أَحَدُكُمْ عَلَى خِطْبَةِ أَخِيهِ حَتَّى يَنْكِحَ أَوْ يَتْرُكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في النكاح (1) عن محمد بن يحيى بن حبّان، عن الأعرج، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب النهي أن يخطب الرّجل على خِطبة أخيه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (1), al-Bukhari (5143), and Muslim (1413).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the prohibition of a man proposing over his brother’s proposal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should propose over the proposal of his brother.” In another narration there is an addition: “Until he marries or leaves it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (1) والبخاري (5143) ومسلم (1413)."},{"num":6274,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي بَكْرِ بْنِ أَبِي الْجَهْمِ بْنِ صُخَيْرٍ الْعَدَوِيِّ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ فَاطِمَةَ بِنْتَ قَيْسٍ تَقُولُ:  إِنَّ زَوْجَهَا طَلَّقَهَا ثَلَاثًا، فَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ لَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سُكْنَى وَلَا نَفَقَةً. قَالَتْ: قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا حَلَلْتِ فَآذِنِينِي، فَآذَنْتُهُ، فَخَطَبَهَا مُعَاوِيَةُ، وَأَبُو جَهْمٍ، وَأُسَامَةُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَمَّا مُعَاوِيَةُ فَرَجُلٌ تَرِبٌ لَا مَالَ لَهُ، وَأَمَّا أَبُو جَهْمٍ فَرَجُلٌ ضَرَّابٌ لِلنِّسَاءِ، وَلَكِنْ أُسَامَةُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ، فَقَالَتْ بِيَدِهَا هَكَذَا: أُسَامَةُ، أُسَامَةُ! فَقَالَ لَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: طَاعَةُ اللهِ وَطَاعَةُ رَسُولِهِ خَيْرٌ لَكِ، قَالَتْ: فَتَزَوَّجْتُهُ، فَاغْتَبَطْتُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الطلاق (47:1480) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا وكيع، حدثنا سليمان، عن أبي بكر بن أبي الجهم فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النهي أن يخطب الرّجل على خِطبة أخيه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (47:1480). His saying “tārib” means poor, because from the severity of his poverty he is as though attached to the dust.","chapter_en":"Chapter on the prohibition of a man proposing over his brother’s proposal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm ibn Sukhayr al-‘Adawi said: I heard Fatimah bint Qays say that her husband divorced her three times, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not assign for her any housing or maintenance. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “When you become lawful for marriage, inform me.” So I informed him. Then Mu‘awiyah, Abu Jahm, and Usamah ibn Zayd proposed to her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “As for Mu‘awiyah, he is a poor man with no wealth. As for Abu Jahm, he is a man who beats women. Rather, marry Usamah ibn Zayd.” She gestured with her hand like this and said: Usamah? Usamah? So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “Obedience to Allah and obedience to His Messenger are better for you.” She said: So I married him and was greatly pleased."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (47:1480). وقوله: (( ترب )) يعني الفقير، لأنه من شدة فقره يكون ملصقا بالتراب."},{"num":6275,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَلَمَةَ، أَنَّ فَاطِمَةَ بِنْتَ قَيْسٍ – أُخْتَ الضَّحَّاكِ بْنِ قَيْسٍ-أَخْبَرَتْهُ أنّ أَبَا حَفْصِ ابن الْمُغِيرَةِ الْمَخْزُومِيَّ طَلَّقَهَا ثَلَاثًا. ثُمَّ انْطَلَقَ إِلَى الْيَمَنِ. فَقَالَ لَهَا أَهْلُهُ: لَيْسَ لَكِ عَلَيْنَا نَفَقَةٌ فَانْطَلَقَ خَالِدُ بْنُ الْوَلِيدِ فِي نَفَرٍ، فَأَتَوْا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَيْتِ مَيْمُونَةَ. فَقَالُوا: إِنَّ أَبَا حَفْصٍ طلّق امْرَأَتَهُ ثَلَاثًا، فَهَلْ لَهَا مِنْ نَفَقَةٍ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَيْسَتْ لَهَا نَفَقَةٌ، وَعَلَيْهَا الْعِدَّةُ وَأَرْسَلَ إِلَيْهَا: أَنْ لَا تَسْبِقِينِي بِنَفْسِكِ ... الحديث. وَفِي لفظ : لَا تفوتينا بِنَفْسِكِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الطلاق (38:1480) عن محمد بن رافع، حدّثنا حسين بن محمد، حدّثنا شيبان، عن يحيى ( وهو ابن كثير)، أخبرني أبو سلمة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب التعريض لخطبة المرأة المتوفى عنها زوجها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (38:1480). His saying “Do not get ahead of us regarding yourself” contains an indirect indication of proposing.","chapter_en":"Chapter on indirect mention of proposing to a woman whose husband has died","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Salamah reported that Fatimah bint Qays, the sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, informed him that Abu Hafs ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi divorced her three times, then left for Yemen. His family said to her: You have no maintenance due from us. So Khalid ibn al-Walid went with a group to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the house of Maymunah and said: Abu Hafs has divorced his wife three times, so does she have any maintenance? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “She has no maintenance, but she must observe the waiting period.” And he sent word to her: “Do not get ahead of us regarding yourself…” in the rest of the hadith. In another wording: “Do not let us miss the chance regarding yourself.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى: ﴿ وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيمَا عَرَّضْتُمْ بِهِ مِنْ خِطْبَةِ النِّسَاءِ أَوْ أَكْنَنْتُمْ فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ ﴾ [البقرة: ٢٣٥]","قال ابن عباس: ( فِيمَا عَرَّضْتُمْ ) يقول:  إني أريد التزويج، ولوددتُ أنه يُيسَّر لي امرأة صالحة .","صحيح: رواه البخاري (٥١٢٤)."],"en":["Allah Most High said: “There is no blame upon you for what you indirectly allude to concerning a proposal to women, or what you keep concealed within yourselves.” [al-Baqarah: 235]","Ibn ‘Abbas said regarding “what you indirectly allude to”: It means saying, “I wish to marry, and I would like for a righteous woman to be made easy for me.”","Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5124)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (38:1480). وقوله: “لا تسبقيني” فيه التعريض بالخطبة."},{"num":6276,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُعَلِّمُنَا الاِسْتِخَارَةَ فِي الأُمُورِ كَمَا يُعَلِّمُنَا السُّورَةَ مِنَ الْقُرْآنِ يَقُولُ: إِذَا هَمَّ أَحَدُكُمْ بِالأَمْرِ، فَلْيَرْكَعْ رَكْعَتَيْنِ مِنْ غَيْرِ الْفَرِيضَةِ ثُمَّ لِيَقُلِ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْتَخِيرُكَ بِعِلْمِكَ، وَأَسْتَقْدِرُكَ بِقُدْرَتِكَ، وَأَسْأَلُكَ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ الْعَظِيمِ، فَإِنَّكَ تَقْدِرُ، وَلاَ أَقْدِرُ، وَتَعْلَمُ، وَلاَ أَعْلَمُ، وَأَنْتَ عَلاَّمُ الْغُيُوبِ، اللَّهُمَّ إِنْ كُنْتَ تَعْلَمُ أَنَّ هَذَا الأَمْرَ خَيْرٌ لِي فِي دِينِي وَمَعَاشِي وَعَاقِبَةِ أَمْرِي ـ أَوْ قَالَ عَاجِلِ أَمْرِي وَآجِلِهِ ـ فَاقْدُرْهُ لِي وَيَسِّرْهُ لِي ثُمَّ بَارِكْ لِي فِيهِ، وَإِنْ كُنْتَ تَعْلَمُ أَنَّ هَذَا الأَمْرَ شَرٌّ لِي فِي دِينِي، وَمَعَاشِي، وَعَاقِبَةِ أَمْرِي ـ أَوْ قَالَ فِي عَاجِلِ أَمْرِي وَآجِلِهِ ـ فَاصْرِفْهُ عَنِّي، وَاصْرِفْنِي عَنْهُ، وَاقْدُرْ لِي الْخَيْرَ حَيْثُ كَانَ، ثُمَّ أَرْضِنِي، بِهِ ـ قَالَ: ـ وَيُسَمِّي حَاجَتَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في التهجد (1162) عن قتيبة قال: حدثنا عبد الرحمن بن أبي الموالِ، عن محمد بن المنكدر، عن جابر بن عبدالله فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الاستخارة في الخِطبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1162).","chapter_en":"Chapter on seeking guidance in betrothal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us istikhārah concerning all matters just as he would teach us a surah from the Qurʾān. He would say: “When one of you intends to undertake a matter, let him pray two rakʿahs other than the obligatory prayer, then say: ‘O Allah, I seek the better choice from You by Your knowledge, and I seek ability from You by Your power, and I ask You from Your immense bounty. You are able and I am not; You know and I do not know; and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if You know that this matter is good for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair—or he said: in the immediate and later parts of my affair—then decree it for me, make it easy for me, and then bless it for me. And if You know that this matter is bad for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair—or he said: in the immediate and later parts of my affair—then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, decree good for me wherever it may be, and then make me content with it.’” He said: “And he should mention his particular need.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1162)."},{"num":6277,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَيُّوبَ بْنِ خَالِدِ بْنِ أَبِي أَيُّوبَ الْأَنْصَارِيِّ، حَدَّثَهُ عَنْ أَبِيهِ، عَنْ جَدِّهِ أَبِي أَيُّوبَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: اكْتُمِ الْخِطْبَةَ، ثُمَّ تَوَضَّأْ فَأَحْسِنْ وُضُوءَكَ، ثُمَّ صلِّ مَا كَتَبَ اللهُ لَكَ، ثُمَّ احْمَدْ ربّك، وَمَجِّدْهُ ثُمَّ قُلْ: اللهُمَّ إِنَّكَ تَقْدِرُ وَلَا أَقْدِرُ، وَتَعْلَمُ وَلَا أَعْلَمُ، وَأَنْتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوبِ، فَإِنْ رَأَيْتَ فِي فُلَانَةَ – تُسَمِّيهَا بِاسْمِهَا-خَيْرًا لِي فِي دِينِي وَدُنْيَايَ وَآخِرَتِي فَاقْدِرْهَا لِي، وَإِنْ كَانَ غَيْرُهَا خَيْرًا لِي مِنْهَا فِي دِينِي وَدُنْيَايَ وَآخِرَتِي فَاقْضِ لِي ذَلِكَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23597) وابن خزيمة (1220) وابن حبان (4040) والحاكم (1181) والبيهقي (13837) وابن المنذر في الأوسط (8/233) كلهم من طريق ابن وهب، أخبرني حيوة، أن الوليد بن الوليد أخبره، أن أيوب بن خالد بن أبي أيوب حدثه بإسناده ومعناه. قال الحاكم: هذه سنة صلاة الاستخارة عزيزة تفرد بها أهل مصر، ورواته عن أخرهم ثقات، ولم يخرجاه.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الاستخارة في الخِطبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (23597), Ibn Khuzaymah (1220), Ibn Hibban (4040), and al-Hakim (1181).","chapter_en":"Chapter on seeking guidance in betrothal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ayyub ibn Khalid ibn Abi Ayyub al-Ansari narrated from his father, from his grandfather Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Keep the proposal concealed, then perform ablution and do it well, then pray whatever Allah has prescribed for you, then praise your Lord and glorify Him, then say: O Allah, You are able and I am not able, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If You know that there is good for me in so-and-so — naming her by name — in my religion, my worldly life, and my Hereafter, then decree her for me. And if someone other than her is better for me than her in my religion, my worldly life, and my Hereafter, then decree that for me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23597)، وابن خزيمة (1220)، وابن حبان (4040)، والحاكم (1181)."},{"num":6278,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سهيل بن سَعْدٍ: أَنَّ امْرَأَةً جَاءَتْ إِلَى رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، جئتُ لأَهَبَ لَكَ نَفْسِي! فَنَظَرَ إِلَيْهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَصَعَّدَ النَّظَرَ إِلَيْهَا وَصَوَّبَهُ، ثُمَّ طَأْطَأَ رَأْسَهُ. فَلَمَّا رَأَتِ الْمَرْأَةُ أَنَّهُ لَمْ يَقْضِ فِيهَا شَيْئًا جَلَسَتْ.....الحديث."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5126) ومسلم في النكاح(76:1425)كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد الثقفي، حدّثنا يعقوب ( يعني ابن عبدالرحمن القاريّ)، عن أبي حازم، عن سهل بن سعد، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب النظر إلى المخطوبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5126) and Muslim (1425/76).","chapter_en":"Chapter on looking at the woman one intends to marry","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd reported: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have come to offer myself to you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at her, looking her up and down, then lowered his head. When the woman saw that he had not made any decision concerning her, she sat down… the remainder of the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5126)، ومسلم (76:1425)."},{"num":6279,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ:  كُنْتُ عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَتَاهُ رَجُلٌ، فَأَخْبَرَهُ أَنَّهُ تَزَوَّجَ امْرَأَةً مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَنَظَرْتَ إِلَيْهَا؟ قَالَ: لَا، قَالَ: فَاذْهَبْ، فَانْظُرْ إِلَيْهَا، فَإِنَّ فِي أَعْيُنِ الْأَنْصَارِ شَيْئًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في النكاح (1424: 74) عن ابن أبي عمر، حدّثنا سفيان، عن يزيد بن كيسان، عن أبي حازم، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النظر إلى المخطوبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (74:1424). His statement “there is something in the eyes of the Ansar” was said by some to mean smallness, and by others to mean a bluish tint.","chapter_en":"Chapter on looking at the woman one intends to marry","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and informed him that he had married a woman from the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Did you look at her?” He said: No. He said: “Then go and look at her, for there is something in the eyes of the Ansar.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1424: 74). قوله: (( في أعين الأنصار شيئا )) قيل المراد بذلك صغر، وقيل زرقة."},{"num":6280,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي حُمَيْدٍ أَوْ أَبِي حُمَيْدَةَ - وَقَدْ رَأَى رسول اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ - قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا خَطَبَ أَحَدُكُمْ امْرَأَةً فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ يَنْظُرَ إِلَيْهَا، إِذَا كَانَ إِنَّمَا يَنْظُرُ لِخِطْبَةٍ، وَإِنْ كَانَتْ لَا تَعْلَمُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (23603) عن أبي كامل، حدثنا زهير، حدثنا عبدالله بن عيسى، حدثني موسى بن عبدالله بن يزيد، عن أبي حُميد أو أبي حميدة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النظر إلى المخطوبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ahmad (23602).","chapter_en":"Chapter on looking at the woman one intends to marry","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Humayd, or Abu Humaydah — and he had seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you proposes to a woman, there is no blame on him if he looks at her, so long as he is only looking for the sake of marriage, even if she does not know.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (23603)."},{"num":6281,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْمُغِيرَةِ بْنِ شُعْبَةَ، قَالَ: أَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَذَكَرْتُ لَهُ امْرَأَةً أَخْطُبُهَا، فَقَالَ: اذْهَبْ فَانْظُرْ إِلَيْهَا، فَإِنَّهُ أَجْدَرُ أَنْ يُؤْدَمَ بَيْنَكُمَا. فَأَتَيْتُ امْرَأَةً مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، فَخَطَبْتُهَا إِلَى أَبَوَيْهَا، وَأَخْبَرْتُهُمَا بِقَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. فَكَأَنَّهُمَا كَرِهَا ذَلِكَ. قَالَ: فَسَمِعَتْ ذَلِكَ الْمَرْأَةُ وَهِيَ فِي خِدْرِهَا، فَقَالَتْ: إِنْ كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمَرَكَ أَنْ تَنْظُرَ، فَانْظُرْ. وَإِلاَّ فَإِنِّي أَنْشُدُكَ. كَأَنَّهَا أَعْظَمَتْ ذَلِكَ. قَالَ: فَنَظَرْتُ إِلَيْهَا: فَتَزَوَّجْتُهَا. فَذَكَرَ مِنْ مُوَافَقَتِهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1087) والنسائي (3235) وابن ماجة (1866) وأحمد (18137) واللفظ له، والبيهقي (7/84-85) وابن الجارود (675) كلهم من حديث بكر بن عبد الله المزني، عن المغيرة بن شعبة فذكره. واختصر البعض. وزاد البيهقي: فما وقعت عندي امرأة بمنزلتها، ولقد تزوجت سبعين، أو بضع وسبعين امرأة.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النظر إلى المخطوبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (1087), al-Nasa’i (3235), Ibn Majah (1866), and Ahmad (18137). The wording is that of Ahmad.","chapter_en":"Chapter on looking at the woman one intends to marry","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Mughirah ibn Shu‘bah said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him a woman whom I intended to propose to. He said: “Go and look at her, for that is more likely to bring harmony between you.” He said: So I went to a woman from the Ansar and proposed to her through her parents, and I informed them of the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was as if they disliked that. Then the woman heard that while she was in her private chamber, and she said: If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded you to look, then look; otherwise, I place you under a solemn appeal. It was as though she regarded the matter as weighty for him. He said: So I looked at her and married her, and he mentioned her good compatibility."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1087)، والنسائي (3235)، وابن ماجه (1866)، وأحمد (18137)، واللفظ له."},{"num":6282,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ الْأَنْصَارِيِّ، قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: إِذَا خَطَبَ أَحَدُكُمُ الْمَرْأَةَ، فَقَدِرَ أَنْ يَرَى مِنْهَا بَعْضَ مَا يَدْعُوهُ إِلَيْهَا، فَلْيَفْعَلْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (14869) عن يعقوب، حدثنا أبي، عن ابن إسحاق، حدثني داود بن الحصين مولى عمرو بن عثمان، عن واقد بن عمرو بن سعد بن معاذ، عن جابر بن عبدالله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب النظر إلى المخطوبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (14869).","chapter_en":"Chapter on looking at the woman one intends to marry","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah al-Ansari said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you proposes to a woman, if he is able to see something of her that will encourage him to marry her, then let him do so.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (14869)."},{"num":6283,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَتَبَ عَلَى ابْنِ آدَمَ حَظَّهُ مِنَ الزِّنَا، أَدْرَكَ ذَلِكَ لاَ مَحَالَةَ، فَزِنَا الْعَيْنِ النَّظَرُ، وَزِنَا اللِّسَانِ الْمَنْطِقُ، وَالنَّفْسُ تمني وَتَشْتَهِي، وَالْفَرْجُ يُصَدِّقُ ذَلِكَ كُلَّهُ وَيُكَذِّبُهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الإستئذان (6243) ومسلم في القدر (2657) كلاهما من حديث عبد الرزاق، أخبرنا معمر، عن ابن طاوس، عن أبيه، عن ابن عباس قال: ما رأيت شيئاً أشبه باللمم مما قال قال أبو هريرة، عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فذكر الحديث.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في غض البصر وتحريم النظر إلى الأجنبية بغير قصد الخطبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (6243) and Muslim (2657).","chapter_en":"Chapter on lowering the gaze and the prohibition of looking at a non-related woman without the intention of betrothal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah has decreed for the son of Adam his share of adultery, and he will inevitably reach it. The adultery of the eye is looking, the adultery of the tongue is speaking, and the soul wishes and desires, while the private part confirms all of that or denies it.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى: ﴿ قُلْ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ يَغُضُّوا مِنْ أَبْصَارِهِمْ وَيَحْفَظُوا فُرُوجَهُمْ ذَٰلِكَ أَزْكَى لَهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ خَبِيرٌ بِمَا يَصْنَعُونَ ﴾ [النور: ٣٠]"],"en":["Allah Most High said: “Tell the believing men to lower their gaze and guard their private parts. That is purer for them. Indeed Allah is fully aware of what they do.” [Al-Nur: 30]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6243) ومسلم (2657)."},{"num":6284,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ:  كُتِبَ عَلَى ابْنِ آدَمَ نَصِيبُهُ مِنَ الزِّنَا، مُدْرِكٌ ذَلِكَ لَا مَحَالَةَ، فَالْعَيْنَانِ زِنَاهُمَا النَّظَرُ، وَالْأُذُنَانِ زِنَاهُمَا الِاسْتِمَاعُ، وَاللِّسَانُ زِنَاهُ الْكَلَامُ، وَالْيَدُ زِنَاهَا الْبَطْشُ، وَالرِّجْلُ زِنَاهَا الْخُطَا، وَالْقَلْبُ يَهْوَى وَيَتَمَنَّى، وَيُصَدِّقُ ذَلِكَ الْفَرْجُ وَيُكَذِّبُهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في القدر (21:2657) عن إسحاق بن منصور، أخبرنا أبو هشام المخزومي، حدثنا وُهيب، حدثنا سهيل بن أبي صالح، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في غض البصر وتحريم النظر إلى الأجنبية بغير قصد الخطبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (21:2657).","chapter_en":"Chapter on lowering the gaze and the prohibition of looking at a non-related woman without the intention of betrothal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “The share of adultery decreed for the son of Adam will inevitably reach him. The adultery of the eyes is looking, the adultery of the ears is listening, the adultery of the tongue is speech, the adultery of the hand is grasping, the adultery of the foot is walking, and the heart desires and wishes, while the private part confirms that or denies it.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Abu Dawud (2152) narrated it through another route and added: “And the mouth commits adultery, and its adultery is kissing.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12868],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (21:2657)."},{"num":6285,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَرِيرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ:  سَأَلْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَنْ نَظَرِ الْفُجَاءَةِ، فَأَمَرَنِي أَنْ أَصْرِفَ بَصَرِي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الآداب (2159) من طرق عن عمرو بن سعيد، عن أبي زرعة، عن جرير بن عبد الله، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في غض البصر وتحريم النظر إلى الأجنبية بغير قصد الخطبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2159).","chapter_en":"Chapter on lowering the gaze and the prohibition of looking at a non-related woman without the intention of betrothal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jarir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the accidental glance, and he ordered me to turn my gaze away."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[12865,14186],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2159)."},{"num":6286,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ بُرَيْدَةَ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِعَلِيٍّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ: يَا عَلِيُّ، لَا تُتْبِعِ النَّظْرَةَ النَّظْرَةَ، فَإِنَّ لَكَ الْأُولَى، وَلَيْسَتْ لَكَ الْآخِرَةُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2148) والترمذي (2777) والحاكم (2788) والبيهقي (13515) وأحمد (22974) والطحاوي في مشكله (1866) كلهم من حديث شريك، عن أبي ربيعة، عن ابن بريدة، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في غض البصر وتحريم النظر إلى الأجنبية بغير قصد الخطبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2148), al-Tirmidhi (2777), who graded it Hasan, al-Hakim (2788), and Ahmad (22974).","chapter_en":"Chapter on lowering the gaze and the prohibition of looking at a non-related woman without the intention of betrothal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Buraydah narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ‘Ali, do not follow one look with another, for you are allowed the first, but not the second.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12866],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2148)، والترمذي (2777) وحسنه، والحاكم (2788)، وأحمد (22974)."},{"num":6287,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ، قَالَ: قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا تُتْبِعِ النَّظَرَ النَّظَرَ، فَإِنَّ الْأُولَى لَكَ، وَلَيْسَتْ لَكَ الْآخِرَةُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (1369) والبزار – كشف الأستار (907) والدارمي (2751) والطحاوي في مشكله (1865) وابن حبان (5570) والحاكم (4623) كلهم من طرق عن حماد بن سلمة، عن محمد بن إسحاق، عن محمد بن إبراهيم، عن سلمة بن أبي الطفيل، عن علي فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في غض البصر وتحريم النظر إلى الأجنبية بغير قصد الخطبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (1369), al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (907), al-Darimi (2751), and al-Tahawi in Mushkil al-Athar (1865).","chapter_en":"Chapter on lowering the gaze and the prohibition of looking at a non-related woman without the intention of betrothal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Do not follow one look with another, for the first is for you, but the second is not for you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (1369)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (907)، والدارمي (2751)، والطحاوي في مشكله (1865)."},{"num":6288,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي بَرْزَةَ الْأَسْلَمِيِّ، أَنَّ جُلَيْبِيبًا كَانَ امْرَأً يَدْخُلُ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ، يَمُرُّ بِهِنَّ وَيُلَاعِبُهُنَّ، فَقُلْتُ لِامْرَأَتِي: لَا يَدْخُلَنَّ عَلَيْكُمْ جُلَيْبِيبٌ؛ فَإِنَّهُ إِنْ دَخَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ، لَأَفْعَلَنَّ وَلَأَفْعَلَنَّ. قَالَ: وَكَانَتِ الْأَنْصَارُ إِذَا كَانَ لِأَحَدِهِمْ أَيِّمٌ، لَمْ يُزَوِّجْهَا حَتَّى يَعْلَمَ هَلْ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِيهَا حَاجَةٌ؟ أَمْ لَا. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِرَجُلٍ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ: زَوِّجْنِي ابْنَتَكَ. فَقَالَ: نِعِمَّ وَكَرَامَةٌ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَنُعْمَ عَيْنِي. قَالَ: إِنِّي لَسْتُ أُرِيدُهَا لِنَفْسِي. قَالَ: فَلِمَنْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: لِجُلَيْبِيبٍ.: قَالَ: فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أُشَاوِرُ أُمَّهَا. فَأَتَى أُمَّهَا، فَقَالَ: رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَخْطُبُ ابْنَتَكِ. فَقَالَتْ: نِعِمَّ. وَنُعْمَةُ عَيْنِي. فَقَالَ: إِنَّهُ لَيْسَ يَخْطُبُهَا لِنَفْسِهِ، إِنَّمَا يَخْطُبُهَا لِجُلَيْبِيبٍ. فَقَالَتْ: أَجُلَيْبِيبٌ إنية؟ أَجُلَيْبِيبٌ إنية؟ أَجُلَيْبِيبٌ إنية؟ لَا. لَعَمْرُ اللهِ، لَا نُزَوَّجُهُ. فَلَمَّا أَرَادَ أَنْ يَقُومَ لِيَأْتِيَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِيُخْبِرَهُ بِمَا قَالَتْ أُمُّهَا: قَالَتِ الْجَارِيَةُ: مَنْ خَطَبَنِي إِلَيْكُمْ؟ فَأَخْبَرَتْهَا أُمُّهَا. فَقَالَتْ: أَتَرُدُّونَ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمْرَهُ؟ ادْفَعُونِي؛ فَإِنَّهُ لَمْ يُضَيِّعْنِي. فَانْطَلَقَ أَبُوهَا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَخْبَرَهُ، فَقَالَ: شَأْنَكَ بِهَا. فَزَوَّجَهَا جُلَيْبِيبًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (19784) عن عفان، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن ثابت، عن كنانة بن نُعيم العَدوي، عن أبي برزة الأسلمي فذكره. قال أحمد: ما حدّث به في الدنيا أحد إلا حماد بن سلمة ما أحسنه من حديث.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب للإمام أن يخطب إلى من أحب على من أحب من رعيته","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ahmad (19784).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the leader proposing on behalf of whomever he wishes among his subjects","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في الخِطبة","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding betrothal","part_no":24,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Barzah al-Aslami reported that Julaybib was a man who used to enter among the women and joke with them, so I said to my wife: Do not let Julaybib enter upon you, for if he enters, I will certainly do such-and-such. He said: The Ansar, if one of them had an unmarried woman, would not marry her until they knew whether the Prophet ﷺ had any interest in her or not. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man from the Ansar: “Marry your daughter to me.” He said: Yes, with honor, O Messenger of Allah, and gladly. He said: “I do not want her for myself.” He said: Then for whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “For Julaybib.” He said: So he said: O Messenger of Allah, let me consult her mother. He went to her mother and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is proposing for your daughter. She said: Yes, gladly and with full welcome. He said: He is not proposing for himself; he is proposing for Julaybib. She said: Julaybib? Him? Julaybib? Him? Julaybib? Him? No, by Allah, we will not marry her to him. When the father was about to leave to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him what her mother had said, the girl said: Who has proposed for me through you? Her mother told her. She said: Are you rejecting the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Give me in marriage, for he will not neglect me. So her father went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, and he said: “The matter is yours with her.” So he married her to Julaybib."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (19784)."},{"num":6289,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: جَلَسَ إِحْدَى عَشْرَةَ امْرَأَةً، فَتَعَاهَدْنَ وَتَعَاقَدْنَ أَنْ لاَ يَكْتُمْنَ مِنْ أَخْبَارِ أَزْوَاجِهِنَّ شَيْئًا. قَالَتِ الْأُولَى: زَوْجِي لَحْمُ جَمَلٍ، غَثٌّ، عَلَى رَأْسِ جَبَلٍ، لاَ سَهْلٍ فَيُرْتَقَى، وَلاَ سَمِينٍ فَيُنْتَقَلُ. قَالَتِ الثَّانِيَةُ: زَوْجِي لاَ أَبُثُّ خَبَرَهُ، إِنِّي أَخَافُ أَنْ لاَ أَذَرَهُ، إِنْ أَذْكُرْهُ أَذْكُرْ عُجَرَهُ وَبُجَرَهُ. قَالَتِ الثَّالِثَةُ: زَوْجِي الْعَشَنَّقُ، إِنْ أَنْطِقْ أُطَلَّقْ، وَإِنْ أَسْكُتْ أُعَلَّقْ. قَالَتِ الرَّابِعَةُ: زَوْجِي كَلَيْلِ تِهَامَةَ، لاَ حَرٌّ، وَلاَ قُرٌّ، وَلاَ مَخَافَةَ، وَلاَ سَآمَةَ. قَالَتِ الْخَامِسَةُ: زَوْجِي إِنْ دَخَلَ فَهِدَ، وَإِنْ خَرَجَ أَسِدَ، وَلاَ يَسْأَلُ عَمَّا عَهِدَ. قَالَتِ السَّادِسَةُ: زَوْجِي إِنْ أَكَلَ لَفَّ، وَإِنْ شَرِبَ اشْتَفَّ، وَإِنِ اضْطَجَعَ الْتَفَّ، وَلاَ يُولِجُ الْكَفَّ لِيَعْلَمَ الْبَثَّ، قَالَتِ السَّابِعَةُ: زَوْجِي غَيَايَاءُ أَوْ عَيَايَاءُ طَبَاقَاءُ، كُلُّ دَاءٍ لَهُ دَاءٌ، شَجَّكِ أَوْ فَلَّكِ أَوْ جَمَعَ كُلاًّ لَكِ. قَالَتِ الثَّامِنَةُ: زَوْجِي الْمَسُّ مَسُّ أَرْنَبٍ، وَالرِّيحُ رِيحُ زَرْنَبٍ. قَالَتِ التَّاسِعَةُ: زَوْجِي رَفِيعُ الْعِمَادِ، طَوِيلُ النِّجَادِ، عَظِيمُ الرَّمَادِ، قَرِيبُ الْبَيْتِ مِنَ النَّادِ. قَالَتِ الْعَاشِرَةُ: زَوْجِي مَالِكٌ، وَمَا مَالِكٌ، مَالِكٌ خَيْرٌ مِنْ ذَلِكِ، لَهُ إِبِلٌ كَثِيرَاتُ الْمَبَارِكِ، قَلِيلاَتُ الْمَسَارِحِ، وَإِذَا سَمِعْنَ صَوْتَ الْمِزْهَرِ، أَيْقَنَّ أَنَّهُنَّ هَوَالِكُ. قَالَتِ الْحَادِيَةَ عَشْرَةَ: زَوْجِي أَبُو زَرْعٍ، فَمَا أَبُو زَرْعٍ، أَنَاسَ مِنْ حُلِيٍّ أُذُنَىَّ، وَمَلأَ مِنْ شَحْمٍ عَضُدَىَّ، وَبَجَّحَنِي فَبَجِحَتْ إِلَىَّ نَفْسِي، وَجَدَنِي فِي أَهْلِ غُنَيْمَةٍ بِشِقٍّ، فَجَعَلَنِي فِي أَهْلِ صَهِيلٍ وَأَطِيطٍ، وَدَائِسٍ وَمُنَقٍّ، فَعِنْدَهُ أَقُولُ فَلاَ أُقَبَّحُ، وَأَرْقُدُ فَأَتَصَبَّحُ، وَأَشْرَبُ فَأَتَقَنَّحُ، أُمُّ أَبِي زَرْعٍ، فَمَا أُمُّ أَبِي زَرْعٍ عُكُومُهَا رَدَاحٌ، وَبَيْتُهَا فَسَاحٌ، ابْنُ أَبِي زَرْعٍ، فَمَا ابْنُ أَبِي زَرْعٍ، مَضْجِعُهُ كَمَسَلِّ شَطْبَةٍ، وَيُشْبِعُهُ ذِرَاعُ الْجَفْرَةِ، بِنْتُ أَبِي زَرْعٍ، فَمَا بِنْتُ أَبِي زَرْعٍ، طَوْعُ أَبِيهَا، وَطَوْعُ أُمِّهَا، وَمِلْءُ كِسَائِهَا، وَغَيْظُ جَارَتِهَا، جَارِيَةُ أَبِي زَرْعٍ، فَمَا جَارِيَةُ أَبِي زَرْعٍ، لاَ تَبُثُّ حَدِيثَنَا تَبْثِيثًا، وَلاَ تُنَقِّثُ مِيرَتَنَا تَنْقِيثًا، وَلاَ تَمْلأُ بَيْتَنَا تَعْشِيشًا، قَالَتْ: خَرَجَ أَبُو زَرْعٍ، وَالأَوْطَابُ تُمْخَضُ، فَلَقِيَ امْرَأَةً مَعَهَا وَلَدَانِ لَهَا كَالْفَهْدَيْنِ، يَلْعَبَانِ مِنْ تَحْتِ خَصْرِهَا بِرُمَّانَتَيْنِ، فَطَلَّقَنِي وَنَكَحَهَا، فَنَكَحْتُ بَعْدَهُ رَجُلاً سَرِيًّا، رَكِبَ شَرِيًّا، وَأَخَذَ خَطِّيًّا، وَأَرَاحَ عَلَىَّ نَعَمًا ثَرِيًّا، وَأَعْطَانِي مِنْ كُلِّ رَائِحَةٍ زَوْجًا، وَقَالَ، كُلِي أُمَّ زَرْعٍ، وَمِيرِي أَهْلَكِ. قَالَتْ: فَلَوْ جَمَعْتُ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ أَعْطَانِيهِ، مَا بَلَغَ أَصْغَرَ آنِيَةِ أَبِي زَرْعٍ. قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كُنْتُ لَكِ كَأَبِي زَرْعٍ لأُمِّ زَرْعٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5189) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2448) كلاهما عن علي بن حُجر، أخبرنا عيسى بن يونس، حدّثنا هشام بن عروة، عن عبد الله بن عروة، عن عروة، عن عائشة، فذكرته موقوفا إلا الجملة الأخيرة وهي قول النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: كُنْتُ لَكِ كَأَبِي زَرْعٍ لأُمِّ زَرْعٍ فهو مرفوع.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حسن المعاشرة مع الأهل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5189) and Muslim (2448).","chapter_en":"Chapter on good companionship with one’s family","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah reported: Eleven women sat together and pledged to one another that they would conceal nothing concerning their husbands. The first said: “My husband is like the meat of a lean camel on top of a mountain: the mountain is not easy to climb, nor is the meat fat enough to be worth carrying away.” The second said: “I will not disclose the story of my husband, for I fear that if I begin, I will not finish. If I mention him, I will have to mention all his outward and inward faults.” The third said: “My husband is tall and foolish. If I speak, I will be divorced; if I remain silent, I will be left suspended.” The fourth said: “My husband is like the night of Tihāmah: neither hot nor cold, and there is neither fear nor weariness with him.” The fifth said: “When my husband enters, he is like a leopard; when he goes out, he is like a lion, and he does not ask about what he has left behind.” The sixth said: “When my husband eats, he devours everything; when he drinks, he drains it all; when he lies down, he wraps himself up, and he does not extend his hand to discover what troubles me.” The seventh said: “My husband is foolish, helpless, and stupid. Every kind of defect is found in him. He may wound you, break you, or combine both against you.” The eighth said: “The touch of my husband is like the touch of a rabbit, and his fragrance is like the fragrance of sweet basil.” The ninth said: “My husband is lofty in his pillars, long in his sword-belt, great in his ashes, and his house is near the gathering place.” The tenth said: “My husband is Mālik. And what is Mālik? Mālik is better than all that. He has many camels that remain near the house and few that are sent out to pasture. Whenever they hear the sound of the lute, they know that they are about to be slaughtered for guests.” The eleventh said: “My husband is Abū Zarʿ. And what is Abū Zarʿ? He filled my ears with jewelry and filled my upper arms with flesh. He made me rejoice until I became pleased with myself. He found me among a poor family possessing only a few sheep in a narrow place, then brought me into a household of horses, camels, grain-threshing, and grain-cleaning. With him I speak and am not rebuked; I sleep until late in the morning; and I drink until I am completely satisfied. The mother of Abū Zarʿ—and what is the mother of Abū Zarʿ? Her storage bags are large and full, and her house is spacious. The son of Abū Zarʿ—and what is the son of Abū Zarʿ? His sleeping place is as slender as a drawn blade, and the foreleg of a young goat is enough to satisfy him. The daughter of Abū Zarʿ—and what is the daughter of Abū Zarʿ? She is obedient to her father and obedient to her mother, fills out her garment, and causes her co-wife to feel jealous. The servant-girl of Abū Zarʿ—and what is the servant-girl of Abū Zarʿ? She does not spread our secrets, does not waste our provisions, and does not fill our house with refuse. Abū Zarʿ went out while the milk-skins were being churned and met a woman who had two children like little leopards, playing beneath her waist with two pomegranates. He divorced me and married her. After him I married a noble man who rode a fine horse, carried an Indian spear, brought me abundant livestock, and gave me a pair of every kind. He said: ‘Eat, O Umm Zarʿ, and give provisions to your family.’ But even if I gathered together everything he gave me, it would not equal the smallest vessel of Abū Zarʿ.” ʿĀʾishah said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “I am to you as Abū Zarʿ was to Umm Zarʿ.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى: (وَعَاشِرُوهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ) [سورة النساء: ١٩]"],"en":["Allah Most High said: “And live with them in kindness.” [Surat al-Nisa’: 19]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5189)، ومسلم (2448)."},{"num":6290,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ النُّعْمَانِ بْنِ بَشِيرٍ، قَالَ: اسْتَأْذَنَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ رَحْمَةُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَسَمِعَ صَوْتَ عَائِشَةَ عَالِيًا، فَلَمَّا دَخَلَ تَنَاوَلَهَا لِيَلْطِمَهَا، وَقَالَ: لاَ أَرَاكِ تَرْفَعِينَ صَوْتَكِ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَجَعَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَحْجُزُهُ، وَخَرَجَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ مُغْضَبًا، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ خَرَجَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: كَيْفَ رَأَيْتِنِي أَنْقَذْتُكِ مِنَ الرَّجُلِ. قَالَ: فَمَكَثَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ أَيَّامًا، ثُمَّ اسْتَأْذَنَ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَوَجَدَهُمَا قَدِ اصْطَلَحَا، فَقَالَ لَهُمَا: أَدْخِلاَنِي فِي سِلْمِكُمَا كَمَا أَدْخَلْتُمَانِي فِي حَرْبِكُمَا. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قَدْ فَعَلْنَا، قَدْ فَعَلْنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4999) وأحمد (18394) كلاهما من حديث أبي إسحاق، عن العيزار بن حريث، عن النعمان بن بشير، فذكره، واللفظ لأبي داود. ولم يذكر أحمد قوله: قد فعلنا، قد فعلنا.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حسن المعاشرة مع الأهل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (4999) and Ahmad (18394). The wording is that of Abu Dawud. Ahmad did not mention the words, “We have done so, we have done so.”","chapter_en":"Chapter on good companionship with one’s family","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Nu‘man ibn Bashir said: Abu Bakr asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ and heard the voice of ‘A’ishah raised. When he entered, he moved toward her to slap her and said: Do I see you raising your voice over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? The Prophet ﷺ began restraining him, and Abu Bakr left angry. When Abu Bakr left, the Prophet ﷺ said: “How did you find that I rescued you from the man?” He said: Abu Bakr stayed away for some days, then asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found that the two had reconciled. So he said to them: Let me enter into your peace just as you made me enter into your conflict. The Prophet ﷺ said: “We have done so, we have done so.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4999) وأحمد (18394)، واللفظ لأبي داود. ولم يذكر أحمد قوله: (( قد فعلنا، قد فعلنا ))."},{"num":6291,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: جَاءَ رَجُلٌ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ امْرَأَتِي لاَ تَمْنَعُ يَدَ لاَمِسٍ. فَقَالَ: غَرِّبْها إِنَّ شئت. قَالَ: إِنِّي أَخَافُ أَنْ تَتْبَعَهَا نَفْسِي، قَالَ: استمتع بِهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2049) والنسائي (3464) والبيهقي (13871) من طريق أبي داود – كلاهما عن حسين بن حُريث المروزي، ثنا الفضل بن موسى، عن الحسين بن واقد، عن عمارة بن أبي حفصة، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره. غير إن أبا داود قال: كتب إليّ حسينُ بن حريث المروزي – يعني أنه رواه عنه كتابة.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حسن المعاشرة مع الأهل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2049), al-Nasa’i (3464), and al-Bayhaqi (7/154).","chapter_en":"Chapter on good companionship with one’s family","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My wife does not refuse the hand of one who touches. He said: “Divorce her if you wish.” The man said: I fear that my soul will still follow after her. He said: “Then continue to live with her.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2049) والنسائي (3464) والبيهقي (13871)."},{"num":6292,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّ رَجُلًا أَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنَّ لِيَ امْرَأَةً وَهِيَ لَا تَدْفَعُ يَدَ لَامِسٍ قَالَ: طَلِّقْهَا. قَالَ: إِنِّي أُحِبُّهَا وَهِيَ جَمِيلَةٌ قَالَ: فَاسْتَمْتِعْ بِهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البيهقي في السنن الكبرى (13873) من طرق عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر بن عبد الله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حسن المعاشرة مع الأهل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in al-Sunan al-Kubra (7/154–155).","chapter_en":"Chapter on good companionship with one’s family","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah reported that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife and she does not push away the hand of one who touches. He said: “Divorce her.” The man said: I love her and she is beautiful. He said: “Then continue to live with her.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “she does not prevent the hand of one who touches,” means that suspicion had entered the man’s heart regarding her, while at the same time he could not bear to part from her. So the Prophet ﷺ instructed him to remain with her and be patient, in hopes that her condition might improve.","The Prophet’s ﷺ statement, “continue to live with her,” is an indication of increasing intimacy with her in order to restrain her desire. And Allah Most High knows best."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البيهقي في السنن الكبرى (13873)."},{"num":6293,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: حُبِّبَ إِلَيَّ النِّسَاءُ، وَالطِّيبُ، وَجُعِلَ قُرَّةُ عَيْنِي فِي الصَّلَاةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3939) وأحمد (13057) والبيهقي (7/78) كلهم من حديث سلام أبي المنذر، عن ثابت، عن أنس فذكره واللفظ لأحمد.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حب النبي ﷺ للنساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3939), Ahmad (13057), and al-Bayhaqi (7/78).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the Prophet’s love for women","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Women and perfume have been made beloved to me, and the comfort of my eye has been placed in prayer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3939) وأحمد (13057) والبيهقي (7/78)."},{"num":6294,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: كُنْتُ أَلْعَبُ بِالْبَنَاتِ عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَكَانَ لِي صَوَاحِبُ يَلْعَبْنَ مَعِي، فَكَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذَا دَخَلَ يَتَقَمَّعْنَ مِنْهُ، فَيُسَرِّبُهُنَّ إِلَىَّ فَيَلْعَبْنَ مَعِي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الأدب (6130) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2440) كلاهما من طريق هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته، واللفظ للبخاري ولفظ مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب انبساط الرجل إلى زوجته","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (6130) and Muslim (2440).","chapter_en":"Chapter on a man being open and easy with his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: I used to play with dolls in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and I had girl-friends who played with me. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, they would hide from him, and he would send them to me so they could play with me."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Her statement, “I used to play with dolls,” shows the permissibility of playing with dolls.","Her statement, “they would hide,” means they would withdraw out of modesty and awe toward him.","Her statement, “he would send them,” means he would send them over and let them come to me."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14738,15630],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6130) ومسلم (2440)."},{"num":6295,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ: عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ:  مَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ، فَإِذَا شَهِدَ أَمْرًا فَلْيَتَكَلَّمْ بِخَيْرٍ أَوْ لِيَسْكُتْ، وَاسْتَوْصُوا بِالنِّسَاءِ، فَإِنَّ الْمَرْأَةَ خُلِقَتْ مِنْ ضِلَعٍ، وَإِنَّ أَعْوَجَ شَيْءٍ فِي الضِّلَعِ أَعْلَاهُ إِنْ ذَهَبْتَ تُقِيمُهُ كَسَرْتَهُ، وَإِنْ تَرَكْتَهُ لَمْ يَزَلْ أَعْوَجَ، اسْتَوْصُوا بِالنِّسَاءِ خَيْرًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5185-5186)، ومسلم في الرضاع (60:1468) كلاهما من طريق حسين بن علي الجُعفي، عن ميسرة، عن أبي حازم، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره. واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5185–5186) and Muslim (1468/60). This is Muslim’s wording.","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, when he is present at a matter, let him speak good or remain silent. Treat women well, for woman was created from a rib, and the most crooked part of the rib is its upper part. If you try to straighten it, you will break it; and if you leave it, it will remain crooked. So treat women well.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim also narrated through another route:","“Woman is like a rib. If you try to straighten her, you will break her; and if you leave her, you may enjoy life with her while crookedness remains in her.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5185-5186)، ومسلم (60:1468)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":6296,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  إِنَّ الْمَرْأَةَ خُلِقَتْ مِنْ ضِلَعٍ. لَنْ تَسْتَقِيمَ لَكَ عَلَى طَرِيقَةٍ، فَإِنِ اسْتَمْتَعْتَ بِهَا اسْتَمْتَعْتَ بِهَا، وَبِهَا عِوَجٌ، وَإِنْ ذَهَبْتَ تُقِيمُهَا كَسَرْتَهَا، وَكَسْرُهَا طَلَاقُهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في الرضاع (1468/61) من طرق عن سفيان، عن أبي الزناد، عن الأعرج، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره، واللفظ له.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (61:1468) and al-Bukhari (5184).","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Woman was created from a rib. She will never become completely straight for you upon one manner. If you enjoy life with her, you enjoy life with her while some crookedness remains in her. And if you try to straighten her, you will break her, and breaking her is divorcing her.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12120],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (1468/61) والبخاري (5184)."},{"num":6297,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  لَا يَفْرَكْ مُؤْمِنٌ مُؤْمِنَةً، إِنْ كَرِهَ مِنْهَا خُلُقًا رَضِيَ مِنْهَا آخَرَ، أَوْ قَالَ: غَيْرَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الرضاع (1469) عن إبراهيم بن موسى الرّازي، حدّثنا عيسى بن يونس، حدّثنا عبد الحميد بن جعفر، عن عمران بن أبي أنس، عن عمر بن الحكم، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1469).","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A believing man should not hate a believing woman. If he dislikes one trait in her, he will be pleased with another,” or he said, “with a different one.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “should not hate,” means should not loathe or detest. It is said in Arabic: he hated him, meaning he came to dislike him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1469)."},{"num":6298,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: وَلَوْلاَ بَنُو إِسْرَائِيلَ لَمْ يخبث الطّعام، وَلَمْ يَخْنَزِ اللَّحْمُ، وَلَوْلاَ حَوَّاءُ لَمْ تَخُنْ أُنْثَى زَوْجَهَا أبدَ الدَّهْرَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في أحاديث الأنبياء (3330)، ومسلم في الرضاع (63:1470) كلاهما من طريق معمر، عن همام بن منبّه قال: هذا ما حدّثنا أبو هريرة عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فذكر أحاديث، منها هذا الحديث واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (3330) and Muslim (63:1470), with this wording from Muslim.","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not for the Children of Israel, food would not spoil, and meat would not rot. And were it not for Hawwa’, no woman would ever betray her husband for all time.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “and meat would not rot,” means it would not become foul-smelling and change."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3330)، ومسلم (63:1470) واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":6299,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَمُرَةَ بْنِ جُنْدُبٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ الْمَرْأَةَ خُلِقَتْ مِنْ ضِلَعٍ، فَإِنْ أَقَمْتَهَا كَسَرْتَهَا، فَدَارِهَا تَعِشْ بِهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1476) والطبراني (6992) وابن حبان (4178) والحاكم (7333) كلهم من طريق عوف بن أبي جميلة، عن أبي رجاء العطاردي، عن سمرة بن جندب فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1476), al-Tabarani (6992), Ibn Hibban (4178), and al-Hakim (4/174).","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Samurah ibn Jundub said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Woman was created from a rib. If you try to straighten her, you will break her, so treat her gently and you will live with her.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1476) والطبراني (6992) وابن حبان (4178) والحاكم (7333)."},{"num":6300,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ فِي حَدِيثِ حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ: حَتَّى إِذَا زَاغَتِ الشَّمْسُ أَمَرَ بِالْقَصْوَاءِ، فرُحلتْ لَهُ، فَأَتَى بَطْنَ الْوَادِي، فَخَطَبَ النَّاسَ وَقَالَ: إِنَّ دِمَاءَكُمْ وَأَمْوَالَكُمْ حَرَامٌ عَلَيْكُمْ كَحُرْمَةِ يَوْمِكُمْ هَذَا فِي شَهْرِكُمْ هَذَا فِي بَلَدِكُمْ هَذَا، أَلَا كُلُّ شيءٍ مِنْ أمرِ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ تَحْتَ قدميَّ مَوْضُوعٌ، وَدِمَاءُ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ مَوْضُوعَةٌ، وَإِنَّ أوَّلَ دمٍ أضعُ مِنْ دِمَائِنَا دمُ ابْنِ رَبِيعَةَ بْنِ الْحَارِثِ -كَانَ مُسْتَرْضِعًا فِي بَنِي سَعْدٍ، فَقَتَلَتْهُ هُذَيْلٌ- وَرِبَا الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ مَوْضُوعٌ، وَأَوَّلُ رِبًا أضعُ رِبَانَا رِبا عَبَّاسِ بْنِ عبدالمطلب فَإِنَّهُ مَوْضُوعٌ كُلُّهُ، فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ فِي النِّسَاءِ، فَإِنَّكُمْ أَخَذْتُمُوهُنَّ بِأَمَانِ اللهِ، وَاسْتَحْلَلْتُمْ فُرُوجَهُنَّ بِكَلِمَةِ اللهِ، وَلَكُمْ عَلَيْهِنَّ أَنْ لَا يُوطِئْنَ فُرُشَكم أَحَدًا تَكْرَهُونَهُ، فإنْ فَعَلْنَ ذَلِكَ فَاضْرِبُوهُنَّ ضَرْبًا غَيْرَ مُبَرِّح، وَلَهُنَّ عَلَيْكُمْ رِزْقُهُنَّ وَكِسْوَتُهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ... "],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1218) من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل، عن جعفر بن محمد، عن أبيه، عن جابر في الحديث الطويل في صفة حجة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1218).","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported in the hadith of the Farewell Pilgrimage: When the sun had passed its zenith, the Prophet ﷺ ordered that al-Qaṣwāʾ be saddled for him. He came to the middle of the valley and addressed the people, saying: “Your blood and your wealth are sacred to one another, just as this day of yours is sacred, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Everything from the affairs of the pre-Islamic period is placed beneath my feet and abolished. The blood claims of the pre-Islamic period are abolished, and the first blood claim of ours that I abolish is that of the son of Rabīʿah ibn al-Ḥārith—he had been sent to be nursed among Banū Saʿd and was killed by Hudhayl. The usury of the pre-Islamic period is abolished, and the first usury of ours that I abolish is that of al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib. All of it is abolished. Fear Allah regarding women, for you have taken them under the trust of Allah and made marital relations with them lawful by the word of Allah. Your right over them is that they do not allow onto your bedding anyone whom you dislike. If they do so, then strike them in a manner that is not severe. Their right over you is that you provide them with food and clothing according to what is reasonable…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1218)."},{"num":6301,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ:  كُنْتُ أَشْرَبُ وَأَنَا حَائِضٌ، ثُمَّ أُنَاوِلُهُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَيَضَعُ فَاهُ عَلَى مَوْضِعِ فِيَّ، فَيَشْرَبُ، وَأَتَعَرَّقُ الْعَرْقَ وَأَنَا حَائِضٌ، ثُمَّ أُنَاوِلُهُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَيَضَعُ فَاهُ عَلَى مَوْضِعِ فِيَّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحيض (300) من طرق عن وكيع، عن مسعر وسفيان، عن المقدام بن شريح، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (300).","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: I would drink while menstruating, then hand it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he would place his mouth where mine had been and drink. And I would gnaw meat from a bone while menstruating, then hand it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he would place his mouth where mine had been."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word ‘irq with a silent ra’ means a bone from which most of the meat has been taken, and its plural is ‘iraq. It was also said that it means a bone that still has some meat on it. In this is the Prophet’s ﷺ gentle companionship in eating and drinking with his family."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[1515],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (300)."},{"num":6302,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: سَابَقَنِي النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَسَبَقْتُهُ، فَلَبِثْنَا حَتَّى إِذَا أَرْهَقَنِي اللَّحْمُ سَابَقَنِي فَسَبَقَنِي. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هَذِهِ بِتِلْكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2578) وابن ماجة (1979) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4691) كلهم من حديث هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2578), Ibn Majah (1979), and authenticated by Ibn Hibban (4691).","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: The Prophet ﷺ raced me, and I beat him. Then time passed until I had put on weight, and he raced me and beat me. So the Prophet ﷺ said: “This is for that.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2578) وابن ماجه (1979) وصححه ابن حبان (4691)."},{"num":6303,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: خَرَجْتُ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَعْضِ أَسْفَارِهِ وَأَنَا جَارِيَةٌ لَمْ أَحْمِلِ اللَّحْمَ، وَلَمْ أَبْدُنْ، فَقَالَ لِلنَّاسِ: تَقَدَّمُوا فَتَقَدَّمُوا، ثُمَّ قَالَ لِي: تَعَالَيْ حَتَّى أُسَابِقَكِ فَسَابَقْتُهُ فَسَبَقْتُهُ، فَسَكَتَ عَنِّي، حَتَّى إِذَا حَمَلْتُ اللَّحْمَ، وَبَدُنْتُ، وَنَسِيتُ، خَرَجْتُ مَعَهُ فِي بَعْضِ أَسْفَارِهِ، فَقَالَ لِلنَّاسِ: تَقَدَّمُوا فَتَقَدَّمُوا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: تَعَالَيْ حَتَّى أُسَابِقَكِ فَسَابَقْتُهُ، فَسَبَقَنِي، فَجَعَلَ يَضْحَكُ، وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: هَذِهِ بِتِلْكَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (26277) عن عمر أبي حفص المعيطي، قال: حدثنا هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (26277).","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: I went out with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his journeys while I was still a young girl, not carrying flesh and not heavy in body. He said to the people: “Go ahead,” so they went ahead. Then he said to me: “Come, so I may race you.” So I raced him and beat him. He said nothing to me about it until later, when I had put on flesh, gained weight, and forgotten about it. Then I went out with him on another journey, and he said to the people: “Go ahead,” so they went ahead. Then he said: “Come, so I may race you.” So I raced him and he beat me, and he began laughing, saying: “This is for that.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (26277)."},{"num":6304,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: أَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِخَزِيرَةٍ قَدْ طَبَخْتُهَا لَهُ، فَقُلْتُ لِسَوْدَةَ - وَالنَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَهَا ـ: كُلِي، فَأَبَتْ، فَقُلْتُ: لَتَأْكُلِنَّ أَوْ لَأُلَطِّخَنَّ وَجْهَكِ، فَأَبَتْ، فَوَضَعْتُ يَدِي فِي الْخَزِيرَةِ، فَطَلَيْتُ وَجْهَهَا، فَضَحِكَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَوَضَعَ بِيَدِهِ لَهَا، وَقَالَ لَهَا: الْطَخِي وَجْهَهَا، فَضَحِكَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَهَا، فَمَرَّ عُمَرُ، فَقَالَ: يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ، يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ، فَظَنَّ أَنَّهُ سَيَدْخُلُ، فَقَالَ: قُومَا فَاغْسِلَا وُجُوهَكُمَا.","قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: فَمَا زِلْتُ أَهَابُ عُمَرَ لِهَيْبَةِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (4476) وأبو بكر الشافعي في الغيلانيات (117) كلاهما من حديث حماد، عن محمد بن عمرو، عن يحيى بن عبد الرحمن بن حاطب ( ابن أبي بلتعة) أن عائشة قالت: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Ya‘la (4476) and Abu Bakr al-Shafi‘i in al-Ghaylaniyyat (117).","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: I brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some khazirah that I had cooked for him, and I said to Sawdah—while the Prophet ﷺ was between me and her—“Eat.” She refused. I said: “Either you eat, or I will smear your face.” She still refused, so I put my hand in the khazirah and smeared her face. The Prophet ﷺ laughed, then he put his hand for her and said to her: “Smear her face.” So the Prophet ﷺ laughed with her. Then ‘Umar passed by and said: “O servant of Allah, O servant of Allah!” and he thought that he would come in. So he said: “Get up and wash your faces.” ‘A’ishah said: I continued to stand in awe of ‘Umar because of the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ awe of him."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Khazirah is a food cooked from meat and flour, somewhat like a thick porridge."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (4476) وأبو بكر الشافعي في الغيلانيات (117)."},{"num":6305,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّ أَعْظَمَ الذُّنُوبِ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ رَجُلٌ تَزَوَّجَ امْرَأَةً، فَلَمَّا قَضَى حَاجَتَهُ مِنْهَا، طَلَّقَهَا، وَذَهَبَ بِمَهْرِهَا، وَرَجُلٌ اسْتَعْمَلَ رَجُلًا، فَذَهَبَ بِأُجْرَتِهِ، وَآخَرُ يَقْتُلُ دَابَّةً عَبَثًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (2743) عن أبي عمرو بن إسماعيل، ثنا أبو بكر محمد بن إسحاق الإمام، ثنا عبد الوارث بن عبد الصمد بن عبد الوارث العنبري، حدثني أبي، عن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن دينار، عن محمد بن سيرين، عن ابن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب الوصية بالنساء خيرا ومداراتهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ḥākim (2743).","chapter_en":"Chapter on enjoining good treatment of women and dealing gently with them","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the gravest sins in the sight of Allah is that a man marries a woman, then, after satisfying his desire with her, divorces her and takes away her dowry; that a man employs another man and then deprives him of his wages; and that a person kills an animal for no purpose.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (2743)."},{"num":6306,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ، عَنْ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: فِي بُضع أَحَدِكُمْ صَدَقَةٌ قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! أَيَأْتِي أَحَدُنَا شَهْوَتَهُ، وَيَكُونُ لَهُ فِيهِ أَجْرٌ. فَقَالَ: أَرَأَيْتُمْ لَوْ وَضَعَهَا فِي الحرام أَكَانَ عَلَيْهِ وزْر. فَكَذَلِكَ إِذَا وَضَعَهَا فِي الْحَلَالِ، كَانَ لَهُ أَجْرٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الزكاة (1006) عن عبد الله بن محمد بن أسماء الضُبعي، حدثنا مهدي بن ميمون، حدثنا واصل مولى أبي عُيينة، عن يحيى بن عُقيل، عن يحيى بن يعمر، عن أبي الأسود الديلي، عن أبي ذر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إن الله عزوجل جعل مواقعة أهله صدقة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim in The Book of Zakāh (1006).","chapter_en":"Chapter that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made intimacy with one’s wife an act of charity","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “And in the sexual intimacy of each one of you there is an act of charity.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah! Does one of us fulfill his desire and receive a reward for it?” He ﷺ said: “Tell me, if he were to satisfy it in what is unlawful, would he bear a sin for that? Likewise, when he satisfies it in what is lawful, he receives a reward.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1006)."},{"num":6307,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عمرو بْنِ الْعَاصِ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ، أَلَمْ أُخْبَرْ أَنَّكَ تَصُومُ النَّهَارَ وَتَقُومُ اللَّيْلَ. قُلْتُ: بَلَى يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. قَالَ: فَلاَ تَفْعَلْ، صُمْ وَأَفْطِرْ، وَقُمْ وَنَمْ، فَإِنَّ لِجَسَدِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقًّا، وَإِنَّ لِعَيْنِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقًّا، وَإِنَّ لِزَوْجِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقًّا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5199)، من طريق الأوزاعي، حدثني يحيى بن أبي كثير، حدثني أبو سلمة بن عبدالرحمن قال: حدثني عبدالله بن عمرو بن العاص فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوجة على الزوج","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5199) and Muslim (1159).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the wife’s right over the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr ibn al-‘As said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ‘Abd Allah, have I not been told that you fast by day and stand in prayer by night?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Do not do that. Fast and break your fast. Stand in prayer and sleep. For your body has a right over you, your eyes have a right over you, and your wife has a right over you.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى: (وَلَهُنَّ مِثْلُ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ) [البقرة: ٢٢٨]"],"en":["Allah Most High said: “And for them is the like of what is upon them, according to what is fair.” [al-Baqarah: 228]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5199)، ومسلم (1159)."},{"num":6308,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي جُحَيْفَةَ عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: آخَى النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْنَ سَلْمَانَ، وَأَبِي الدَّرْدَاءِ، فَزَارَ سَلْمَانُ أَبَا الدَّرْدَاءِ، فَرَأَى أُمَّ الدَّرْدَاءِ مُتَبَذِّلَةً. فَقَالَ لَهَا: مَا شَأْنُكِ؟ قَالَتْ: أَخُوكَ أَبُو الدَّرْدَاءِ لَيْسَ لَهُ حَاجَةٌ فِي الدُّنْيَا. فَجَاءَ أَبُو الدَّرْدَاءِ، فَصَنَعَ لَهُ طَعَامًا. فَقَالَ: كُلْ. قَالَ فَإِنِّي صَائِمٌ. قَالَ: مَا أَنَا بِآكِلٍ حَتَّى تَأْكُلَ. قَالَ فَأَكَلَ. فَلَمَّا كَانَ اللَّيْلُ ذَهَبَ أَبُو الدَّرْدَاءِ يَقُومُ. قَالَ: نَمْ. فَنَامَ، ثُمَّ ذَهَبَ يَقُومُ. فَقَالَ: نَمْ. فَلَمَّا كَانَ مِنْ آخِرِ اللَّيْلِ قَالَ سَلْمَانُ: قُمِ الْآنَ. فَصَلَّيَا، فَقَالَ لَهُ سَلْمَانُ: إِنَّ لِرَبِّكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقًّا، وَلِنَفْسِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقًّا، وَلأَهْلِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقًّا، فَأَعْطِ كُلَّ ذِي حَقٍّ حَقَّهُ. فَأَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَذَكَرَ ذَلِكَ لَهُ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: صَدَقَ سَلْمَانُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الصوم (1968)، عن محمد بن بشّار، حدّثنا جعفر بن عون، حدّثنا أبو العُميس، عن عَون بن أبي جحيفة، عن أبيه، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوجة على الزوج","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1968).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the wife’s right over the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Juhayfah said: The Prophet ﷺ made Salman and Abu al-Darda’ brothers. Salman visited Abu al-Darda’ and saw Umm al-Darda’ in worn clothing, so he said to her: What is the matter with you? She said: Your brother Abu al-Darda’ has no interest in worldly things. Then Abu al-Darda’ came and prepared food for him. Abu al-Darda’ said: Eat, for I am fasting. Salman said: I will not eat until you eat. So Abu al-Darda’ ate. When night came, Abu al-Darda’ got up to pray, but Salman said: Sleep. So he slept. Then he got up again, and Salman said: Sleep. Then at the end of the night Salman said: Now get up. So they prayed. Then Salman said to him: Your Lord has a right over you, your self has a right over you, and your family has a right over you, so give each possessor of a right his right. Then Abu al-Darda’ came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Salman has spoken the truth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[15271],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1968)."},{"num":6309,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ زَمْعَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لاَ يَجْلِدُ أَحَدُكُمُ امْرَأَتَهُ جَلْدَ الْعَبْدِ، ثُمَّ يُجَامِعُهَا فِي آخِرِ الْيَوْمِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5204)، ومسلم في الجنة وصفة نعيمها وأهلها (2855) من طريق هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن زمعة، فذكره، واللفظ للبخاري، هو عند مسلم بسياق أطول.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوجة على الزوج","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5204) and Muslim (2855), with the wording from al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"Chapter on the wife’s right over the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn Zam‘ah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Let none of you flog his wife like the flogging of a slave and then have relations with her at the end of the day.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5204)، ومسلم (2855)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":6310,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حَكِيمِ بْنِ مُعَاوِيَةَ الْقُشَيْرِيِّ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! مَا حَقُّ زَوْجَةِ أَحَدِنَا عَلَيْهِ؟ قَالَ أَنْ تُطْعِمَهَا إِذَا طَعِمْتَ، وَتَكْسُوَهَا إِذَا اكْتَسَيْتَ، - أَوِ اكْتَسَبْتَ - وَلاَ تَضْرِبِ الْوَجْهَ، وَلاَ تُقَبِّحْ، وَلاَ تَهْجُرْ إِلاَّ فِي الْبَيْتِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2142) وابن ماجة (1850) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4175) والحاكم (2764) كلهم من طريق أبي قزعة عن حكيم بن معاوية، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوجة على الزوج","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2142), Ibn Majah (1850), authenticated by Ibn Hibban (4175), and al-Hakim (2764).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the wife’s right over the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Hakim ibn Mu‘awiyah al-Qushayri reported from his father that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of one of our wives over him? He said: “That you feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, do not revile her, and do not forsake her except within the house.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2142) وابن ماجه (1850) وصححه ابن حبان (4175) والحاكم (2764)."},{"num":6311,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ:  جَاءَتْ هِنْدٌ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَاللهِ مَا كَانَ عَلَى ظَهْرِ الْأَرْضِ أَهْلُ خِبَاءٍ أَحَبَّ إِلَيَّ مِنْ أَنْ يُذِلَّهُمُ اللهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ خِبَائِكَ، وَمَا عَلَى ظَهْرِ الْأَرْضِ أَهْلُ خِبَاءٍ أَحَبَّ إِلَيَّ مِنْ أَنْ يُعِزَّهُمُ اللهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ خِبَائِكَ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: وَأَيْضًا، وَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ. ثُمَّ قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ أَبَا سُفْيَانَ رَجُلٌ مُمْسِكٌ، فَهَلْ عَلَيَّ حَرَجٌ أَنْ أُنْفِقَ عَلَى عِيَالِهِ مِنْ مَالِهِ بِغَيْرِ إِذْنِهِ؟ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا حَرَجَ عَلَيْكِ أَنْ تُنْفِقِي عَلَيْهِمْ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصـار (3825)، ومسلم في الأقضيــة (1714: 8) كلاهما من حديث الزهري، عن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوجة على الزوج","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (3825) and Muslim (8:1714), with this wording from Muslim. Al-Bukhari’s wording is close to it.","chapter_en":"Chapter on the wife’s right over the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: Hind bint ‘Utbah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, there was no household on the face of the earth more beloved to me that Allah should disgrace than your household, and now there is no household on the face of the earth more beloved to me that Allah should honor than your household. The Prophet ﷺ said: “And also, by the One in whose hand is my soul.” Then she said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man. Is there any sin upon me if I spend on his dependents from his wealth without his permission? The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no sin upon you to spend on them in a fair manner.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3825)، ومسلم (1714: 8) والسياق لمسلم، وسياق البخاري قريب منه."},{"num":6312,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَكْمَلُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِيمَانًا أَحْسَنُهُمْ خُلُقًا، وَخِيَارُكُمْ خِيَارُكُمْ لِنِسَائِهِمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1162)، وأبو داود (4682) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4176) والحاكم (1) كلهم من طريق محمد بن عمرو، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة فذكر الحديث واللفظ للترمذي وابن حبان.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في قوله: خياركم خياركم لأهله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (1162), Abu Dawud (4682), authenticated by Ibn Hibban (4176), and al-Hakim (1).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the saying: the best of you are the best to their families","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most complete of the believers in faith are those best in character, and the best of you are the best of you to their women.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1162)، وأبو داود (4682) وصححه ابن حبان (4176) والحاكم (1)."},{"num":6313,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: خَيْرُكُمْ خَيْرُكُمْ لأَهْلِهِ، وَأَنَا خَيْرُكُمْ لأَهْلِي، وَإِذَا مَاتَ صَاحِبُكُمْ فَدَعُوهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3895) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4177) وأبو نعيم في الحلية (1709) كلهم من حديث محمد بن يوسف، عن الثوري، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في قوله: خياركم خياركم لأهله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3895), authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (4177), and narrated by Abū Nuʿaym in al-Ḥilyah (7/138).","chapter_en":"Chapter on the saying: the best of you are the best to their families","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you are those who are best to their families, and I am the best of you to my family. When your companion dies, leave him alone.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3895)، وصححه ابن حبان (4177)، وأبو نعيم في الحلية (1709)."},{"num":6314,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أُمِّ سَلَمَةَ، أَخْبَرَتْهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَلَفَ لاَ يَدْخُلُ عَلَى بَعْضِ أَهْلِهِ شَهْرًا، فَلَمَّا مَضَى تِسْعَةٌ وَعِشْرُونَ يَوْمًا غَدَا عَلَيْهِنَّ أَوْ رَاحَ، فَقِيلَ لَهُ: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ، حَلَفْتَ أَنْ لاَ تَدْخُلَ عَلَيْهِنَّ شَهْرًا؟ قَالَ: إِنَّ الشَّهْرَ يَكُونُ تِسْعَةً وَعِشْرِينَ يَوْمًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5202)، ومسلم في الصيام (25:1085) من طريق ابن جريج قال: أخبرني يحيى بن عبد الله بن صيفيّ، أن عكرمة بن عبد الرحمن بن الحارث أخبره، أن أم سلمة أخبرته، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5202) and Muslim (25:1085).","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Salamah reported that the Prophet ﷺ swore that he would not enter upon some of his wives for one month. Then when twenty-nine days had passed, he came to them in the morning or evening. It was said to him: O Prophet of Allah, you swore that you would not enter upon them for a month. He said: “The month may be twenty-nine days.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى: ﴿وَاللَّاتِي تَخَافُونَ نُشُوزَهُنَّ فَعِظُوهُنَّ وَاهْجُرُوهُنَّ فِي الْمَضَاجِعِ وَاضْرِبُوهُنَّ فَإِنْ أَطَعْنَكُمْ فَلَا تَبْغُوا عَلَيْهِنَّ سَبِيلًا إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيًّا كَبِيرًا﴾ [النساء: ٣٤]"],"en":["Allah Most High said: “As for those women whose disobedience you fear, admonish them, leave them in the beds, and strike them. But if they obey you, then seek no way against them. Indeed, Allah is Most High, Most Great.” [Surat al-Nisa’: 34]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[4326,6645],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5202)، ومسلم (25:1085)."},{"num":6315,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِذَا دَعَا الرَّجُلُ امْرَأَتَهُ إِلَى فِرَاشِهِ، فَأَبَتْ أَنْ تَجِيءَ لَعَنَتْهَا الْمَلاَئِكَةُ حَتَّى تُصْبِحَ.","وفي رواية: إذا باتت المرأة مهاجرةً فراش زوجها، لعنتها الملائكة حتى ترجع."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5193)، ومسلم في النكاح (12:1436) كلاهما عن سليمان الأعمش، عن أبي حازم، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره، واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5193) and Muslim (12:1436), with the wording from al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If a man calls his wife to his bed and she refuses to come, the angels curse her until morning.” In another narration: “If a woman spends the night forsaking her husband’s bed, the angels curse her until she returns.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5193)، ومسلم (12:1436)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":6316,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لاَ يَحِلُّ لِلْمَرْأَةِ أَنْ تَصُومَ وَزَوْجُهَا شَاهِدٌ إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِهِ، وَلاَ تَأْذَنَ فِي بَيْتِهِ إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِهِ، وَمَا أَنْفَقَتْ مِنْ نَفَقَةٍ عَنْ غَيْرِ أَمْرِهِ فَإِنَّهُ يُؤَدَّى إِلَيْهِ شَطْرُهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5195)، من طريق أبي الزناد، عن الأعرج، عن أبي هريرة، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5195) and Muslim (1026).","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a woman to fast while her husband is present except with his permission, and she must not allow anyone into his house except with his permission. Whatever she spends without his instruction, half of its reward goes to him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5195)، ومسلم (1026)."},{"num":6317,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن طلق بن عَلِيٍّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِذَا الرَّجُلُ دَعَا زَوْجَتَهُ لِحَاجَتِهِ فَلْتَأْتِهِ، وَإِنْ كَانَتْ عَلَى التَّنُّورِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1160) وابن حبان في صحيحه (4165) والبيهقي (14710) كلهم من طريق ملازم بن عمرو، حدثنا عبد الله بن بدر، عن قيس بن طلق، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (1160), who graded it Hasan, Ibn Hibban in his Sahih (4165), and al-Bayhaqi (7/294).","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Talq ibn ‘Ali said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man calls his wife for his need, she should come to him, even if she is at the oven.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1160)، وحسنه، وابن حبان في صحيحه (4165)، والبيهقي (14710)."},{"num":6318,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ أَرْقَمَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: إِذَا دَعَا الرَّجُلُ امْرَأَتَهُ فَلْتُجِبْ، وَإِنْ كَانَتْ عَلَى ظَهْرِ قَتْبٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار- كشف الأستار (1472) والطبراني في المعجم الأوسط (7429) كلاهما من حديث محمد بن سواء، ثنا سعيد، عن قتادة، عن القاسم الشيباني، عن زيد بن أرقم، فذكره، ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1472) and al-Tabarani in al-Mu‘jam al-Awsat (7429).","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Arqam reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man calls his wife, she should respond, even if she is on the back of a saddle.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1472)، والطبراني في المعجم الأوسط (7429)."},{"num":6319,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْحُصَيْنِ بْنِ مِحْصَنٍ، أَنَّ عَمَّةً لَهُ أَتَتِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَاجَةٍ، فَفَرَغَتْ مِنْ حَاجَتِهَا، فَقَالَ لَهَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَذَاتُ زَوْجٍ أَنْتِ؟ قَالَتْ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: كَيْفَ أَنْتِ لَهُ؟ قَالَتْ: مَا آلُوهُ إِلَّا مَا عَجَزْتُ عَنْهُ، قَالَ: فَانْظُرِي أَيْنَ أَنْتِ مِنْهُ، فَإِنَّمَا هُوَ جَنَّتُكِ وَنَارُكِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (19003) والطبراني في الكبير (25/183) والأوسط (532) والحاكم (2769) وعنه البيهقي (7/291) والنسائي في الكبرى (8963) كلهم من حديث يحيى بن سعيد الأنصاري، عن بُشير بن يسار، عن الحصين بن محصن فذكره. وقال الحاكم: صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ahmad (19003), al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (25/183), al-Awsat (532), and al-Hakim (3/189).","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Husayn ibn Mihsan reported that an aunt of his came to the Prophet ﷺ regarding a need. When she had finished her need, the Prophet ﷺ said to her: “Do you have a husband?” She said: Yes. He said: “How are you with him?” She said: I do not fail him except in what I am unable to do. He said: “Then look at where you stand with respect to him, for he is your Paradise and your Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (19003)، والطبراني في الكبير (25/183)، والأوسط (532)، والحاكم (3/189)."},{"num":6320,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَوْ كُنْتُ آمِرًا أَحَدًا أَنْ يَسْجُدَ لأَحَدٍ، لأَمَرْتُ الْمَرْأَةَ أَنْ تَسْجُدَ لِزَوْجِهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1159) والبيهقي (14704) وابن أبي الدنيا في العيال (534) كلهم من حديث النضر بن شميل، أنا محمد بن عمرو، عن أبي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة فذكره. وإسناده حسن من أجل محمد بن عمرو وهو ابن علقمة الليثي فإنه حسن الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (1159), al-Bayhaqi (7/291), and Ibn Abi al-Dunya in al-‘Iyal (534).","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12572],"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1159)، والبيهقي (14704)، وابن أبي الدنيا في العيال (534)."},{"num":6321,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سراقة بن مَالِكٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَوْ كُنْتُ آمِرًا أَحَدًا أَنْ يَسْجُدَ لِأَحَدٍ لَأَمَرْتُ الْمَرْأَةَ أَنْ تَسْجُدَ لِزَوْجِهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (6590) وابن أبي الدنيا في العيال (537) موسوعة ابن أبي الدنيا – كلاهما من حديث وهب بن جرير بن حازم، حدثنا موسى بن عُلّى، عن أبيه، عن سراقة بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (7/152) and Ibn Abi al-Dunya in al-‘Iyal (537).","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Suraqah ibn Malik said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12571],"tks":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (6590)، وابن أبي الدنيا في العيال (537)."},{"num":6322,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَوْ أَمَرْتُ أَحَدًا أَنْ يَسْجُدَ لأَحَدٍ لأَمَرْتُ الْمَرْأَةَ أَنْ تَسْجُدَ لِزَوْجِهَا، وَلَوْ أَنَّ رَجُلاً أَمَرَ امْرَأَةً أَنْ تَنْقُلَ مِنْ جَبَلٍ أَحْمَرَ إِلَى جَبَلٍ أَسْوَدَ، وَمِنْ جَبَلٍ أَسْوَدَ إِلَى جَبَلٍ أَحْمَرَ - لَكَانَ نَوْلُهَا أَنْ تَفْعَلَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجة (1852) عن ابن أبي شيبة وهو في مصنفه (4/206) وأحمد (24471) كلهم من طريق عفان، قال: حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن علي بن زيد، عن سعيد بن المسيب، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Majah (1852), Ibn Abi Shaybah in his Musannaf (4/206), and Ahmad (24471).","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband. And if a man were to command his wife to move from a red mountain to a black mountain, and from a black mountain to a red mountain, it would be her duty to do so.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (1852)، وابن أبي شيبة في مصنفه (17134)، وأحمد (24471)."},{"num":6323,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: ثَلاَثَةٌ لاَ تَرْتَفِعُ صَلاَتُهُمْ فَوْقَ رُءُوسِهِمْ شِبْرًا: رَجُلٌ أَمَّ قَوْمًا وَهُمْ لَهُ كَارِهُونَ، وَامْرَأَةٌ بَاتَتْ وَزَوْجُهَا عَلَيْهَا سَاخِطٌ، وَأَخَوَانِ مُتَصَارِمَانِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (971) قال: حدثنا محمد بن عمر بن هيَّاج، قال: حدثنا يحيى بن عبدالرحمن الأرحبي، قال: حدثنا عبيدة بن الأسود، عن القاسم بن الوليد، عن المنهال بن عمرو، عن سعيد بن جبير، عن ابن عباس فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حق الزوج على الزوجة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Majah (971).","chapter_en":"The husband’s right over his wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three persons’ prayer does not rise even a handspan above their heads: a man who leads people in prayer while they dislike him, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and two brothers who are in estrangement with one another.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[2254],"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (971)."},{"num":6324,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرٍو قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يَنْظُرُ اللَّهُ إِلَى امْرَأَةٍ لَا تَشْكَرُ لِزَوْجِهَا، وَهِيَ لَا تَسْتَغْنِي عَنْهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (9086) عن عمرو بن منصور، قال: حدثنا محمد بن محبوب، قال: حدثنا سَرَّار بن مجشِّر بن قبيصة البصري-ثقة-، عن سعيد بن أبي عروبة، عن قتادة، عن سعيد بن المسيب، عن عبدالله بن عمرو، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب شكر المرأة لزوجها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasa’i in al-Kubra (9086).","chapter_en":"The recommendation that a woman be grateful to her husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr ibn al-‘As said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah does not look at a woman who is ungrateful to her husband while she cannot do without him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (9086)."},{"num":6325,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: خَيْرُ نِسَاءٍ رَكِبْنَ الإِبِلَ صَالِحُو نِسَاءِ قُرَيْشٍ، أَحْنَاهُ عَلَى وَلَدٍ فِي صِغَرِهِ، وَأَرْعَاهُ عَلَى زَوْجٍ فِي ذَاتِ يَدِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5082) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (200:2527) كلاهما من طريق أبي الزناد، عن الأعرج، عن أبي هريرة فذكره،","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رعاية المرأة لزوجها وولدها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5082) and Muslim (200:2527), with the wording from al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"A woman’s care for her husband and her child","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The best women who rode camels are the righteous women of Quraysh: the most tender toward a child in his young age, and the most careful in safeguarding her husband’s property.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6223],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5082)، ومسلم (200:2527)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":6326,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَسْمَاءَ بِنْتِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَتْ: تَزَوَّجَنِي الزُّبَيْرُ، وَمَا لَهُ فِي الأَرْضِ مِنْ مَالٍ، وَلاَ مَمْلُوكٍ، وَلاَ شَىْءٍ غَيْرَ نَاضِحٍ، وَغَيْرَ فَرَسِهِ، فَكُنْتُ أَعْلِفُ فَرَسَهُ، وَأَسْتَقِي الْمَاءَ، وَأَخْرِزُ غَرْبَهُ وَأَعْجِنُ، وَلَمْ أَكُنْ أُحْسِنُ أَخْبِزُ، وَكَانَ يَخْبِزُ جَارَاتٌ لِي مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، وَكُنَّ نِسْوَةَ صِدْقٍ، وَكُنْتُ أَنْقُلُ النَّوَى مِنْ أَرْضِ الزُّبَيْرِ الَّتِي أَقْطَعَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى رَأْسِي، وَهْىَ مِنِّي عَلَى ثُلُثَىْ فَرْسَخٍ، فَجِئْتُ يَوْمًا وَالنَّوَى عَلَى رَأْسِي، فَلَقِيتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَعَهُ نَفَرٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، فَدَعَانِي ثُمَّ قَالَ: إِخْ إِخْ. لِيَحْمِلَنِي خَلْفَهُ، فَاسْتَحْيَيْتُ أَنْ أَسِيرَ مَعَ الرِّجَالِ، وَذَكَرْتُ الزُّبَيْرَ وَغَيْرَتَهُ، وَكَانَ أَغْيَرَ النَّاسِ، فَعَرَفَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنِّي قَدِ اسْتَحْيَيْتُ فَمَضَى، فَجِئْتُ الزُّبَيْرَ فَقُلْتُ: لَقِيَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَعَلَى رَأْسِي النَّوَى، وَمَعَهُ نَفَرٌ مِنْ أَصْحَابِهِ، فَأَنَاخَ لأَرْكَبَ، فَاسْتَحْيَيْتُ مِنْهُ وَعَرَفْتُ غَيْرَتَكَ. فَقَالَ: وَاللَّهِ لَحَمْلُكِ النَّوَى كَانَ أَشَدَّ عَلَىَّ مِنْ رُكُوبِكِ مَعَهُ. قَالَتْ: حَتَّى أَرْسَلَ إِلَىَّ أَبُو بَكْرٍ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ بِخَادِمٍ يَكْفِينِي سِيَاسَةَ الْفَرَسِ، فَكَأَنَّمَا أَعْتَقَنِي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5224)، ومسلم في السلام (2182) كلاهما من حديث أبي أسامة، حدّثنا هشام، قال: أخبرني أبي، عن أسماء بنت أبي بكر رضي الله عنهما، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رعاية المرأة لزوجها وولدها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5224) and Muslim (2182).","chapter_en":"A woman’s care for her husband and her child","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Asma’ bint Abi Bakr said: Al-Zubayr married me when he had no wealth on earth, no servant, and nothing except a camel for drawing water and his horse. So I used to feed his horse, fetch water, stitch his water-skin, and knead dough. I was not good at baking bread, and some neighbor women from the Ansar used to bake for me, and they were truthful women. I used to carry date-stones on my head from the land of al-Zubayr that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had granted him, and it was about two-thirds of a farsakh away. One day I came carrying date-stones on my head, and I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group of the Ansar. He called me and then said, “Ikh, ikh,” to make me ride behind him. But I felt shy to go with the men, and I remembered al-Zubayr and his jealousy, and he was the most jealous of people. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ realized that I was shy and continued on. Then I came to al-Zubayr and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me while I had date-stones on my head, and he had some of his Companions with him, and he made his camel kneel so I could ride, but I felt shy before him and remembered your jealousy. He said: By Allah, your carrying date-stones on your head was harder on me than your riding with him. She said: Then later Abu Bakr sent me a servant who relieved me of tending the horse, and it was as if he had freed me."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5224)، ومسلم (2182)."},{"num":6327,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عليّ، أَنَّ فَاطِمَةَ ـ عَلَيْهِمَا السَّلاَمُ ـ أَتَتِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَشْكُو إِلَيْهِ مَا تَلْقَى فِي يَدِهَا مِنَ الرَّحَى، وَبَلَغَهَا أَنَّهُ جَاءَهُ رَقِيقٌ، فَلَمْ تُصَادِفْهُ، فَذَكَرَتْ ذَلِكَ لِعَائِشَةَ، فَلَمَّا جَاءَ أَخْبَرَتْهُ عَائِشَةُ، ـ قَالَ: ـ فَجَاءَنَا وَقَدْ أَخَذْنَا مَضَاجِعَنَا، فَذَهَبْنَا نَقُومُ، فَقَالَ: عَلَى مَكَانِكُمَا. فَجَاءَ فَقَعَدَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَهَا، حَتَّى وَجَدْتُ بَرْدَ قَدَمَيْهِ عَلَى بَطْنِي، فَقَالَ: أَلاَ أَدُلُّكُمَا عَلَى خَيْرٍ مِمَّا سَأَلْتُمَا، إِذَا أَخَذْتُمَا مَضَاجِعَكُمَا، ـ أَوْ أَوَيْتُمَا إِلَى فِرَاشِكُمَا، ـ فَسَبِّحَا ثَلاَثًا وَثَلاَثِينَ، وَاحْمَدَا ثَلاَثًا وَثَلاَثِينَ، وَكَبِّرَا أَرْبَعًا وَثَلاَثِينَ، فَهْوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمَا مِنْ خَادِمٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النفقات ( 5361) ومسلم في الذكر والدعاء (2727) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، قال: حدثني الحكم، عن ابن أبي ليلى، حدّثنا علي، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رعاية المرأة لزوجها وولدها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5361) and Muslim (2727).","chapter_en":"A woman’s care for her husband and her child","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Ali ibn Abi Talib reported that Fatimah came to the Prophet ﷺ complaining about what her hands suffered from grinding with the millstone. News had reached her that some captives had come to him, but she did not find him, so she mentioned it to ‘A’ishah. When he came, ‘A’ishah informed him. He said: So he came to us after we had gone to our beds, and we started to get up, but he said: “Stay where you are.” Then he came and sat between me and her until I felt the coolness of his feet on my stomach. Then he said: “Shall I not direct you to something better than what you asked for? When you go to your beds, or lie down in your bed, say ‘Subhan Allah’ thirty-three times, ‘Alhamdulillah’ thirty-three times, and ‘Allahu Akbar’ thirty-four times. That is better for you than a servant.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5361)، ومسلم (2727)."},{"num":6328,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: كُلُّكُمْ رَاعٍ، وَكُلُّكُمْ مَسْئُولٌ عَنْ رَعِيَّتِهِ، وَالأَمِيرُ رَاعٍ، وَالرَّجُلُ رَاعٍ عَلَى أَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ، وَالْمَرْأَةُ رَاعِيَةٌ عَلَى بَيْتِ زَوْجِهَا وَوَلَدِهِ، فَكُلُّكُمْ رَاعٍ وَكُلُّكُمْ مَسْئُولٌ عَنْ رَعِيَّتِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5200) من طريق موسى بن عُقبة، ومسلم في الإمارة (20:1829) من طريق الليث – كلاهما عن نافع، عن ابن عمر.وزاد مسلم: والعبدُ راعٍ على مال سيّده، وهو مسؤول عنه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رعاية المرأة لزوجها وولدها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5200) and Muslim (20:1829).","chapter_en":"A woman’s care for her husband and her child","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible for his flock. The ruler is a shepherd. A man is a shepherd over the people of his household. A woman is a shepherd over the house of her husband and his child. So each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible for his flock.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5200)، ومسلم (20:1829)."},{"num":6329,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، رضي الله عنه قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مِنْ بَنِي آدَمَ سَيِّدٌ، فَالرَّجُلُ سَيِّدُ أَهْلِهِ، وَالْمَرْأَةُ سَيِّدَةُ بَيْتِهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابنُ السنّي في عمل اليوم والليلة (389)، وابنُ عدي في الكامل (1013)-ترجمة عبد الله بن وهب المصري- كلاهما من طرقٍ عن أحمد بن عمرو بن السرح، حدثنا ابنُ وهب، أخبرني عمرو بن الحارث، عن أبي يونس (واسمه سليم بن جبير مولى أبي هريرة)، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب رعاية المرأة لزوجها وولدها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn al-Sunni in ‘Amal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah (389), and Ibn ‘Adi in al-Kamil (4/1520).","chapter_en":"A woman’s care for her husband and her child","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every soul from the children of Adam is a master. So the man is the master of his family, and the woman is the lady of her house.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن السني في عمل اليوم والليلة (389)، وابن عدي في الكامل (1013)."},{"num":6330,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنِّي لأَعْلَمُ إِذَا كُنْتِ عَنِّي رَاضِيَةً، وَإِذَا كُنْتِ عَلَىَّ غَضْبَى. قَالَتْ: فَقُلْتُ: مِنْ أَيْنَ تَعْرِفُ ذَلِكَ؟ فَقَالَ: أَمَّا إِذَا كُنْتِ عَنِّي رَاضِيَةً فَإِنَّكِ تَقُولِينَ: لاَ وَرَبِّ مُحَمَّدٍ، وَإِذَا كُنْتِ غَضْبَى قُلْتِ: لاَ وَرَبِّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ. قَالَتْ: قُلْتُ: أَجَلْ وَاللَّهِ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، مَا أَهْجُرُ إِلاَّ اسْمَكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5228)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (80:2439) كلاهما من طريق أبي أسامة، عن هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب غضب المرأة على زوجها وهجرها له","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5228) and Muslim (80:2439).","chapter_en":"A wife’s anger with her husband and her forsaking him","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “I certainly know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry with me.” She said: I said: How do you know that? He said: “When you are pleased with me, you say: ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad,’ and when you are angry, you say: ‘No, by the Lord of Ibrahim.’” She said: I replied: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not forsake except your name."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The anger meant here is the jealousy that affected the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. As for anger in the sense of hatred, that cannot be imagined from ‘A’ishah toward the Prophet ﷺ, because that would be a grave matter and ruinous to deeds. As for someone other than the Prophet ﷺ, that is possible."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10391],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5228)، ومسلم (80 :2439)."},{"num":6331,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ:  تَزَوَّجْتُ امْرَأَةً. فَقَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هَلْ تَزَوَّجْتَ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: أَبِكْرًا أَمْ ثَيِّبًا؟ قُلْتُ: ثَيِّبًا. قَالَ: فَأَيْنَ أَنْتَ مِنَ الْعَذَارَى وَلِعَابِهَا؟","قَالَ شُعْبَةُ: فَذَكَرْتُهُ لِعَمْرِو بْنِ دِينَارٍ. فَقَالَ: قَدْ سَمِعْتَهُ مِنْ جَابِرٍ. وَإِنَّمَا قَالَ: فَهَلَّا جَارِيَةً تُلَاعِبُهَا وَتُلَاعِبُكَ؟."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5080)، ومسلم في الرضاع (55:1466) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، حدّثنا محارب قال: سمعت جابر بن عبد الله يقول: فذكره","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ملاعبة الزوجة ومضاحكتها والانبساط إليها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5080) and Muslim (55:715), and the wording is that of Muslim.","chapter_en":"Playing with one’s wife, joking with her, and being relaxed and cheerful with her","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: I married a woman, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Have you married?” I said: Yes. He said: “A virgin or a previously married woman?” I said: A previously married woman. He said: “Then why not a young virgin, so you could play with her and she could play with you?”","Shu‘bah said: I mentioned it to ‘Amr ibn Dinar, and he said: I heard it from Jabir. Rather, he said: “Why not a young girl whom you could amuse and who could amuse you?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6199,6202],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5080)، ومسلم (55 :715)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":6332,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: كُنَّا نَتَّقِي الْكَلاَمَ وَالاِنْبِسَاطَ إِلَى نِسَائِنَا عَلَى عَهْدِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ هَيْبَةَ أَنْ يُنْزَلَ فِينَا شيء، فَلَمَّا تُوُفِّيَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَكَلَّمْنَا وَانْبَسَطْنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5187) عن أبي نعيم، حدثنا سفيان، عن عبد الله بن دينار، عن ابن عمر رضي الله عنهما. فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ملاعبة الزوجة ومضاحكتها والانبساط إليها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5187).","chapter_en":"Playing with one’s wife, joking with her, and being relaxed and cheerful with her","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar said: During the lifetime of the Prophet ﷺ, we used to avoid speaking freely and being relaxed with our wives out of fear that something might be revealed concerning us. But when the Prophet ﷺ passed away, we spoke more openly and became relaxed."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His saying, “When he passed away…” Ibn Hajar said: This indicates that what they had been leaving off was originally permissible under the basic presumption of permissibility. They had feared that a prohibition might be revealed concerning it. After the Prophet ﷺ passed away, they felt safe and did it, holding to the original presumption of permissibility."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5187)."},{"num":6333,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، أَنَّ امْرَأَةً، مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ زَوَّجَتِ ابْنَتَهَا، فَتَمَعَّطَ شَعَرُ رَأْسِهَا، فَجَاءَتْ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَذَكَرَتْ ذَلِكَ لَهُ، فَقَالَتْ: إِنَّ زَوْجَهَا أَمَرَنِي أَنْ أَصِلَ فِي شَعَرِهَا. فَقَالَ: لاَ، إِنَّهُ قَدْ لُعِنَ الْمُوصِلاَتُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5205)، ومسلم في اللباس والزينة (118:2123) كلاهما من طريق إبراهيم بن نافع، أخبرني الحسن بن مسلم ابن ينّاق، عن صفية بنت شيبة، عن عائشة، فذكرته. واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب النهي عن وصل شعر المرأة، وإن أمر به زوجها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5205) and Muslim (118:2123), with the wording from al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"The prohibition of adding hair to a woman’s hair, even if her husband commands it","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah reported that a woman from the Ansar married off her daughter, and the hair of her head fell out. So she came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and said: Her husband has ordered me to add hair to hers. He said: “No. Indeed, those who add hair have been cursed.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5205)، ومسلم (118 :2123)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":6334,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لاَ يَطْرُقُ أَهْلَهُ، كَانَ لاَ يَدْخُلُ إِلاَّ غُدْوَةً أَوْ عَشِيَّةً."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الحج (1800)، ومسلم في الإمارة (1928-180) كلاهما من حديث همام بن يحيى، حدثنا إسحاق بن عبد الله بن أبي طلحة، عن أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب النهي أن يطرق الرجل أهله ليلاً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (1800) and Muslim (180:1928).","chapter_en":"The prohibition of a man arriving suddenly to his family at night","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas said: The Prophet ﷺ would not come suddenly upon his family at night. He would only enter in the morning or in the evening."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1800)، ومسلم (180-1928)."},{"num":6335,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ:  كُنَّا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي غَزَاةٍ، فَلَمَّا قَدِمْنَا الْمَدِينَةَ ذَهَبْنَا لِنَدْخُلَ، فَقَالَ: أَمْهِلُوا حَتَّى نَدْخُلَ لَيْلًا (أَيْ عِشَاءً) كَيْ تَمْتَشِطَ الشَّعِثَةُ، وَتَسْتَحِدَّ الْمُغِيبَةُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5079)، ومسلم في الإمارة (1928: 181) كلاهما من طريق هُشيم، حدثنا سيّار، عن الشعبي، عن جابر، فذكره، واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب النهي أن يطرق الرجل أهله ليلاً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5079) and Muslim (181:1928), with the wording from Muslim.","chapter_en":"The prohibition of a man arriving suddenly to his family at night","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an expedition. When we arrived at Madinah and were about to enter, he said: “Wait until we enter at night — meaning in the evening — so that the woman with disheveled hair may comb herself, and the woman whose husband has been absent may remove her unwanted hair.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In a narration in al-Bukhari (5244): “If one of you has been away for a long time, he should not come to his family suddenly at night.”","And in a narration in Abu Dawud (2777) by another chain: “The best way for a man to enter upon his family when returning from a journey is at the beginning of the night.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5079)، ومسلم (1928: 181)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":6336,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: كان النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم يكره أن يأتي الرجل أهله طروقاً. وزاد في رواية: يتخوّنهم أو يلتمِسُ عثراتهم."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5243)، ومسلم في الإمارة (185:1928) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، حدثنا محارب بن دثار، قال: سمعت جابر بن عبد الله، فذكره. واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب النهي أن يطرق الرجل أهله ليلاً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5243) and Muslim (185:1928), with the wording from al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"The prohibition of a man arriving suddenly to his family at night","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: The Prophet ﷺ disliked that a man should come upon his family suddenly at night. And in another narration there is an addition: seeking to suspect them of betrayal or looking for their faults."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His saying, “suspecting them…” means searching for betrayal and whether she is chaste or not. But the basic assumption regarding a believing woman is that she is chaste, so it is not permissible to spy concerning her chastity. This is one of the wisdoms behind the prohibition of entering upon women suddenly at night."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5243)، ومسلم (185 :1928)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":6337,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: كُنَّا فِي غَزْوَةٍ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لا تَطْرُقُوا النِّسَاءَ، وَأَرْسِلَ مَنْ يُؤَذِّنُ النَّاسَ أَنَّهُمْ قَادِمُونَ الْغَدَاةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن خزيمة كما في إتحاف المهرة (9/249)، وأبو عوانة في مسنده (7536)، والبيهقي في الكبرى (18583) كلهم من طريق ابن وهب، قال: حدثني عمر بن محمد بن زيد، عن نافع، عن عبد الله بن عمر قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النهي أن يطرق الرجل أهله ليلاً","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah as cited in Ithaf al-Maharah (9/249), Abu ‘Awanah (7536), and al-Bayhaqi (9/174).","chapter_en":"The prohibition of a man arriving suddenly to his family at night","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar said: We were on an expedition, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not come suddenly upon the women.” And he sent someone to announce to the people that they would be arriving the next morning."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن خزيمة كما في إتحاف المهرة (9/249)، وأبو عوانة (7536)، والبيهقي (18583)."},{"num":6338,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : إِنِّي رَأَيْتُ الْجَنَّةَ فَتَنَاوَلْتُ مِنْهَا عُنْقُودًا، وَلَوْ أَخَذْتُهُ لأَكَلْتُمْ مِنْهُ مَا بَقِيَتِ الدُّنْيَا، وَرَأَيْتُ النَّارَ فَلَمْ أَرَ كَالْيَوْمِ مَنْظَرًا قظ أَفْظَعَ وَرَأَيْتُ أكثرها النِّسَاءَ قَالُوا: لِمَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: لِكُفْرِهِنَّ قِيلَ: أَيَكْفُرْنَ بِاللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: وَيَكْفُرْنَ الْعَشِيرَ، وَيَكْفُرْنَ الإِحْسَانَ، لَوْ أَحْسَنْتَ إِلَيْهَا الدَّهْرَ كُلَّهُ، ثُمَّ رَأَتْ مِنْكَ شَيْئًا، قَالَتْ: مَا رَأَيْتُ مِنْكَ خَيْرًا قَطُّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في صلاة الكسوف (2) عن زيد بن أسلم، عن عطاء بن يسار، عن عبد الله بن عباس، فذكره بتمامه في صلاة الكسوف.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب نهي النساء عن كفر العشير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (2), al-Bukhārī (5197), and Muslim (907).","chapter_en":"Warning women against ingratitude toward the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw Paradise and reached for a cluster from it. Had I taken it, you would have continued eating from it for as long as this world remained. I also saw the Fire, and I have never seen a sight more terrifying than it today, and I saw that most of its inhabitants were women.” They asked: “Why, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Because of their ingratitude.” It was asked: “Do they disbelieve in Allah?” He replied: “They are ungrateful to their husbands and ungrateful for kindness. If you were good to one of them for an entire lifetime, then she saw one thing from you that displeased her, she would say: ‘I have never seen any good from you at all.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word al-ʿashīr means the husband.","The expression “they commit kufr” means that they deny or show ingratitude. This demonstrates that the word kufr may be used for ingratitude toward rights without thereby making a person a disbeliever in Allah Most High. The detailed discussion appears in the Book of Faith.","The word “cluster” refers to grapes or similar fruit gathered together on a single stem; it is also called a qiṭf."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (2)، والبخاري (5197)، ومسلم (907)."},{"num":6339,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، قَالَ خَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي أَضْحًى ـ أَوْ فِطْرٍ ـ إِلَى الْمُصَلَّى، فَمَرَّ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ، فَقَالَ: يَا مَعْشَرَ النِّسَاءِ تَصَدَّقْنَ، فَإِنِّي أُرِيتُكُنَّ أَكْثَرَ أَهْلِ النَّارِ. فَقُلْنَ: وَبِمَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: تُكْثِرْنَ اللَّعْنَ، وَتَكْفُرْنَ الْعَشِيرَ، مَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الحيض (304)، ومسلم في الإيمان (80) من طريق سعيد بن أبي مريم، أخبرنا محمد بن جعفر، أخبرني زيد بن أسلم، عن عياض بن عبد الله، عن أبي سعيد الخدري، فذكره. واللفظ للبخاري. ولم يذكر مسلم لفظه وإنما حال فيه على حديث ابن عمر رضي الله عنهما، وهو الآتي:","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب نهي النساء عن كفر العشير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (304) and Muslim (80), and the wording is from al-Bukhari.","chapter_en":"Warning women against ingratitude toward the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the Day of Adha or Fitr to the prayer-place. He passed by the women and said: “O gathering of women, give charity, for I saw that you are the majority of the people of the Fire.” They said: Why is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “You frequently curse, and you are ungrateful to the husband…” to the end of the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[16503],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (304)، ومسلم (80)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":6340,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ. قَالَ:  شَهِدْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الصَّلَاةَ يَوْمَ الْعِيدِ. فَبَدَأَ بِالصَّلَاةِ قَبْلَ الْخُطْبَةِ. بِغَيْرِ أَذَانٍ وَلَا إِقَامَةٍ. ثُمَّ قَامَ مُتَوَكِّئًا عَلَى بِلَالٍ. فَأَمَرَ بِتَقْوَى اللَّهِ. وَحَثَّ عَلَى طَاعَتِهِ. وَوَعَظَ النَّاسَ. وَذَكَّرَهُمْ. ثُمَّ مَضَى. حَتَّى أَتَى النِّسَاءَ. فَوَعَظَهُنَّ وَذَكَّرَهُنَّ. فَقَالَ: تَصَدَّقْنَ. فَإِنَّ أَكْثَرَكُنَّ حَطَبُ جَهَنَّمَ، فَقَامَتِ امْرَأَةٌ مِنْ سِطَةِ النِّسَاءِ سَفْعَاءُ الْخَدَّيْنِ. فَقَالَتْ: لِمَ؟ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! قَالَ: لِأَنَّكُنَّ تُكْثِرْنَ الشَّكَاةَ. وَتَكْفُرْنَ الْعَشِيرَ، قَالَ: فَجَعَلْنَ يَتَصَدَّقْنَ مِنْ حُلِيِّهِنَّ. يُلْقِينَ فِي ثَوْبِ بِلَالٍ مِنْ أَقْرِطَتِهِنَّ وَخَوَاتِمِهِنَّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في صلاة العيدين (4:885) عن محمد بن عبدا لله بن نمير، حدثنا أبي، حدّثنا عبدالملك بن أبي سليمان، عن عطاء، عن جابر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب نهي النساء عن كفر العشير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (4:885) and al-Bukhari (978).","chapter_en":"Warning women against ingratitude toward the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: I witnessed the Eid prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He began with the prayer before the sermon, without adhan or iqamah. Then he stood, leaning on Bilal, and commanded the people to fear Allah, urged them to obey Him, admonished them, and reminded them. Then he moved on until he came to the women, and he admonished and reminded them, saying: “Give charity, for most of you are the fuel of Hell.” Then a woman from the middle of the women stood up, with darkened cheeks, and said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Because you complain much and are ungrateful to the husband.” He said: Then they began giving charity from their jewelry, throwing into Bilal’s cloth their earrings and rings."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (4:885)، والبخاري (978)."},{"num":6341,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن عُمَرَ، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: يَا مَعْشَرَ النِّسَاءِ تصدَّقْنَ وأكثِرْنَ الِاسْتِغْفَارَ، فَإِنِّي رَأَيْتُكُنَّ أَكْثَرَ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، فَقَالَتِ امْرَأَةٌ مِنْهُنَّ، جَزْلَةٌ: وَمَا لَنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَكْثَرَ أَهْلِ النَّارِ؟ قَالَ: تُكْثِرْنَ اللَّعْنَ، وتكفُرْنَ الْعَشِيرَ الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (79) عن محمد بن رُمح بن المهار المصريّ، أخبرنا الليث (هو ابن سعد)، عن ابن الهاد، عن عبدالله بن دينار، عن عبدالله بن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب نهي النساء عن كفر العشير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (79).","chapter_en":"Warning women against ingratitude toward the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O gathering of women, give charity and seek forgiveness often, for I saw that you are the majority of the people of the Fire.” A strong-minded woman among them said: Why are we, O Messenger of Allah, the majority of the people of the Fire? He said: “You curse frequently and you are ungrateful to the husband,” to the end of the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[16504],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (79)."},{"num":6342,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمِثْلِ مَعْنَى حَدِيثِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (80) من طريق إسماعيل( هو ابن جعفر) عن عمرو بن أبي عمرو، عن المقبري، عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ولم يذكر مسلم لفظه وإنما أحال فيه على حديث ابن عمر السابق.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب نهي النساء عن كفر العشير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (80).","chapter_en":"Warning women against ingratitude toward the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ something with the same meaning as the hadith of Ibn ‘Umar from the Prophet ﷺ, as stated by Muslim."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (80)."},{"num":6343,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَسْمَاءَ بِنْتِ يَزِيدَ –إِحْدَى نساء بني عَبْدِ الأشهل- تَقُولُ: مَرَّ بِنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَنَحْنُ فِي نِسْوَةٍ، فسلَّم عَلَيْنَا، وَقَالَ: إِيَّاكُنَّ وَكُفْرَ الْمُنَعَّمِينَ، فَقُلْنَا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَمَا كُفْرُ الْمُنَعَّمِينَ؟ قَالَ: لَعَلَّ إِحْدَاكُنَّ أَنْ تَطُولَ أَيْمَتُهَا بَيْنَ أَبَوَيْهَا، وَتَعْنُسَ، فَيَرْزُقَهَا اللهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ زَوْجًا، وَيَرْزُقَهَا مِنْهُ مَالًا وَوَلَدًا، فَتَغْضَبَ الْغَضْبَةَ، فَتَقُولُ: مَا رَأَيْتُ مِنْهُ يَوْمًا خَيْرًا قَطُّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (27561) والطبراني في الكبير (24/164) كلاهما من حديث شهر يقول: سمعت أسماء تقول: فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب نهي النساء عن كفر العشير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (27561) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr (24/164).","chapter_en":"Warning women against ingratitude toward the husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Asmāʾ bint Yazīd, one of the women of Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal, reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by us while we were with a group of women. He greeted us and said: “Beware of ingratitude toward those who bestow favors upon you.” We asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is ingratitude toward those who bestow favors?” He said: “One of you may remain unmarried for a long time in the house of her parents and grow older, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, provides her with a husband and grants her through him wealth and children. Then she becomes angry on one occasion and says: ‘I have never seen any good from him at all.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (27561)، والطبراني في الكبير (24/164)."},{"num":6344,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قَالَ لاَ تُؤْذِي امْرَأَةٌ زَوْجَهَا فِي الدُّنْيَا إِلاَّ قَالَتْ زَوْجَتُهُ مِنَ الْحُورِ الْعِينِ: لاَ تُؤْذِيهِ قَاتَلَكِ اللَّهُ، فَإِنَّمَا هُوَ عِنْدَكِ دَخِيلٌ، يُوشِكُ أَنْ يُفَارِقَكِ إِلَيْنَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1174) وابن ماجة (2014) وأحمد (22101) كلهم من حديث إسماعيل بن عياش، عن بَحير بن سعد، عن خالد بن معدان، عن كثير بن مرة، عن معاذ بن جبل فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب النهي عن إيذاءِ المرأةِ زوجَها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (1174), who graded it Hasan, Ibn Majah (2014), and Ahmad (22101).","chapter_en":"The prohibition of a woman harming her husband","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Mu‘adh ibn Jabal said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No woman harms her husband except that his wife from the women of Paradise says: ‘Do not harm him, may Allah fight you. He is only a temporary guest with you, and soon he will leave you and come to us.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1174) وحسنه، وابن ماجه (2014)، وأحمد (22101)."},{"num":6345,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : إِذَا اسْتَأْذَنَتِ امْرَأَةُ أَحَدِكُمْ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ فَلاَ يَمْنَعْهَا.","وزاد في رواية: فقال بلال بن عبد الله: والله لنمنعهنّ، قال: فأقبل عليه عبد الله فسبّه سبّاً سيئاً، ما سمعته سبّه مثله قط، وقال: أخبرُك عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وتقول: والله لنمنعهنّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5238)، ومسلم في الصلاة (134:442) كلاهما من طريق ابن عيينة، حدثنا الزهري، سمع سالماً يحدّث عن أبيه، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الإذن للنساء في الخروج إلى المسجد وقضاء حوائجهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5238) and Muslim (134:442), and the addition is in Muslim (135:442).","chapter_en":"Permission for women to go out to the mosque and to fulfill their needs","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Umar reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “If the wife of one of you asks permission to go to the mosque, he should not prevent her.” And in an added narration: Bilal ibn ‘Abd Allah said: By Allah, we will surely prevent them. So ‘Abd Allah turned to him and rebuked him harshly, with a rebuke the like of which I had never heard from him, and said: I inform you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you say: By Allah, we will surely prevent them?"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5238)، ومسلم (134 :442)، والزيادة في رواية مسلم (135 :442)."},{"num":6346,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: خَرَجَتْ سَوْدَةُ بِنْتُ زَمْعَةَ لَيْلاً، فَرَآهَا عُمَرُ فَعَرَفَهَا، فَقَالَ: إِنَّكِ وَاللَّهِ يَا سَوْدَةُ مَا تَخْفَيْنَ عَلَيْنَا، فَرَجَعَتْ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَذَكَرَتْ ذَلِكَ لَهُ، وَهْوَ فِي حُجْرَتِي يَتَعَشَّى، وَإِنَّ فِي يَدِهِ لَعَرْقًا، فَأُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ، فَرُفِعَ عَنْهُ، وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: قَدْ أَذِنَ لَكُنَّ أَنْ تَخْرُجْنَ لِحَوَائِجِكُنَّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5237) من طريق علي بن مُسهر- ومسلم في السلام (17:2170) من طريق أبي أسامة – كلاهما عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته، واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الإذن للنساء في الخروج إلى المسجد وقضاء حوائجهن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5237) and Muslim (2170/17). This is the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"Permission for women to go out to the mosque and to fulfill their needs","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah reported: Sawdah bint Zamʿah went out at night. ʿUmar saw her and recognized her, and said: “By Allah, O Sawdah, you cannot remain unrecognized by us.” She returned to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned this to him while he was eating supper in my apartment, with a bone containing some meat still in his hand. Revelation came down upon him. When it had ended, he said: “Permission has been granted to you women to go out for your needs.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5237)، ومسلم (17:2170)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":6347,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لاَ تُبَاشِرِ الْمَرْأَةُ الْمَرْأَةَ، فَتَنْعَتَهَا لِزَوْجِهَا، كَأَنَّهُ يَنْظُرُ إِلَيْهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5240) عن محمد بن يوسف، حدثنا سفيان، عن منصور، عن أبي وائل، عن عبد الله بن مسعود فذكره ورواه أيضا (5241) من وجه آخر عن أبي وائل مثله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا تباشر المرأة المرأة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5240).","chapter_en":"A woman must not closely expose another woman","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn Mas‘ud said: the Prophet ﷺ said: “A woman should not closely examine another woman and then describe her to her husband as though he were looking at her.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His saying, “describe her to her husband,” is because of the fear that the husband may become taken by that description, then divorce his wife or become infatuated with the woman being described."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5240)."},{"num":6348,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا تُبَاشِرِ الْمَرْأَةُ الْمَرْأَةَ، وَلَا الرَّجُلُ الرَّجُلَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (8318) والطبراني في الصغير (653) والطحاوي في مشكله (3258) كلهم من حديث أبي بكر، عن هشام، عن ابن سيرين، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب لا تباشر المرأة المرأة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (8318), al-Tabarani in al-Saghir (653), and al-Tahawi in Mushkil al-Athar (3258).","chapter_en":"A woman must not closely expose another woman","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman should not lie in close bodily contact with another woman, and a man should not lie in close bodily contact with another man.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (8318)، والطبراني في الصغير (653)، والطحاوي في مشكل الآثار (3258)."},{"num":6349,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يُبَاشِرِ الرَّجُلُ الرَّجُلَ، وَلا الْمَرْأَةُ الْمَرْأَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (2773) والطبراني في الكبير (11728) والبزار في كشف الأستار (2074) وابن حبان (5582) كلهم من حديث إسرائيل، عن سماك بن حرب، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا تباشر المرأة المرأة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ahmad (2773), al-Tabarani in al-Kabir (11728), and al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (2074).","chapter_en":"A woman must not closely expose another woman","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man should not lie in close bodily contact with another man, and a woman should not lie in close bodily contact with another woman.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (2773)، والطبراني في الكبير (11728)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (2074)."},{"num":6350,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَنْهَى أَنْ يُبَاشِرَ الرَّجُلُ الرَّجُلَ، فِي ثَوْبٍ وَاحِدٍ، وَالْمَرْأَةُ الْمَرْأَةُ فِي ثَوْبٍ وَاحِدٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (7775) من حديث عبد الرحمن بن أبي الزناد، عن موسى بن عقبة، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب لا تباشر المرأة المرأة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Hakim (4/287).","chapter_en":"A woman must not closely expose another woman","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid that a man closely join another man under one garment, and that a woman closely join another woman under one garment."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (7775)."},{"num":6351,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ:  لَا يَنْظُرُ الرَّجُلُ إِلَى عَوْرَةِ الرَّجُلِ، وَلَا الْمَرْأَةُ إِلَى عَوْرَةِ الْمَرْأَةِ. وَلَا يُفْضِي الرَّجُلُ إِلَى الرَّجُلِ فِي ثَوْبٍ وَاحِدٍ، وَلَا تُفْضِي الْمَرْأَةُ إِلَى الْمَرْأَةِ فِي الثَّوْبِ الْوَاحِدِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحيض (338) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا زيد بن الحُباب، عن الضحاك بن عثمان قال: أخبرني زيد بن أسلم، عن عبد الرحمن بن أبي سعيد، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم النظر إلى العورات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (338).","chapter_en":"The prohibition of looking at the private parts","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man must not look at the private part of another man, and a woman must not look at the private part of another woman. A man must not lie closely with another man under one garment, and a woman must not lie closely with another woman under one garment.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (338)."},{"num":6352,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّ مِنْ أشرّ النَّاسِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ، الرَّجُلَ يُفْضِي إِلَى امْرَأَتِهِ، وَتُفْضِي إِلَيْهِ ثُمَّ يَنْشُرُ سِرَّهَا.","وفي لفظ: إِنَّ مِنْ أَعْظَمِ الْأَمَانَةِ عِنْدَ اللهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ، الرَّجُلَ يُفْضِي إِلَى امْرَأَتِهِ وَتُفْضِي إِلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ يَنْشُرُ سِرَّهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه مسلم في النكاح (123:1437) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا مروان بن معاوية، عن عمر بن حمزة العمري، حدّثنا عبد الرحمن بن سعد، قال: سمعت أبا سعيد الخدري يقول:فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم إفشاء أسرار الجماع بين الزوجين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Muslim (123:1437).","chapter_en":"The prohibition of disclosing the secrets of intimacy between spouses","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the worst of people on the Day of Resurrection is a man who goes in unto his wife and she goes in unto him, then he spreads her secret.” And in another wording: “Among the greatest betrayals of trust before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is that a man goes in unto his wife and she goes in unto him, then he spreads her secret.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه مسلم (123:1437)."},{"num":6353,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: أَلَا عَسَى أَحَدُكُمْ أَنْ يَخْلُوَ بِأَهْلِهِ يُغْلِقُ بَابًا، ثُمَّ يُرْخِي سِتْرًا، ثُمَّ يَقْضِي حَاجَتَهُ، ثُمَّ إِذَا خَرَجَ حَدَّثَ أَصْحَابَهُ بِذَلِكَ، أَلَا عَسَى إِحْدَاكُنَّ أَنْ تُغْلِقَ بَابَهَا، وَتُرْخِي سِتْرَهَا، فَإِذَا قَضَيْتَ حَاجَتَهَا، حَدَّثَتْ صَوَاحِبَهَا، فَقَالَتِ امْرَأَةٌ سَفْعَاءُ الْخَدَّيْنِ: وَاللَّهِ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّهُنَّ لَيَفْعَلْنَ، وَإِنَّهُمْ لَيَفْعَلُونَ، قَالَ: فَلا تَفْعَلُوا، فَإِنَّهُ مِثْلُ ذَلِكَ مِثْلُ الشَّيْطَانِ لَقِيَ شَيْطَانَةً عَلَى قَارِعَةِ الطَّرِيقِ، فَقَضَى حَاجَتَهُ مِنْهَا، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ وَتَرَكَهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1450) عن روح بن حاتم أبي غسّان، ثنا مهدي بن عيسى، ثنا عباد بن عباد المهلبي، ثنا سعيد بن يزيد أبو مسلمة، عن أبي نضرة، عن أبي سعيد فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم إفشاء أسرار الجماع بين الزوجين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzar in Kashf al-Astar (1450).","chapter_en":"The prohibition of disclosing the secrets of intimacy between spouses","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Sa‘id narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Perhaps one of you is alone with his wife, closes the door, lets down the curtain, then fulfills his need, and when he comes out he tells his companions about it. And perhaps one of you women closes her door and lets down her curtain, then when she fulfills her need, she tells her female companions.” A dark-cheeked woman said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, the women do that, and the men do that too. He said: “Then do not do that, for the likeness of that is the likeness of a devil who met a she-devil on the roadside, fulfilled his need with her, then went away and left her.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1450)."},{"num":6354,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ -فِي حَدِيثِ طَوِيلٍ كَمَا ذُكِر-، وَجَاءَ فِيهِ:  هَلْ فِيكُمْ رجـل إِذَا أَتَى أَهْلَهُ أَغْلَقَ بَابَهُ، وَأَرْخَى سِتْرَهُ، ثُمَّ يَخْرُجُ فَيُحَدِّثُ فَيَقُولُ: فَعَلْتُ بِأَهْلِي كَذَا، وَفَعَلْتُ بِأَهْلِي كَذَا فَسَكَتُوا، فَأَقْبَلَ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ فَقَالَ: هَلْ مِنْكُنَّ تُحَدِّثُ، فَجَثَتْ فَتَاةٌ كَعَابٌ عَلَى إِحْدَى رُكْبَتَيْهَا، وَتَطَالَتْ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِيَرَاهَا وَيَسْمَعَ كَلَامَهَا، فَقَالَتْ: إِي وَاللهِ إِنَّهُمْ ليتحدثون، وَإِنَّهُنَّ لَيُحَدِّثْنَ، قَالَ: فَهَلْ تَدْرُونَ مَا مَثَلُ مَنْ فَعَلَ ذَلِكَ؟ إِنَّ مَثَلَ ذَلِكَ، مَثَلُ شَيْطَانٍ وَشَيْطَانَةٍ لَقِيَ أَحَدُهُمَا صَاحِبَهُ بِالسِّكَّةِ، فَقَضَى حَاجَتَهُ مِنْهَا وَالنَّاسُ يَنْظُرُونَ إِلَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (10977) وأبو داود (2174) والترمذي (2787) والنسائي (5118،5117) وابن السني (615) كلهم من حديث سعيد الجريري، عن أبي نضرة، عن الطفاوي، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم إفشاء أسرار الجماع بين الزوجين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ahmad (10977), Abu Dawud (2174), and al-Khara’iti in Masawi’ al-Akhlaq (430).","chapter_en":"The prohibition of disclosing the secrets of intimacy between spouses","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah narrated — in a long hadith as previously mentioned — and in it there came: “Is there among you any man who, when he goes to his wife, closes his door and lets down his curtain, then goes out and says: I did such-and-such with my wife, and I did such-and-such with my wife?” They remained silent. Then he turned to the women and said: “Is there any among you who speaks of such things?” Then a young full-breasted girl knelt on one of her knees and stretched herself up so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ could see her and hear her words. She said: Yes, by Allah, the men certainly speak of it, and the women certainly speak of it too. He said: “Do you know what the likeness of the one who does that is? The likeness of that is like a male devil and a female devil who met one another in the street, then he fulfilled his desire with her while the people were watching.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (10977)، وأبو داود (2174)، والخرائطي في مساوئ الأخلاق (430)."},{"num":6355,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عمرو، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِذَا تَزَوَّجَ أَحَدُكُمُ امْرَأَةً، أَوِ اشْتَرَى خَادِمًا فَلْيَقُلِ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ خَيْرَهَا، وَخَيْرَ مَا جَبَلْتَها عَلَيْهِ، وَأَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّهَا وَمِنْ شَرِّ مَا جَبَلْتَها عَلَيْهِ، وَإِذَا اشْتَرَى بَعِيرًا فَلْيَأْخُذْ بِذِرْوَةِ سَنانه وَلْيَقُلْ مِثْلَ ذَلِكَ.","وفي لفظ: إذا أفاد أحدُكم امرأةً، أو خادماً، أو دابّةً، فليأخذ بناصيتها، وليقُلْ: فذكر الحديث."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2160) وابن ماجة (1918) وابن السني (100) والحاكم (2/185) والبيهقي (13838) كلهم من حديث محمد بن عجلان، عن عمرو بن شعيب، بإسناده مثله.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما يقول الرجل إذا دخل على عروسه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2160), Ibn Majah (1918), Ibn al-Sunni (100), and al-Hakim (2/185).","chapter_en":"What a man says when he enters upon his bride","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “When one of you marries a woman or buys a servant, let him say: O Allah, I ask You for her good and the good upon which You created her, and I seek refuge in You from her evil and the evil upon which You created her. And if he buys a camel, let him take hold of the top of its hump and say the same.” And in another wording: “When one of you acquires a wife, a servant, or a riding beast, let him take hold of its forelock,” then let him say the supplication just mentioned."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2160)، وابن ماجه (1918)، وابن السني (100)، والحاكم (2/185)."},{"num":6356,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَمَا لَوْ أَنَّ أَحَدَهُمْ يَقُولُ حِينَ يَأْتِي أَهْلَهُ: بِاسْمِ اللَّهِ، اللَّهُمَّ جَنِّبْنِي الشَّيْطَانَ، وَجَنِّبِ الشَّيْطَانَ مَا رَزَقْتَنَا، ثُمَّ قُدِّرَ بَيْنَهُمَا فِي ذَلِكَ، أَوْ قُضِيَ وَلَدٌ، لَمْ يَضُرَّهُ شَيْطَانٌ أَبَدًا.","وفي لفظ: لو أن أحدهم إذا أراد أن يأتي أهله..."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5165)، ومسلم في النكاح (116:1434) كلاهما من طريق منصور، عن سالم بن أبي الجعد، عن كُريب، عن ابن عباس، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب التسمية عند الجماع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5165) and Muslim (116:1434). The first wording is from al-Bukhari, and the second from Muslim.","chapter_en":"The recommendation to mention Allah’s name before intercourse","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: the Prophet ﷺ said: “If one of you were to say when he goes to his wife: In the name of Allah. O Allah, keep Satan away from me, and keep Satan away from what You provide us, then if it is decreed that a child be conceived between them in that act, Satan will never harm him.” And in another wording: “If one of them, when he intends to go to his wife…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5165)، ومسلم (116:1434)، واللفظ للبخاري، واللفظ الثاني لمسلم."},{"num":6357,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ بَهْزِ بْنِ حَكِيمٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، عَنْ جَدِّهِ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! عَوْرَاتُنَا مَا نَأْتِي مِنْهَا وَمَا نَذَرُ؟ قَالَ: احْفَظْ عَوْرَتَكَ إِلاَّ مِنْ زَوْجَتِكَ، أَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ يَمِينُكَ. قَالَ قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! إِذَا كَانَ الْقَوْمُ بَعْضُهُمْ فِي بَعْضٍ؟ قَالَ: إِنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ أَنْ لاَ يَرَيَنَّهَا أَحَدٌ، فَلاَ يَرَيَنَّهَا. قَالَ قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! إِذَا كَانَ أَحَدُنَا خَالِيًا؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُ أَحَقُّ أَنْ يُسْتَحْيَا مِنْهُ مِنَ النَّاسِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4017) والترمذي (2794،2769) وابن ماجة (1920) والحاكم (7358) والبيهقي (960) كلهم من هذا الوجه. وإسناده حسن من أجل بهز بن حكيم وأبيه حكيم بن معاوية فإنهما صدوقان.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب استحباب التستر عند الجماع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (4017), al-Tirmidhi (2769, 2794), Ibn Majah (1920), and al-Hakim (7358).","chapter_en":"The recommendation of concealment during intercourse","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, regarding our private parts, what may we uncover and what must we conceal? He said: “Guard your private part except from your wife or from what your right hand possesses.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if the people are among one another? He said: “If you are able that no one should see it, then let no one see it.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if one of us is alone? He said: “Then Allah has more right that one should be shy before Him than before people.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[1496,12870],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4017)، والترمذي (2769، 2794)، وابن ماجه (1920)، والحاكم (7358)."},{"num":6358,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر قال: كانت اليهود تقول: إذا أتى الرجلُ امرأته من دُبُرها في قُبلها، كان الولد أحول فنزلت: ﴿نِسَاؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَكُمْ فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أَنَّى شِئْتُمْ﴾ [سورة البقرة: 223]. "],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4528)، ومسلم في النكاح (117:1435) كلاهما من طريق سفيان (هو الثوري)، عن ابن المنكدر، سمع جابراً يقول (فذكره).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المرأة في قبلها كيف ما شاء، إذا تجنب الإتيان في الدبر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari in al-Tafsir (4528) and Muslim in al-Nikah (117:1435), both by the route of Sufyan — that is, al-Thawri — from Ibn al-Munkadir, who heard Jabir say it.","chapter_en":"Going to one’s wife in her front as one wishes, so long as anal intercourse is avoided","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: The Jews used to say: If a man comes to his wife from behind while entering in her front, the child will be cross-eyed. So this verse was revealed: “Your wives are a place of cultivation for you, so go to your place of cultivation however you wish.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى: (نِسَاؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَكُمْ فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أَنَّى شِئْتُمْ) [البقرة: ٢٢٣]"],"en":["Allah Most High said: “Your wives are a place of cultivation for you, so go to your place of cultivation however you wish.” [al-Baqarah: 223]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4528)، ومسلم (117:1435)."},{"num":6359,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ قَالَ: قَالَتِ الْيَهُودُ: إِنَّ الرَّجُلَ إِذَا أَتَى امْرَأَتَهُ وَهِيَ مُجَبِّيَةٌ، جَاءَ وَلَدُهُ أَحْوَلَ، فَنَزَلَتْ: ﴿نِسَاؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَكُمْ فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أَنَّى شِئْتُمْ﴾ [البقرة: ٢٢٣] إِنْ شَاءَ مُجَبِّيَةً وَإِنْ شَاءَ غَيْرَ مُجَبِّيَةٍ إِذَا كَانَ فِي صِمَامٍ وَاحِدٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في النكاح (119:1435) وابن حبان في صحيحه (4166) كلاهما من حديث وهب بن جرير، قال: حدثنا أبي، قال: سمعت النعمان بن راشد، يحدث عن الزهري، عن محمد بن المنكدر، عن جابر فذكره واللفظ لابن حبان. وأما مسلم فلم يذكر لفظ الحديث كاملا، وإنما أحال على السابق وقال: وزاد في حديث النعمان عن الزهري: \"وإن شاء مُجبّية وإن شاء غير مجَبّية غير أن ذلك في صمام واحد\".","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المرأة في قبلها كيف ما شاء، إذا تجنب الإتيان في الدبر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (119:1435) and Ibn Hibban in his Sahih (4166), and the wording is that of Ibn Hibban.","chapter_en":"Going to one’s wife in her front as one wishes, so long as anal intercourse is avoided","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: The Jews said: If a man comes to his wife while she is bent forward, the child will come out cross-eyed. So the verse was revealed: “Your wives are a place of cultivation for you, so go to your place of cultivation however you wish” [al-Baqarah: 223] — whether bent forward or otherwise, so long as it is in one opening."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His saying, “mujabbiyah,” means bent over on her face, resembling the posture of prostration. And his saying, “one opening,” means one orifice, namely the front passage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (119:1435)، وابن حبان في صحيحه (4166)، واللفظ لابن حبان."},{"num":6360,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: جَاءَ عُمَرُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! هَلَكْتُ. قَالَ: وَمَا أَهْلَكَكَ. قَالَ: حَوَّلْتُ رَحْلِي اللَّيْلَةَ. قَالَ: فَلَمْ يَرُدَّ عَلَيْهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ شَيْئًا، قَالَ: فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ هَذِهِ الآيَةَ: ﴿نِسَاؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَكُمْ فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أَنَّى شِئْتُمْ﴾ [سورة البقرة: 223] ) أَقْبِلْ وَأَدْبِرْ، وَاتَّقِ الدُّبُرَ وَالْحِيضَةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (2980) وأحمد (2703) والبيهقي (14125) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4202) كلهم من طريق يعقوب بن عبد الله القمي، قال: حدثنا جعفر بن المغيرة، عن سعيد بن جبير، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المرأة في قبلها كيف ما شاء، إذا تجنب الإتيان في الدبر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (2980), Ahmad (2703), al-Bayhaqi (7/197), and authenticated by Ibn Hibban (4202).","chapter_en":"Going to one’s wife in her front as one wishes, so long as anal intercourse is avoided","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ‘Abbas said: ‘Umar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined. He said: “What has ruined you?” He said: I changed my position on my mount last night. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not answer him with anything. Then this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Your wives are a place of cultivation for you, so go to your place of cultivation however you wish” — from the front or from behind, but avoid the anus and menstruation."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12003],"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (2980)، وأحمد (2703)، والبيهقي (14125)، وصححه ابن حبان (4202)."},{"num":6361,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: إِنَّ ابْنَ عُمَرَ - وَاللَّهُ يَغْفِرُ لَهُ - أَوْهَمَ، إِنَّمَا كَانَ هَذَا الْحَىُّ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ - وَهُمْ أَهْلُ وَثَنٍ - مَعَ هَذَا الْحَىِّ مِنْ يَهُودَ - وَهُمْ أَهْلُ كِتَابٍ - وَكَانُوا يَرَوْنَ لَهُمْ فَضْلاً عَلَيْهِمْ فِي الْعِلْمِ، فَكَانُوا يَقْتَدُونَ بِكَثِيرٍ مِنْ فِعْلِهِمْ. وَكَانَ مِنْ أَمْرِ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ أَنْ لاَ يَأْتُوا النِّسَاءَ إِلاَّ عَلَى حَرْفٍ، وَذَلِكَ أَسْتَرُ مَا تَكُونُ الْمَرْأَةُ فَكَانَ هَذَا الْحَىُّ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ قَدْ أَخَذُوا بِذَلِكَ مِنْ فِعْلِهِمْ، وَكَانَ هَذَا الْحَىُّ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ يَشْرَحُونَ النِّسَاءَ شَرْحًا مُنْكَرًا، وَيَتَلَذَّذُونَ مِنْهُنَّ مُقْبِلاَتٍ وَمُدْبِرَاتٍ وَمُسْتَلْقِيَاتٍ. فَلَمَّا قَدِمَ الْمُهَاجِرُونَ الْمَدِينَةَ. تَزَوَّجَ رَجُلٌ مِنْهُمُ امْرَأَةً مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، فَذَهَبَ يَصْنَعُ بِهَا ذَلِكَ، فَأَنْكَرَتْهُ عَلَيْهِ وَقَالَتْ: إِنَّمَا كُنَّا نُؤْتَى عَلَى حَرْفٍ فَاصْنَعْ ذَلِكَ، وَإِلاَّ فَاجْتَنِبْنِي حَتَّى شَرِيَ أَمْرُهُمَا. فَبَلَغَ ذَلِكَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ﴿نِسَاؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَكُمْ فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أَنَّى شِئْتُمْ﴾ [سورة البقرة: 223] } أَىْ مُقْبِلاَتٍ وَمُدْبِرَاتٍ وَمُسْتَلْقِيَاتٍ يَعْنِي بِذَلِكَ مَوْضِعَ الْوَلَدِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2164) عن عبد العزيز بن يحيى أبي الأصبغ حدثني محمد – يعني ابن سلمة – عن محمد بن إسحاق، عن أبان بن صالح، عن مجاهد، عن ابن عباس قال:فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المرأة في قبلها كيف ما شاء، إذا تجنب الإتيان في الدبر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (2164).","chapter_en":"Going to one’s wife in her front as one wishes, so long as anal intercourse is avoided","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās reported: Ibn ʿUmar—may Allah forgive him—was mistaken. This group of the Anṣār had formerly been idol worshippers and lived alongside a group of Jews who were People of the Book. The Anṣār regarded them as superior to themselves in knowledge and therefore followed many of their practices. Among the practices of the People of the Book was that they would approach women in only one position, considering that to be the most concealing position for the woman. The Anṣār had adopted this practice from them. The people of Quraysh, however, used to engage with women in a variety of positions, enjoying them facing them, from behind, and while lying down. When the Emigrants came to Madinah, one of them married a woman from the Anṣār and wished to approach her in that way. She objected and said: “We were approached only in one position. Either do that or keep away from me.” Their dispute became serious and intensified, and the matter reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then revealed: “Your wives are a place of cultivation for you, so approach your place of cultivation however you wish.”  [al-Baqarah: 223] Meaning: facing them, from behind, or while they are lying down, provided that it is in the place from which children are born."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The phrase “their matter became serious” means that their dispute became grave and intensified."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2164)."},{"num":6362,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ خُزَيْمَةَ بْنِ ثَابِتٍ قال: أَنَّ سَائِلًا سَأَلَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم عَنْ إتْيَانِ النِّسَاءِ فِي أَدْبَارِهِنَّ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم: حَلَالٌ ثُمَّ دَعَاهُ، أَوْ أَمَرَ بِهِ، فَدُعِيَ فَقَالَ: كَيْفَ قُلْت فِي أَيِّ الْخَرِبَتَيْنِ، أَوْ فِي أَيِّ الْخَرَزَتَيْنِ، أَوْ فِي الخصفين؟ أ من دُبْرِهَا فِي قُبُلِهَا فَنَعَمْ، أَمْ مِنْ دُبْرِهَا فِي دُبْرِهَا فَلَا، إنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَسْتَحْيِ مِنْ الْحَقِّ، لَا تَأْتُوا النِّسَاءَ فِي أَدْبَارِهِنَّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الشافعي في الأم (2209) قال: أخبرنا عمي محمد بن علي بن شافع، عن عبد الله بن علي بن السائب، عن عمرو بن أحيحة أو ابن فلان ابن أحيحة بن فلان الأنصار. قال: قال محمد بن علي وكان ثقة – عن خزيمة بن ثابت فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المرأة في قبلها كيف ما شاء، إذا تجنب الإتيان في الدبر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Shafi‘i in al-Umm (5/94).","chapter_en":"Going to one’s wife in her front as one wishes, so long as anal intercourse is avoided","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khuzaymah ibn Thabit said: A questioner asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about going to women in their backsides. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Lawful.” Then he called him back — or ordered that he be called — and when he was brought, he said: “How did you say it? In which of the two openings? Or which of the two parts? Or which of the two places? If from her back into her front, then yes. But if from her back into her back, then no. Indeed Allah is not shy of the truth. Do not go to women in their backsides.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الشافعي في الأم (2209)."},{"num":6363,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قَالَ لاَ يَنْظُرُ اللَّهُ إِلَى رَجُلٍ جَامَعَ امْرَأَتَهُ فِي دُبُرِهَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2162) وابن ماجه (1923) وأحمد (7684) وعبد الرزاق (20952) والبيهقي (14123) كلهم من حديث سهيل بن أبي صالح، عن الحارث بن مُخلّد، عن أبي هريرة فذكره. ولفظ أبي داود: «مَلْعونٌ مَنْ أتى امرأتَه في دُبُرِها»","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المرأة في قبلها كيف ما شاء، إذا تجنب الإتيان في الدبر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2162), Ibn Majah (1923), and Ahmad (7684).","chapter_en":"Going to one’s wife in her front as one wishes, so long as anal intercourse is avoided","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “Allah will not look at a man who has intercourse with his wife in her anus.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2162)، وابن ماجه (1923)، وأحمد (7684)."},{"num":6364,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لاَ يَنْظُرُ اللَّهُ إِلَى رَجُلٍ أَتَى رَجُلاً، أَوِ امْرَأَةً فِي الدُّبُرِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1165) وأبو بكر بن أبي شيبة (16803) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4418، 4204 ،4203) وابن الجارود (729) كلهم من حديث أبي خالد الأحمر، عن الضحاك بن عثمان، عن مخرمة بن سليمان، عن كُريب، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المرأة في قبلها كيف ما شاء، إذا تجنب الإتيان في الدبر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (1165), Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah (4/251–252), and authenticated by Ibn Hibban (4418).","chapter_en":"Going to one’s wife in her front as one wishes, so long as anal intercourse is avoided","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will not look at a man who goes to a man, or to a woman, in the anus.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1165)، وأبو بكر بن أبي شيبة (16803)، وصححه ابن حبان (4418)."},{"num":6365,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ نَهَى عَنْ مَحَاشِّ النِّسَاءِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط –مجمع البحرين (2308) عن محمد بن عيسى بن السكن، ثنا علي بن بحر، عن ابن أبي فُديك، عن الضحاك بن عثمان، عن محمد بن المنكدر، عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المرأة في قبلها كيف ما شاء، إذا تجنب الإتيان في الدبر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Awsat — Majma‘ al-Bahrayn (2308).","chapter_en":"Going to one’s wife in her front as one wishes, so long as anal intercourse is avoided","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah reported that the Prophet ﷺ forbade approaching the buttocks of women."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (2308)."},{"num":6366,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُقْبَةَ بْنِ عَامِرٍ الْجُهَنِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَعَنَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ يَأْتُونَ النِّسَاءَ فِي مَحَاشِّهِنَّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط –مجمع البحرين (2309) من طريق عبد الصمد بن الفضل، عن عبد الله بن وهب، أخبرني ابنُ لهعية، عن مِشرح بن هاعان، عن عقبة بن عامر الجهني قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إتيان المرأة في قبلها كيف ما شاء، إذا تجنب الإتيان في الدبر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Awsaṭ — Majmaʿ al-Baḥrayn (2309).","chapter_en":"Going to one’s wife in her front as one wishes, so long as anal intercourse is avoided","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah curse those who have intercourse with women in their anuses.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ibn al-Qayyim said in al-Ṭibb al-Nabawī (p. 313):","“As for intercourse through the anus, it was never made permissible upon the tongue of any prophet. Whoever attributes to some of the early Muslims the view that intercourse with one’s wife through the anus is permissible has wrongly attributed that view to them.”","He also said:","“If Allah prohibited intercourse in the vagina because of temporary harm, then what should be thought of a place that is inherently a place of constant harm, in addition to the further corruption of exposing oneself to the cessation of offspring?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (2309)."},{"num":6367,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: كَانَتْ إِحْدَانَا إِذَا كَانَتْ حَائِضًا، فَأَرَادَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يُبَاشِرَهَا، أَمَرَهَا أَنْ تَتَّزِرَ فِي فَوْرِ حَيْضَتِهَا، ثُمَّ يُبَاشِرُهَا. قَالَتْ: وَأَيُّكُمْ يَمْلِكُ إِرْبَهُ كَمَا كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَمْلِكُ إِرْبَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الحيض (302) ومسلم في الحيض (293) كلاهما من طريق علي بن مسهرن قال: أخبرنا أبو إسحاق الشيباني، عن عبدالرحمن بن الأسود، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في مباشرة الحائض دون الجماع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (302) and Muslim (293).","chapter_en":"What has been reported about intimacy with a menstruating wife short of intercourse","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["‘A’ishah said: When one of us was menstruating and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to enjoy her, he would command her to wrap a waistcloth around herself at the beginning of her menstruation, then he would enjoy her. She said: Which of you can control his desire as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ controlled his desire?"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[1521],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (302)، ومسلم (293)."},{"num":6368,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن مَيْمُونَةَ قَالَتْ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذَا أَرَادَ أَنْ يُبَاشِرَ امْرَأَةً مِنْ نِسَائِهِ أَمَرَهَا فَاتَّزَرَتْ، وَهْىَ حَائِضٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الحيض (303) ومسلم في الحيض (294) كلاهما من طريق الشيباني، عن عبدالله بن شداد، قال: سمعت ميمونة، قالت: فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في مباشرة الحائض دون الجماع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (303) and Muslim (294).","chapter_en":"What has been reported about intimacy with a menstruating wife short of intercourse","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Maymunah said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wished to enjoy one of his wives, he would command her to wrap herself in a waistcloth while she was menstruating."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[1522],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (303)، ومسلم (294)."},{"num":6369,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ:  أَنَّ الْيَهُودَ كَانُوا إِذَا حَاضَتِ الْمَرْأَةُ فِيهِمْ لَمْ يُؤَاكِلُوهَا وَلَمْ يُجَامِعُوهُنَّ فِي الْبُيُوتِ، فَسَأَلَ أَصْحَابُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: ﴿وَيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْمَحِيضِ قُلْ هُوَ أَذًى فَاعْتَزِلُوا النِّسَاءَ فِي الْمَحِيضِ﴾ إِلَى آخِرِ الْآيَةِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اصْنَعُوا كُلَّ شَيْءٍ إِلَّا النِّكَاحَ، فَبَلَغَ ذَلِكَ الْيَهُودَ، فَقَالُوا: مَا يُرِيدُ هَذَا الرَّجُلُ أَنْ يَدَعَ مِنْ أَمْرِنَا شَيْئًا إِلَّا خَالَفَنَا فِيهِ، فَجَاءَ أُسَيْدُ بْنُ حُضَيْرٍ وَعَبَّادُ بْنُ بِشْرٍ فَقَالَا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ الْيَهُودَ تَقُولُ: كَذَا وَكَذَا، فَلَا نُجَامِعُهُنَّ، فَتَغَيَّرَ وَجْهُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى ظَنَنَّا أَنْ قَدْ وَجَدَ عَلَيْهِمَا، فَخَرَجَا فَاسْتَقْبَلَهُمَا هَدِيَّةٌ مِنْ لَبَنٍ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَرْسَلَ فِي آثَارِهِمَا فَسَقَاهُمَا، فَعَرَفَا أَنْ لَمْ يَجِدْ عَلَيْهِمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحيض (302) عن زهير بن حرب، حدثنا عبدالرحمن بن مهدي، حدَّثنا حمَّاد بن سلمة، حدثنا ثابت، عن أنسٍ، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في مباشرة الحائض دون الجماع","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (302).","chapter_en":"What has been reported about intimacy with a menstruating wife short of intercourse","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas said: The Jews, when a woman among them menstruated, would not eat with her and would not live with her in the houses. So the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ asked the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah Most High revealed: “And they ask you about menstruation. Say: It is harm, so keep away from women during menstruation” to the end of the verse [al-Baqarah: 222]. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do everything except intercourse.” That reached the Jews, and they said: This man does not want to leave anything from our affairs except that he opposes us in it. Then Usayd ibn Hudayr and ‘Abbad ibn Bishr came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews say such-and-such; should we then have intercourse with them? The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed until we thought that he was angry with them. Then they went out, and a gift of milk for the Prophet ﷺ met them, so he sent after them and gave them drink, and they knew that he had not been angry with them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (302)."},{"num":6370,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ مُحَيْرِيزٍ، أَنَّهُ قَالَ: دَخَلْتُ الْمَسْجِدَ، فَرَأَيْتُ أَبَا سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيَّ، فَجَلَسْتُ إِلَيْهِ، فَسَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ الْعَزْلِ،، قَالَ أَبُو سَعِيدٍ خَرَجْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي غَزْوَةِ بَنِي الْمُصْطَلِقِ، فَأَصَبْنَا سَبْيًا مِنْ سَبْىِ الْعَرَبِ، فَاشْتَهَيْنَا النِّسَاءَ، وَاشْتَدَّتْ عَلَيْنَا الْعُزْبَةُ، وَأَحْبَبْنَا الْعَزْلَ، فَأَرَدْنَا أَنْ نَعْزِلَ، وَقُلْنَا نَعْزِلُ وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْنَ أَظْهُرِنَا قَبْلَ أَنْ نَسْأَلَهُ، فَسَأَلْنَاهُ عَنْ ذَلِكَ، فَقَالَ: مَا عَلَيْكُمْ أَنْ لاَ تَفْعَلُوا، مَا مِنْ نَسَمَةٍ كَائِنَةٍ إِلَى يَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ إِلاَّ وَهْىَ كَائِنَةٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الطلاق (95)، عن ربيعة بن عبد الرحمن، عن محمد بن يحيى بن حبان، عن ابن محيريز، فذكره. ورواه البخاري في العتق (2542) عن عبد الله بن يوسف، عن مالك بإسناده.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Malik (95), al-Bukhari (2542), and Muslim (125:1438).","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Muhayriz said: I entered the mosque and saw Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri, so I sat with him and asked him about withdrawal. He said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq, and we obtained female captives from the Arab captives. We desired women, celibacy had become hard on us, and we wanted ransom money, so we intended to practice withdrawal. We said: Shall we practice withdrawal while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is among us before asking him? So we asked him about that, and he said: “There is no blame upon you if you do not do it. There is no soul that will exist until the Day of Resurrection except that it will surely come into existence.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8897],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (95)، والبخاري (2542)، ومسلم (125:1438)."},{"num":6371,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، قَالَ: أَصَبْنَا سَبْيًا فَكُنَّا نَعْزِلُ، فَسَأَلْنَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: أَوَإِنَّكُمْ لَتَفْعَلُونَ؟ قَالَهَا ثَلاَثًا مَا مِنْ نَسَمَةٍ كَائِنَةٍ إِلَى يَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ إِلاَّ هِيَ كَائِنَةٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5210)، ومسلم في النكاح (127:1438) كلاهما عن عبد الله بن محمد، حدثنا جويرية، عن مالك، عن الزهري، عن ابن مُحيريز، عن أبي سعيد الخدري، قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5210) and Muslim (1438:127).","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Saʿid al-Khudri said: We captured female prisoners, and we used to practice withdrawal, so we asked the Messenger of Allah about it. He said: “Do you really do that?” He said it three times. “There is no soul that is destined to exist until the Day of Resurrection except that it will surely come into existence.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5210)، ومسلم (127:1438)."},{"num":6372,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، أَنَّ رَجُلاً، قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنَّ لِي جَارِيَةً، وَأَنَا أَعْزِلُ عَنْهَا، وَأَنَا أَكْرَهُ أَنْ تَحْمِلَ، وَأَنَا أُرِيدُ مَا يُرِيدُ الرِّجَالُ، وَإِنَّ الْيَهُودَ تُحَدِّثُ أَنَّ الْعَزْلَ مَوْءُودَةُ الصُّغْرَى. قَالَ كَذَبَتْ يَهُودُ، لَوْ أَرَادَ اللَّهُ أَنْ يَخْلُقَهُ مَا اسْتَطَعْتَ أَنْ تَصْرِفَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: روى عن أبي سعيد الخدري من طرق:","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2171), Ahmad (11477, 11288), and al-Tahawi in Mushkil al-Athar (1917).","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Saʿid al-Khudri narrated that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a slave-girl, and I withdraw from her. I dislike that she should become pregnant, though I desire what men desire. The Jews say that withdrawal is minor infanticide. He said: “The Jews have lied. If Allah intended to create it, you would not be able to turn it away.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2171)، وأحمد (11477، 11288)، والطحاوي في مشكل الآثار (1917)."},{"num":6373,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، أَنَّ رَجُلًا أَتَى رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ لِي جَارِيَةً هِيَ خَادِمُنَا وَسَانِيَتُنَا، وَأَنَا أَطُوفُ عَلَيْهَا، وَأَنَا أَكْرَهُ أَنْ تَحْمِلَ؟ فَقَالَ: اعْزِلْ عَنْهَا إِنْ شِئْتَ، فَإِنَّهُ سَيَأْتِيهَا مَا قدّر لَهَا فَلَبِثَ الرَّجُلُ ثُمَّ أَتَاهُ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ الْجَارِيَةَ قَدْ حَبِلَتْ؟ فَقَالَ: قَدْ أَخْبَرْتُكَ أَنَّهُ سَيَأْتِيهَا مَا قدّر لَهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في النكاح (1439) عن أحمد بن عبد الله بن يونس، حدّثنا زهير، أخبرنا أبو الزبير، عن جابر بن عبد الله فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1439). In another narration: “That will not prevent anything Allah has intended.” Then the man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the slave-girl I mentioned to you has become pregnant. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.”","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah narrated that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “I have a slave-girl who serves us and waters our land, and I have relations with her, but I dislike that she should become pregnant.” He said: “Practice withdrawal from her if you wish, for what has been decreed for her will come to her.” The man stayed away for some time, then came back and said: The slave-girl has become pregnant. He said: “I told you that what had been decreed for her would come to her.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1439). وفي رواية: (( إن ذلك لن يمنع شيئا أراده الله )). قال: فجاء الرجل فقال: يا رسول الله، إن الجارية التي كنت ذكرتها لك حملت؟ فقال رسول الله ﷺ: (( أنا عبد الله ورسوله ))."},{"num":6374,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ، قَالَ: كُنَّا نَعْزِلُ وَالْقُرْآنُ يَنْزِلُ. زَادَ إِسْحَاقُ قَالَ سُفْيَانُ لَوْ كَانَ شَيْئًا يُنْهَى عَنْهُ لَنَهَانَا عَنْهُ الْقُرْآنُ.","وفي لفظ: كنا نعزل على عهد رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5208)، ومسلم في النكاح (1440) كلاهما من طريق سفيان (هو ابن عيينة)، عن عمرو (هو ابن دينار) أخبرني عطاء، أنه سمع جابراً، فذكره. واللفظ الآخر عند البخاري (5207) من طريق ابن جريج، ومسلم من طريق معقل- كلاهما عن عطاء، عن جابر.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5208) and Muslim (1440).","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah said: We used to practice withdrawal while the Qur’an was being revealed. If it had been something forbidden, the Qur’an would have forbidden us from it. And in another wording: We used to practice withdrawal during the time of the Messenger of Allah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5208)، ومسلم (1440)."},{"num":6375,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ، قَالَ:  كُنَّا نَعْزِلُ عَلَى عَهْدِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَبَلَغَ ذَلِكَ نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَمْ يَنْهَنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في النكاح (138:1439) عن أبي غسّان المِسْمعي، حدّثنا معاذ بن هشام، حدثني أبي، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1440:163).","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabir said: We used to practice withdrawal during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that reached the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, yet he did not forbid us."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (138:1439)."},{"num":6376,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَامِرِ بْنِ سَعْدٍ، أَنَّ أُسَامَةَ بْنَ زَيْدٍ، أَخْبَرَ وَالِدَهُ، سَعْدَ بْنَ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ، أَنَّ رَجُلاً، جَاءَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  فَقَالَ: إِنِّي أَعْزِلُ عَنِ امْرَأَتِي. فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  لِمَ تَفْعَلُ ذَلِكَ. فَقَالَ الرَّجُلُ: أُشْفِقُ عَلَى وَلَدِهَا أَوْ عَلَى أَوْلاَدِهَا. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  لَوْ كَانَ ذَلِكَ ضَارًّا ضَرَّ فَارِسَ وَالرُّومَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في النكاح (143:1443) من طريق عبد الله بن يزيد المقبري، حدّثنا حيوة، حدثني عيّاش بن عباس، أن أبا النضر حدّثه عن عامر بن سعد، به، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1443:143).","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAmir ibn Saʿd narrated that Usamah ibn Zayd informed his father Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqas that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I practice withdrawal from my wife. Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said to him: “Why do you do that?” The man said: I fear for her child, or for her children. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If it were harmful, it would have harmed the Persians and the Romans.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (143:1443)."},{"num":6377,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَكَ فِي جِمَاعِ زَوْجَتِكَ أَجْرٌ، فَقِيلَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَفِي شَهْوَةٍ يَكُونُ مِنْ أَجْرٍ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، أَرَأَيْتَ لَوْ كَانَ لَكَ وَلَدٌ قَدْ أَدْرَكَ، ثُمَّ مَاتَ أَكُنْتَ مُحْتَسِبَهُ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: أَنْتَ كُنْتَ خَلَقْتَهُ؟ قَالَ: بَلِ اللَّهُ خَلَقَهُ، قَالَ: أَنْتَ كُنْتَ هَدَيْتَهُ؟ قَالَ: بَلِ اللَّهُ هَدَاهُ، قَالَ: أَكُنْتَ تَرْزُقُهُ؟ قَالَ: بَلِ اللَّهُ كَانَ رَزَقَهُ، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَضَعْهُ فِي حَلَالِهِ وَجَنِّبْهُ حَرَامَهُ، وَأَقْرِرْهُ، فَإِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ أَحْيَاهُ، وَإِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ أَمَاتَهُ، وَلَكَ أَجْرٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (4192)، عن ابن سلم، قال: حدثنا حرملة، قال: حدثنا ابن وهب، قال: أخبرني عمرو بن الحارث، أن سعيد بن أبي هلال حدّثه عن أبي سعيد مولى المهري، عن أبي ذر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Hibban (4192).","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You have a reward in having intercourse with your wife.” It was said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, does one of us fulfill his desire and still get a reward for it? He said: “Yes. Tell me, if you had a child who reached maturity and then died, would you hope for reward for that?” He said: Yes. He said: “Did you create him?” He said: Rather, Allah created him. He said: “Did you guide him?” He said: Rather, Allah guided him. He said: “Did you provide for him?” He said: Rather, Allah provided for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then place it in its lawful place, keep it away from what is unlawful, and let it take its course. If Allah wills, He will give it life, and if He wills, He will cause it to die, and you will have a reward.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (4192)."},{"num":6378,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: عَلَى كُلِّ نَفْسٍ فِي كُلِّ يَوْمٍ طَلَعَتْ فِيهِ الشَّمْسُ صَدَقَةٌ مِنْهُ عَلَى نَفْسِهِ. قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، مِنْ أَيْنَ أَتَصَدَّقُ وَلَيْسَ لَنَا أَمْوَالٌ؟ قَالَ: لأنّ مِنْ أَبْوَابِ الصَّدَقَةِ التَّكْبِيرَ، وَسُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ، وَلَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، وَأَسْتَغْفِرُ اللهَ، وَتَأْمُرُ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَتَنْهَى عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ، وَتَعْزِلُ الشَّوْكَةَ عَنْ طَرِيقِ النَّاسِ وَالْعَظْمَ وَالْحَجَرَ، وَتَهْدِي الْأَعْمَى، وَتُسْمِعُ الصم وَالْأَبْكَمَ حَتَّى يَفْقَهَ، وَتُدِلُّ الْمُسْتَدِلَّ عَلَى حَاجَةٍ لَهُ قَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَكَانَهَا، وَتَسْعَى بِشِدَّةِ سَاقَيْكَ إِلَى اللهْفَانِ الْمُسْتَغِيثِ، وَتَرْفَعُ بِشِدَّةِ ذِرَاعَيْكَ مَعَ الضَّعِيفِ، كُلُّ ذَلِكَ مِنْ أَبْوَابِ الصَّدَقَةِ مِنْكَ عَلَى نَفْسِكَ، وَلَكَ فِي جِمَاعِكَ زَوْجَتَكَ أَجْرٌ قـال أَبُو ذَرٍّ: كَيْفَ يَكُونُ لِي أَجْرٌ فِي شَهْوَتِي؟! فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَرَأَيْتَ لَوْ كَانَ لَكَ وَلَدٌ فَأَدْرَكَ وَرَجَوْتَ خَيْرَهُ فَمَاتَ، أَكُنْتَ تَحْتَسِبُ بِهِ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَأَنْتَ خَلَقْتَهُ؟ قَالَ: بَلِ اللَّهُ خَلَقَهُ. قَالَ: فَأَنْتَ هَدَيْتَهُ؟ قَالَ: بَلِ اللَّهُ هَدَاهُ، قَالَ: فَأَنْتَ تَرْزُقُهُ؟ قَالَ: بَلِ اللَّهُ كَانَ يَرْزُقُهُ، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : كَذَلِكَ فَضَعْهُ فِي حَلَالِهِ وَجَنِّبْهُ حَرَامَهُ، فَإِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ أَحْيَاهُ، وَإِنْ شَاءَ أَمَاتَهُ، وَلَكَ أَجْرٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (21484) عن عبدالملك بن عمرو، حدثنا علي- يعني ابن المبارك، عن يحيى، عن زيد بن سلاّم، عن أبي سلاّم، قال: قال أبو ذر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (21484).","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr reported: Every person owes a charity on behalf of himself on every day upon which the sun rises. I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, how can I give charity when we have no wealth?” He said: “Among the doors of charity are saying ‘Allahu Akbar,’ ‘Subḥān Allah,’ ‘al-ḥamdu lillāh,’ ‘lā ilāha illā Allah,’ and ‘astaghfirullāh’; commanding what is right and forbidding what is wrong; removing a thorn, a bone, or a stone from the path of the people; guiding the blind; helping the deaf and mute understand; directing someone seeking guidance to a need whose location you know; hurrying with the strength of your legs to aid a distressed person calling for help; and using the strength of your arms to assist someone weak. All of these are doors of charity that you perform on behalf of yourself, and you also receive a reward for intercourse with your wife.” Abū Dharr asked: “How can I receive a reward for fulfilling my desire?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Suppose you had a child who reached maturity and you hoped for good from him, then he died. Would you seek reward from Allah for him?” I said: “Yes.” He asked: “Did you create him?” He replied: “Rather, Allah created him.” He asked: “Did you guide him?” He replied: “Rather, Allah guided him.” He asked: “Did you provide for him?” He replied: “Rather, Allah provided for him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Likewise, place your desire in what is lawful and keep it away from what is unlawful. If Allah wills, He gives life, and if He wills, He causes death, and you receive a reward.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (21484)."},{"num":6379,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: سُئِلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَنِ الْعَزْلِ قَالُوا: إِنَّ الْيَهُودَ تَزْعُمُ أَنَّ الْعَزْلَ هِيَ الْمَوْؤُدَةُ الصُّغْرَى قَالَ: كَذَبَتِ الْيَهُودُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1451) والبيهقي (14315) كلاهما من حديث محمد بن عمرو، ثنا أبو سلمة، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzar, Kashf al-Astar (1451), and al-Bayhaqi (7/230).","chapter_en":"What has been reported concerning withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about withdrawal. They said: The Jews claim that withdrawal is minor infanticide. He said: “The Jews have lied.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Jurisprudence of this chapter: Regarding the ruling on withdrawal, I do not know of anyone who said it is forbidden. As for it being disliked, yes, some jurists held that view. The basic principle is that it is permissible, based on what we know from the approval of the Qur’an and the Sunnah.","Women are of three types:","If she is owned, then the harm in her becoming pregnant and giving birth is that she becomes an umm walad, and an umm walad may not be sold.","If she is a female slave and bondwoman, then the harm in not practicing withdrawal from her is that if she becomes pregnant and gives birth, her child will be a slave following his mother.","If she is his free wife, then withdrawal with her is not permitted except with her permission, such as if she is ill and allows withdrawal for fear of pregnancy. But without her permission, that is not allowed, because it is her right to enjoy intimacy, become pregnant, and bear children."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1451)، والبيهقي (14315)."},{"num":6380,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جدامة بنت وهب أخت عكاشة بن وهب قالت: حضرت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وسألوه عن العزل فقال: الوأد الخفي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في النكاح (141:1442) من طريق عن عبد الله بن يزيد المقرئ، حدثنا سعيد بن أبي أيوب، حدثني أبو الأسود، عن عروة، عن عائشة، عن جدامة بنت وهب فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ماجاء في كراهية العزل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1442:141).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Regarding the Dislike of Withdrawal","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Judamah bint Wahb, the sister of ʿUkkashah ibn Wahb, said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they asked him about withdrawal, so he said: “It is hidden infanticide.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (141:1442)."},{"num":6381,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، أُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، عَنْ جُدَامَةَ بِنْتِ وَهْبٍ الأَسَدِيَّةِ، أَنَّهَا أَخْبَرَتْهَا أَنَّهَا، سَمِعَتْ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: لَقَدْ هَمَمْتُ أَنْ أَنْهَى عَنِ الْغِيلَةِ، حَتَّى ذَكَرْتُ أَنَّ الرُّومَ وَفَارِسَ يَصْنَعُونَ ذَلِكَ، فَلاَ يَضُرُّ أَوْلاَدَهُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في الرضاع (16) عن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن نوفل أنه قال: أخبرني عروة بن الزبير، عن عائشة أم المؤمنين، به.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الغيلة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Malik (16) and Muslim (1442:140).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Regarding Ghilah","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿA’ishah narrated from Judamah bint Wahb al-Asadiyyah that she informed her that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “I had intended to forbid ghilah, until I remembered that the Romans and Persians do that, and it does not harm their children.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مالك (16)."},{"num":6382,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جُدَامَةَ بِنْتِ وَهْبٍ، أُخْتِ عُكَّاشَةَ قَالَتْ: حَضَرْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ   فِي أُنَاسٍ وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: لَقَدْ هَمَمْتُ أَنْ أَنْهَى عَنِ الْغِيلَةِ، فَنَظَرْتُ فِي الرُّومِ وَفَارِسَ، فَإِذَا هُمْ يُغِيلُونَ أَوْلاَدَهُمْ، فَلاَ يَضُرُّ أَوْلاَدَهُمْ ذَلِكَ شَيْئًا. ثُمَّ سَأَلُوهُ عَنِ الْعَزْلِ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:   ذَلِكَ الْوَأْدُ الْخَفِيُّ.","زاد في رواية: ﴿وَإِذَا الْمَوْءُودَةُ سُئِلَتْ﴾[التكوير: ٨]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في النكاح (141،1442) من طريق المقرئ، حدثنا سعيد بن أبي أيوب، حدثني أبو الأسود، عن عروة، عن عائشة، عن جدامة بنت وهب فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الغيلة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1442:141).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Regarding Ghilah","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Judamah bint Wahb, the sister of ʿUkkashah, said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among some people while he was saying: “I had intended to forbid ghilah, but I looked at the Romans and Persians, and they practice ghilah with their children, yet that does not harm their children at all.” Then they asked him about withdrawal, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “That is hidden infanticide.” In one narration there is the addition: “And when the buried girl is asked” [Surat al-Takwir: 8]."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (141:1442)."},{"num":6383,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَطَاءٍ، عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سُئِلَ عَنِ الْغَيْلِ، فَقَالَ: لَوْ كَانَ ضَارًّا أَحَدًا ضَرَّ فَارِسَ وَالرُّومَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1454) عن محمد بن أبي غالب، ثنا صفوان بن صالح، ثنا عيسى بن يونس، ثنا ابن جريج، عن عطاء، عن عبد عبد الله بن عباس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الغيلة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bazzar, Kashf al-Astar (1454).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported Regarding Ghilah","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿAbbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about ghayl, and he said: “If it were harmful to anyone, it would have harmed the Persians and the Romans.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1454)."},{"num":6384,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عطاء قَالَ: حَضَرْنَا مَعَ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ جَنَازَةَ مَيْمُونَةَ بِسَرِفَ، فَقَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: هَذِهِ زَوْجَةُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَإِذَا رَفَعْتُمْ نَعْشَهَا فَلاَ تُزَعْزِعُوهَا، وَلاَ تُزَلْزِلُوهَا، وَارْفُقُوا، فَإِنَّهُ كَانَ عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تِسْعٌ، كَانَ يَقْسِمُ لِثَمَانٍ وَلاَ يَقْسِمُ لِوَاحِدَةٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5067) من طريق هشام بن يوسف، ومسلم في الرضاع (51:1465)من طريق محمد بن بكر – كلاهما عن ابن جريج قال: أخبرني عطاء، فذكره. وزاد مسلم: قال عطاء: التي لا يقسم لها صفية بنت حييّ بن أخطب.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب العدل بين الزوجات في القسم إلا من وهبت نوبتها لضرتها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5067) and Muslim (1465:51).","chapter_en":"Justice Between Wives in Allotment, Except for the One Who Gives Her Turn to Her Co-Wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAta’ said: We attended the funeral of Maymunah at Sarif with Ibn ʿAbbas, and Ibn ʿAbbas said: This is the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, so when you lift her bier, do not shake it or jolt it; be gentle, for the Prophet ﷺ had nine wives. He used to divide his time among eight and did not divide for one of them."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى: (فَانكِحُوا مَا طَابَ لَكُم مِّنَ النِّسَاءِ مَثْنَىٰ وَثُلَاثَ وَرُبَاعَ ۖ فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلَّا تَعْدِلُوا فَوَاحِدَةً أَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ أَدْنَىٰ أَلَّا تَعُولُوا) [النساء: ٣]\\n\\nوقال تعالى: (وَلَن تَسْتَطِيعُوا أَن تَعْدِلُوا بَيْنَ النِّسَاءِ وَلَوْ حَرَصْتُمْ فَلَا تَمِيلُوا كُلَّ الْمَيْلِ فَتَذَرُوهَا كَالْمُعَلَّقَةِ) [النساء: ١٢٩] قال ابن عباس: أي في الحب والجماع."],"en":["Allah the Exalted said: “Marry those women who are lawful for you, two, three, or four; but if you fear that you will not be just, then one, or those whom your right hands possess. That is more likely that you will not commit injustice.” [Surat al-Nisa’: 3]\\n\\nAnd He said: “You will never be able to be completely just between wives, even if you are eager. So do not incline completely toward one and leave another hanging.” [Surat al-Nisa’: 129]\\n\\nIbn ʿAbbas said: This means in love and intercourse."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5067)، ومسلم (51:1465)."},{"num":6385,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ صَفِيَّةَ بِنْتِ حُيَيٍّ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَجَّ بِنِسَائِهِ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ فِي بَعْضِ الطَّرِيقِ نَزَلَ رَجُلٌ، فَسَاقَ بِهِنَّ، فَأَسْرَعَ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَذَاكَ سَوْقُكَ بِالْقَوَارِيرِ يَعْنِي النِّسَاءَ، فَبَيْنَا هُمْ يَسِيرُونَ بَرَكَ بِصَفِيَّةَ بِنْتِ حُيَيٍّ جَمَلُهَا، وَكَانَتْ مِنْ أَحْسَنِهِنَّ ظَهْرًا، فَبَكَتْ، وَجَاءَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ أُخْبِرَ بِذَلِكَ، فَجَعَلَ يَمْسَحُ دُمُوعَهَا بِيَدِهِ، وَجَعَلَتْ تَزْدَادُ بُكَاءً، وَهُوَ يَنْهَاهَا، فَلَمَّا أَكْثَرَتْ، زَبَرَهَا، وَانْتَهَرَهَا، وَأَمَرَ النَّاسَ بِالنُّزُولِ، فَنَزَلُوا، وَلَمْ يَكُنْ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يَنْزِلَ، قَالَتْ: فَنَزَلُوا، وَكَانَ يَوْمِي، فَلَمَّا نَزَلُوا، ضُرِبَ خِبَاءُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَدَخَلَ فِيهِ، قَالَتْ: فَلَمْ أَدْرِ عَلَامَ أُهْجَمُ مِنْ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَخَشِيتُ أَنْ يَكُونَ فِي نَفْسِهِ شَيْءٌ مِنِّي، فَانْطَلَقْتُ إِلَى عَائِشَةَ، فَقُلْتُ لَهَا: تَعْلَمِينَ أَنِّي لَمْ أَكُنْ أَبِيعُ يَوْمِي مِنْ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِشَيْءٍ أَبَدًا، وَإِنِّي قَدْ وَهَبْتُ يَوْمِي لَكِ عَلَى أَنْ تُرْضِي رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَنِّي، قَالَتْ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: فَأَخَذَتْ عَائِشَةُ خِمَارًا لَهَا، قَدْ ثَرَدَتْهُ بِزَعْفَرَانٍ، فَرَشَّتْهُ بِالمَاءِ لِيُذَكِّيَ رِيحَهُ، ثُمَّ لَبِسَتْ ثِيَابَهَا، ثُمَّ انْطَلَقَتْ إِلَى رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَرَفَعَتْ طَرَفَ الْخِبَاءِ، فَقَالَ لَهَا: مَا لَكِ يَا عَائِشَةُ؟ إِنَّ هَذَا لَيْسَ بِيَوْمِكِ، قَالَتْ: ذَلِكَ فَضْلُ الله يُؤْتِيهِ مَنْ يَشَاءُ، فَقَالَ مَعَ أَهْلِهِ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ عِنْدَ الرَّوَاحِ، قَالَ لِزَيْنَبَ بِنْتِ جَحْشٍ: يَا زَيْنَبُ أَفْقِرِي أُخْتَكِ صَفِيَّةَ جَمَلًا، وَكَانَتْ مِنْ أَكْثَرِهِنَّ ظَهْرًا، فَقَالَتْ: أَنَا أُفْقِرُ يَهُودِيَّتَكَ، فَغَضِبَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ سَمِعَ ذَلِكَ مِنْهَا، فَهَجَرَهَا، فَلَمْ يُكَلِّمْهَا حَتَّى قَدِمَ مَكَّةَ، وَأَيَّامَ مِنًى فِي سَفَرِهِ، حَتَّى رَجَعَ إِلَى المَدِينَةِ، وَالمُحَرَّمَ، وَصَفَرَ، فَلَمْ يَأْتِهَا وَلَمْ يَقْسِمْ لَهَا، وَيَئِسَتْ مِنْهُ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ شَهْرُ رَبِيعٍ الْأَوَّلِ دَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا، فَرَأَتْ ظِلَّهُ، فَقَالَتْ: إِنَّ هَذَا لَظِلُّ رَجُلٍ، وَمَا يَدْخُلُ عَلَيَّ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَمَنْ هَذَا؟ فَدَخَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَمَّا رَأَتْهُ، قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ الله مَا أَدْرِي مَا أَصْنَعُ حِينَ دَخَلْتَ عَلَيَّ، قَالَتْ: وَكَانَتْ لَهَا جَارِيَةٌ، وَكَانَتْ تَخْبَؤُهَا مِنْ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَتْ: فُلَانَةُ لَكَ، فَمَشَى النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى سَرِيرِ زَيْنَبَ، وَكَانَ قَدْ رُفِعَ، فَوَضَعَهُ بِيَدِهِ، ثُمَّ أَصَابَ أَهْلَهُ، وَرَضِيَ عَنْهُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (26866) عن عبد الرزاق، قال: حدثنا جعفر بن سليمان، عن ثابت، قال: حدثتني شميسة أو سمية -قال عبد الرزاق هو في كتابي سمية- عن صفية بنت حُيي فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب العدل بين الزوجات في القسم إلا من وهبت نوبتها لضرتها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imam Ahmad (26866).","chapter_en":"Justice Between Wives in Allotment, Except for the One Who Gives Her Turn to Her Co-Wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Safiyyah bint Huyayy narrated that the Prophet ﷺ performed Hajj with his wives. During part of the journey, a man came down and drove them on quickly, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Take care when driving these glass vessels,” meaning the women. While they were traveling, Safiyyah bint Huyayy’s camel knelt down, and she was one of those with the best mounts, so she cried. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came when he was informed of that and began wiping her tears with his hand, but she cried even more while he was trying to calm her. When she cried excessively, he rebuked her and scolded her, then ordered the people to halt, though he had not intended to stop. She said: So they stopped, and it was my day. The Prophet’s tent was pitched and he entered it. She said: I did not know why the Messenger of Allah had withdrawn from me, and I feared that something about me was in his heart. So I went to ʿA’ishah and said to her: You know that I would never give up my day with the Messenger of Allah for anything, but I have given my day to you on condition that you make the Messenger of Allah pleased with me. She said: Yes. She said: Then ʿA’ishah took a head-covering of hers which she had perfumed with saffron, sprinkled it with water so that its fragrance would be stronger, then put on her clothes and went to the Messenger of Allah and lifted the edge of the tent. He said to her: “What is the matter, O ʿA’ishah? This is not your day.” She said: That is the bounty of Allah; He gives it to whom He wills. So he remained with his family. Then when it was time to set out, he said to Zaynab bint Jahsh: “O Zaynab, lend your sister Safiyyah a camel.” Zaynab had more riding animals than any of them, but she said: Shall I lend my camel to your Jewish woman? The Prophet became angry when he heard that from her, and he forsook her and did not speak to her until he arrived in Makkah, and through the days of Mina on his journey, then until he returned to Madinah through Muharram and Safar. He did not go to her and did not allot her a turn, and she despaired of him. Then when the month of Rabiʿ al-Awwal came, he entered upon her. She saw his shadow and said: This is surely the shadow of a man, but the Prophet does not enter upon me, so who is this? Then the Prophet entered, and when she saw him, she said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not know what to do now that you have entered upon me. She said: She had a slave-girl whom she used to hide from the Prophet, so she said: So-and-so is yours. Then the Prophet went to Zaynab’s bed, which had been raised, lowered it with his own hand, then went in to his wife, and became pleased with them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (26866)."},{"num":6386,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بْنِ مَالِكٍ حَدَّثَهُمْ أَنَّ نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ يَطُوفُ عَلَى نِسَائِهِ فِي اللَّيْلَةِ الْوَاحِدَةِ، وَلَهُ يَوْمَئِذٍ تِسْعُ نِسْوَةٍ.","وَفِي رواية: كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم يَدُورُ عَلَى نِسَائِهِ فِي السَّاعَةِ الوَاحِدَةِ مِنَ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَهُنَّ إِحْدَى عَشْرَةَ. قَالَ: قُلْتُ لِأَنَسٍ: أَوَ كَانَ يُطِيقُهُ؟ قَالَ: كُنَّا نَتَحَدَّثُ أَنَّهُ أُعْطِيَ قُوَّةَ ثَلَاثِينَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5215) عن عبدالأعلى بن حماد، حدّثنا يزيد بن زريع، حدثنا سعيد، عن قتادة، أن أنس بن مالك حدّثهم، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب العدل بين الزوجات في القسم إلا من وهبت نوبتها لضرتها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5215) and (268).","chapter_en":"Justice Between Wives in Allotment, Except for the One Who Gives Her Turn to Her Co-Wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Malik said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to go around to his wives in a single night, and at that time he had nine wives. In another narration: The Prophet ﷺ used to go around to his wives in a single hour of the night and day, and they were eleven. I said to Anas: Was he able to do that? He said: We used to say that he had been given the strength of thirty men."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (5215)."},{"num":6387,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ:  كَانَ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تِسْعُ نِسْوَةٍ، فَكَانَ إِذَا قَسَمَ بَيْنَهُنَّ لَا يَنْتَهِي إِلَى الْمَرْأَةِ الْأُولَى إِلَّا فِي تِسْعٍ، فَكُنَّ يَجْتَمِعْنَ كُلَّ لَيْلَةٍ فِي بَيْتِ الَّتِي يَأْتِيهَا، فَكَانَ فِي بَيْتِ عَائِشَةَ، فَجَاءَتْ زَيْنَبُ فَمَدَّ يَدَهُ إِلَيْهَا، فَقَالَتْ: هَذِهِ زَيْنَبُ، فَكَفَّ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَدَهُ، فَتَقَاوَلَتَا حَتَّى اسْتَخَبَتَا، وَأُقِيمَتِ الصَّلَاةُ. فَمَرَّ أَبُو بَكْرٍ عَلَى ذَلِكَ، فَسَمِعَ أَصْوَاتَهُمَا، فَقَالَ: اخْرُجْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِلَى الصَّلَاةِ، وَاحْثُ فِي أَفْوَاهِهِنَّ التُّرَابَ، فَخَرَجَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: الْآنَ يَقْضِي النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صَلَاتَهُ، فَيَجِيءُ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَيَفْعَلُ بِي وَيَفْعَلُ، فَلَمَّا قَضَى النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صَلَاتَهُ، أَتَاهَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَقَالَ لَهَا قَوْلًا شَدِيدًا، وَقَالَ: أَتَصْنَعِينَ هَذَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الرضاع (1462) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، حدّثنا شبابة بن سوّار، حدّثنا سليمان بن المغيرة، عن ثابت، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب العدل بين الزوجات في القسم إلا من وهبت نوبتها لضرتها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1462).","chapter_en":"Justice Between Wives in Allotment, Except for the One Who Gives Her Turn to Her Co-Wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas said: The Prophet ﷺ had nine wives. When he divided his time among them, he would not return to the first wife until nine days had passed. They used to gather every night in the house of the one whose turn it was. It happened in the house of ʿA’ishah. Then Zaynab came, and the Prophet ﷺ extended his hand toward her. ʿA’ishah said: This is Zaynab. So the Prophet ﷺ withdrew his hand. Then the two exchanged words until their voices rose. The prayer was called, and Abu Bakr passed by and heard their voices, so he said: Go out, O Messenger of Allah, to the prayer, and throw dust into their mouths. The Prophet went out, and ʿA’ishah said: Now the Prophet will finish his prayer, and then Abu Bakr will come and do such-and-such to me. When the Prophet finished his prayer, Abu Bakr came to her, spoke to her harshly, and said: Do you do this?"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1462)."},{"num":6388,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذَا أَرَادَ سَفَرًا أَقْرَعَ بَيْنَ نِسَائِهِ، فَأَيَّتُهُنَّ خَرَجَ سَهْمُهَا خَرَجَ بِهَا مَعَهُ، وَكَانَ يَقْسِمُ لِكُلِّ امْرَأَةٍ مِنْهُنَّ يَوْمَهَا وَلَيْلَتَهَا، غَيْرَ أَنَّ سَوْدَةَ بِنْتَ زَمْعَةَ وَهَبَتْ يَوْمَهَا وَلَيْلَتَهَا، لِعَائِشَةَ زَوْجِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَبْتَغِي بِذَلِكَ رِضَا رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الهبة (2593) عن حِبّان بن موسى، أخبرنا عبد الله، أخبرنا يونس، عن الزهري، عن عروة، عن عائشة، قالت: فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب العدل بين الزوجات في القسم إلا من وهبت نوبتها لضرتها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2593).","chapter_en":"Justice Between Wives in Allotment, Except for the One Who Gives Her Turn to Her Co-Wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾishah reported: Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives. Whichever wife’s lot was drawn, he would take her with him. He would allot each of his wives her own day and night, except that Sawdah bint Zamʿah gave her day and night to ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, seeking thereby the pleasure of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2593)."},{"num":6389,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ:  مَا رَأَيْتُ امْرَأَةً أَحَبَّ إِلَيَّ أَنْ أَكُونَ فِي مِسْلَاخِهَا مِنْ سَوْدَةَ بِنْتِ زَمْعَةَ مِنِ امْرَأَةٍ فِيهَا حِدَّةٌ، قَالَتْ: فَلَمَّا كَبِرَتْ جَعَلَتْ يَوْمَهَا مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِعَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَدْ جَعَلْتُ يَوْمِي مِنْكَ لِعَائِشَةَ، فَكَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقْسِمُ لِعَائِشَةَ يَوْمَيْنِ: يَوْمَهَا، وَيَوْمَ سَوْدَةَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5212)، ومسلم في الرضاع (47:1463) كلاهما من طريق هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته، واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب العدل بين الزوجات في القسم إلا من وهبت نوبتها لضرتها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5212) and Muslim (1463:47). The wording is from Muslim.","chapter_en":"Justice Between Wives in Allotment, Except for the One Who Gives Her Turn to Her Co-Wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿA’ishah said: I never saw a woman in whose place I would have preferred to be more than Sawdah bint Zamʿah, a woman who had some sharpness in her nature. When she grew older, she gave her day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ʿA’ishah. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given my day with you to ʿA’ishah. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to allot two days to ʿA’ishah: her own day and the day of Sawdah."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Her words, “in her skin,” mean: in her place, meaning that I would be she."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9411],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5212)، ومسلم (47:1463)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":6390,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاذَةَ، عَنْ عَائِشَةَ ـ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ يَسْتَأْذِنُ فِي يَوْمِ الْمَرْأَةِ مِنَّا، بَعْدَ أَنْ أُنْزِلَتْ هَذِهِ الآيَةُ ﴿تُرْجِئُ مَنْ تَشَاءُ مِنْهُنَّ وَتُؤْوِي إِلَيْكَ مَنْ تَشَاءُ وَمَنِ ابْتَغَيْتَ مِمَّنْ عَزَلْتَ فَلاَ جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكَ﴾ [سورة الأحزاب: 51]}. فَقُلْتُ لَهَا: مَا كُنْتِ تَقُولِينَ؟ قَالَتْ: كُنْتُ أَقُولُ لَهُ: إِنْ كَانَ ذَاكَ إِلَىَّ فَإِنِّي لاَ أُرِيدُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَنْ أُوثِرَ عَلَيْكَ أَحَدًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4789) ومسلم في الطلاق (1476) كلاهما من حديث عاصم الأحول، عن معاذة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب العدل بين الزوجات في القسم إلا من وهبت نوبتها لضرتها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (4789) and Muslim (1476).","chapter_en":"Justice Between Wives in Allotment, Except for the One Who Gives Her Turn to Her Co-Wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿadhah narrated from ʿA’ishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to ask permission on the day of each one of us, after this verse had been revealed: “You may defer whom you will of them and take to yourself whom you will, and whomever you desire of those you had set aside—there is no blame upon you.” [al-Ahzab: 51] I said to her: What did you used to say? She said: I used to say to him: If that were left to me, then, O Messenger of Allah, I would not wish to prefer anyone over you."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[13090],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4789)، ومسلم (1476)."},{"num":6391,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: يَا ابْنَ أُخْتِي كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لاَ يُفضّل بَعْضَنَا عَلَى بَعْضٍ فِي الْقَسْمِ، مِنْ مُكْثِهِ عِنْدَنَا، وَكَانَ قلّ يَوْمٌ إِلاَّ وَهُوَ يَطُوفُ عَلَيْنَا جَمِيعًا، فَيَدْنُو مِنْ كُلِّ امْرَأَةٍ مِنْ غَيْرِ مَسِيسٍ حَتَّى يَبْلُغَ إِلَى الَّتِي هُوَ يَوْمُهَا فَيَبِيتُ عِنْدَهَا. وَلْقَدْ قَالَتْ سَوْدَةُ بِنْتُ زَمْعَةَ حِينَ أَسَنَّتْ، وَفَرِقَتْ أَنْ يُفَارِقَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ يَوْمِي لِعَائِشَةَ، فَقَبِلَ ذَلِكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْهَا. قَالَتْ: نَقُولُ فِي ذَلِكَ: أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عزوجل وَفِي أَشْبَاهِهَا أُرَاهُ قَالَ: ﴿وَإِنِ امْرَأَةٌ خَافَتْ مِنْ بَعْلِهَا نُشُوزًا﴾ [النساء: ١٢٨]."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2135) ومن طريقه البيهقي (13434) والحاكم (2760) كلاهما من طريق أحمد بن يونس، حدثنا عبد الرحمن بن أبي الزناد، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه قال: قالت عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب العدل بين الزوجات في القسم إلا من وهبت نوبتها لضرتها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2135), and through him al-Bayhaqi (7/47), and al-Hakim (2/186).","chapter_en":"Justice Between Wives in Allotment, Except for the One Who Gives Her Turn to Her Co-Wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿA’ishah said: O son of my sister, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not favor some of us over others in how long he stayed with us when dividing his time. There was hardly a day when he would not go around to all of us, drawing near to each woman without intimacy, until he reached the one whose day it was, and then he would spend the night with her. Sawdah bint Zamʿah, when she grew old and feared that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ might separate from her, said: O Messenger of Allah, my day is for ʿA’ishah. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted that from her. She said: We say that regarding this, and similar cases, Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed, as I think: “And if a woman fears ill-treatment or aversion from her husband…” [al-Nisa’: 128]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2135)، ومن طريقه البيهقي (13434)، والحاكم (2760)."},{"num":6392,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: تُوُفِّيَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَعِنْدَهُ تِسْعُ نِسْوَةٍ يُصِيبُهُنَّ إِلاَّ سَوْدَةَ فَإِنَّهَا وَهَبَتْ يَوْمَهَا وَلَيْلَتَهَا لِعَائِشَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3197) عن إبراهيم بن يعقوب، قال: ثنا ابن أبي مريم، قال: أخبرنا سفيان قال: حدثني عمرو بن دينار، عن عطاء، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب العدل بين الزوجات في القسم إلا من وهبت نوبتها لضرتها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasa’i (3197).","chapter_en":"Justice Between Wives in Allotment, Except for the One Who Gives Her Turn to Her Co-Wife","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he had nine wives with whom he had marital relations, except Sawdah, for she had given her day and night to ʿA’ishah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي (3197)."},{"num":6393,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ كَانَتْ لَهُ امْرَأَتَانِ يَمِيلُ مَعَ إِحْدَاهُمَا عَلَى الأُخْرَى، جَاءَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَأَحَدُ شِقَّيْهِ سَاقِطٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2133) والترمذي (1141) والنسائي (3942) وابن ماجة (1969) وابن الجارود (722) وصحّحه ابن حبان (4207) والحاكم (2/186) كلهم من حديث همام بن يحيى، عن قتادة، عن النضر بن أنس، عن بشير بن نَهيك، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء فيمن لم يعدل بين نسائه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abu Dawud (2133), al-Tirmidhi (1141), al-Nasa’i (3942), Ibn Majah (1969), and Ibn al-Jarud (722).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported About One Who Does Not Deal Justly Between His Wives","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has two wives and inclines toward one over the other will come on the Day of Resurrection with one side of his body fallen.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His words, “inclines toward one over the other,” mean in the rights of companionship, such as food, drink, and clothing, not the inclination of the heart, for hearts are not under one’s control."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2133)، والترمذي (1141)، والنسائي (3942)، وابن ماجه (1969)، وابن الجارود (722)."},{"num":6394,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا {وَإِنِ امْرَأَةٌ خَافَتْ مِنْ بَعْلِهَا نُشُوزًا أَوْ إِعْرَاضًا} قَالَتْ: هِيَ الْمَرْأَةُ تَكُونُ عِنْدَ الرَّجُلِ، لاَ يَسْتَكْثِرُ مِنْهَا، فَيُرِيدُ طَلاَقَهَا، وَيَتَزَوَّجُ غَيْرَهَا، تَقُولُ لَهُ: أَمْسِكْنِي وَلاَ تُطَلِّقْنِي، ثُمَّ تَزَوَّجْ غَيْرِي، فَأَنْتَ فِي حِلٍّ مِنَ النَّفَقَةِ عَلَىَّ وَالْقِسْمَةِ لِي، فَذَلِكَ قَوْلُهُ تَعَالَى: ﴿فَلاَ جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَا أَنْ يَصَّالَحَا بَيْنَهُمَا صُلْحًا وَالصُّلْحُ خَيْرٌ﴾ [سورة النساء: 128]}."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5206) عن ابن سلام، أخبرنا أبو معاوية، عن هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته. ورواه مسلم في التفسير (3021) من وجهين آخرين عن هشام مختصراً.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في تصالح الزوجين على عدم النفقة والقسمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5206) and Muslim (3021).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported About a Husband and Wife Reconciling Over Waiving Maintenance and Division","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":33,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿA’ishah said concerning the verse, “And if a woman fears ill-treatment or aversion from her husband…” [al-Nisa’: 128]: It refers to a woman who is with a man who no longer has much desire for her, so he wants to divorce her and marry another. She says to him: Keep me and do not divorce me, then marry someone else; you are released from spending on me and from dividing your time for me. That is the meaning of His saying, Exalted is He: “Then there is no sin upon them if they make terms of settlement between them, and settlement is best.” [al-Nisa’: 128]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5206)، ومسلم (3021)."},{"num":6395,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس قال: خشيت سودة أن يُطلِّقها النبي صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فقالت: لا تُطلقني، وأمسِكني، واجعلْ يومي لعائشة. ففعل. فنزلت: ﴿فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَا أَنْ يُصْلِحَا بَيْنَهُمَا صُلْحًا وَالصُّلْحُ خَيْرٌ﴾ [ النساء: ١٢٨]."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3040) حدثنا محمد بن المثنى، حدثنا أبو داود الطيالسي، حدثنا سليمان بن معاذ، عن سماك، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره. والحديث في مسند أبي داود (2805) ومن طريقه أخرجه أيضا البيهقي (14735)","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في تصالح الزوجين على عدم النفقة والقسمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (3040) and al-Bayhaqi (7/297). Al-Tirmidhi said: “Hasan sahih gharib.”","chapter_en":"What Has Been Reported About a Husband and Wife Reconciling Over Waiving Maintenance and Division","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":33,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbas said: Sawdah feared that the Prophet ﷺ might divorce her, so she said: Do not divorce me; keep me, and give my day to ʿA’ishah. So he did that. Then the verse was revealed: “Then there is no sin upon them if they make terms of settlement between them, and settlement is best.” [al-Nisa’: 128]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3040)، والبيهقي (14735). قال الترمذي: “حسن صحيح غريب”."},{"num":6396,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، عَنْ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ دَخَلَ عَلَى حَفْصَةَ، فَقَالَ: يَا بُنَيَّةِ لاَ يَغُرَّنَّكِ هَذِهِ الَّتِي أَعْجَبَهَا حُسْنُهَا حُبُّ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِيَّاهَا ـ يُرِيدُ عَائِشَةَ ـ فَقَصَصْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَتَبَسَّمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: أخرجه البخاري في النكاح (5218) عن عبد العزيز بن عبدالله، حدثنا سليمان، عن يحيى، عن عُبيد بن حُنين، سمع ابن عباس، فذكره. وأخرجه مسلم في الطلاق (1479/31) من وجه آخر عن سليمان بن بلال بإسناده مطولا.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب جواز حب الرجل بعض زوجاته أكثر من بعض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhari (5218) and Muslim (1479:31).","chapter_en":"The Permissibility of a Man Loving Some of His Wives More Than Others","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbas narrated from ʿUmar that he entered upon Hafsah and said: O my daughter, do not let that one whose beauty and the Messenger of Allah’s love for her have impressed her deceive you — meaning ʿA’ishah. I related that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he smiled."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: أخرجه البخاري (5218)، ومسلم (1479/31)."},{"num":6397,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ زوج النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وآله وَسَلَّمَ قَالَتْ:  أَرْسَلَ أَزْوَاجُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَاطِمَةَ، بِنْتَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَاسْتَأْذَنَتْ عَلَيْهِ وَهُوَ مُضْطَجِعٌ مَعِي فِي مِرْطِي. فَأَذِنَ لَهَا، فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ أَزْوَاجَكَ أَرْسَلْنَنِي إِلَيْكَ يَسْأَلْنَكَ الْعَدْلَ فِي ابْنَةِ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ، - وَأَنَا سَاكِتَةٌ. قَالَتْ: فَقَالَ لَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَيْ بُنَيَّةُ، أَلَسْتِ تُحِبِّينَ مَا أُحِبُّ؟ فَقَالَتْ: بَلَى، قَالَ: فَأَحِبِّي هَذِهِ. قَالَتْ: فَقَامَتْ فَاطِمَةُ حِينَ سَمِعَتْ ذَلِكَ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَرَجَعَتْ إِلَى أَزْوَاجِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَخْبَرَتْهُنَّ بِالَّذِي قَالَتْ. وَبِالَّذِي قَالَ لَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْنَ لَهَا: مَا نُرَاكِ أَغْنَيْتِ عَنَّا مِنْ شَيْءٍ، فَارْجِعِي إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقُولِي لَهُ: إِنَّ أَزْوَاجَكَ يَنْشُدْنَكَ الْعَدْلَ فِي ابْنَةِ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ. فَقَالَتْ فَاطِمَةُ: وَاللهِ! لَا أُكَلِّمُهُ فِيهَا أَبَدًا. قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: فَأَرْسَلَ أَزْوَاجُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ زَيْنَبَ بِنْتَ جَحْشٍ، زَوْجَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهِيَ الَّتِي كَانَتْ تُسَامِينِي مِنْهُنَّ فِي الْمَنْزِلَةِ عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَلَمْ أَرَ امْرَأَةً قَطُّ خَيْرًا فِي الدِّينِ مِنْ زَيْنَبَ، وَأَتْقَى لِلهِ. وَأَصْدَقَ حَدِيثًا. وَأَوْصَلَ لِلرَّحِمِ. وَأَعْظَمَ صَدَقَةً، وَأَشَدَّ ابْتِذَالًا لِنَفْسِهَا فِي الْعَمَلِ الَّذِي تَصَدَّقُ بِهِ، وَتَقَرَّبُ بِهِ إِلَى اللَّهِ تَعَالَى، مَا عَدَا سَوْرَةً مِنْ حِدَّةٍ كَانَتْ فِيهَا تُسْرِعُ مِنْهَا الْفَيْئَةَ. قَالَتْ: فَاسْتَأْذَنَتْ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَعَ عَائِشَةَ فِي مِرْطِهَا. عَلَى الْحَالَةِ الَّتِي دَخَلَتْ فَاطِمَةُ عَلَيْهَا وَهُوَ بِهَا، فَأَذِنَ لَهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ أَزْوَاجَكَ أَرْسَلْنَنِي إِلَيْكَ يَسْأَلْنَكَ الْعَدْلَ فِي ابْنَةِ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ! قَالَتْ: ثُمَّ وَقَعَتْ بِي. فَاسْتَطَالَتْ عَلَيَّ، وَأَنَا أَرْقُبُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَأَرْقُبُ طَرْفَهُ، هَلْ يَأْذَنُ لِي فِيهَا؟ قَالَتْ: فَلَمْ تَبْرَحْ زَيْنَبُ حَتَّى عَرَفْتُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَا يَكْرَهُ أَنْ أَنْتَصِرَ. قَالَتْ: فَلَمَّا وَقَعْتُ بِهَا لَمْ أَنْشَبْهَا حَتَّى أَنْحَيْتُ عَلَيْهَا. قَالَتْ: فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَتَبَسَّمَ: إِنَّهَا ابْنَةُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2442) من طريق يعقوب بن إبراهيم بن سعد، حدثني أبي، عن صالح، عن ابن شهاب، أخبرني محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن الحارث بن هشام، عن عائشة، فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب جواز حب الرجل بعض زوجاته أكثر من بعض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2442).","chapter_en":"The Permissibility of a Man Loving Some of His Wives More Than Others","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿA’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: The wives of the Prophet ﷺ sent Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She asked permission to enter while he was lying with me under my wrap, and he permitted her. She said: O Messenger of Allah, your wives have sent me to ask you to be fair regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah. I remained silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “O my daughter, do you not love whom I love?” She said: Yes. He said: “Then love this one.” So Fatimah got up when she heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She returned to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ and informed them of what she had said and what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said to her. They said to her: We do not think you helped us at all. Go back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him: Your wives ask you for fairness regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah. Fatimah said: By Allah, I will never speak to him about her again. ʿA’ishah said: Then the wives of the Prophet ﷺ sent Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and she was the one among them who rivaled me in standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I never saw a woman better in religion than Zaynab, more mindful of Allah, more truthful in speech, more dutiful to kinship ties, greater in charity, and more willing to exert herself in deeds by which she gave charity and sought nearness to Allah the Exalted — except for some sharpness in her nature from which she would quickly return. She asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was with ʿA’ishah under her wrap, in the same condition in which Fatimah had found him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her permission. She said: O Messenger of Allah, your wives have sent me to ask you to be fair regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah. Then she began attacking me and speaking at length against me, while I watched the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and watched his eyes to see whether he would allow me to answer her. Zaynab did not stop until I knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not dislike my defending myself. Then once I turned on her, I quickly silenced her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said: “She is the daughter of Abu Bakr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2442)."},{"num":6398,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ: رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا أَنَّ نِسَاءَ، رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كُنَّ حِزْبَيْنِ، فَحِزْبٌ فِيهِ عَائِشَةُ وَحَفْصَةُ وَصَفِيَّةُ وَسَوْدَةُ، وَالْحِزْبُ الآخَرُ أُمُّ سَلَمَةَ وَسَائِرُ نِسَاءِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَكَانَ الْمُسْلِمُونَ قَدْ عَلِمُوا حُبَّ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَائِشَةَ، فَإِذَا كَانَتْ عِنْدَ أَحَدِهِمْ هَدِيَّةٌ، يُرِيدُ أَنْ يُهْدِيَهَا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَخَّرَهَا، حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَيْتِ عَائِشَةَ بَعَثَ صَاحِبُ الْهَدِيَّةِ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَيْتِ عَائِشَةَ، فَكَلَّمَ حِزْبُ أُمِّ سَلَمَةَ، فَقُلْنَ لَهَا: كَلِّمِي رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ، فَيَقُولُ: مَنْ أَرَادَ أَنْ يُهْدِيَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ هَدِيَّةً فَلْيُهْدِهِ إِلَيْهِ حَيْثُ كَانَ مِنْ بُيُوتِ نِسَائِهِ، فَكَلَّمَتْهُ أُمُّ سَلَمَةَ بِمَا قُلْنَ، فَلَمْ يَقُلْ لَهَا شَيْئًا، فَسَأَلْنَهَا. فَقَالَتْ: مَا قَالَ لِي شَيْئًا. فَقُلْنَ لَهَا: فَكَلِّمِيهِ. قَالَتْ: فَكَلَّمَتْهُ حِينَ دَارَ إِلَيْهَا أَيْضًا، فَلَمْ يَقُلْ لَهَا شَيْئًا، فَسَأَلْنَهَا. فَقَالَتْ: مَا قَالَ لِي شَيْئًا. فَقُلْنَ لَهَا: كَلِّمِيهِ حَتَّى يُكَلِّمَكِ. فَدَارَ إِلَيْهَا فَكَلَّمَتْهُ. فَقَالَ لَهَا: لاَ تُؤْذِينِي فِي عَائِشَةَ، فَإِنَّ الْوَحْىَ لَمْ يَأْتِنِي، وَأَنَا فِي ثَوْبِ امْرَأَةٍ إِلاَّ عَائِشَةَ. قَالَتْ: فَقَالَتْ: أَتُوبُ إِلَى اللَّهِ مِنْ أَذَاكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. ثُمَّ إِنَّهُنَّ دَعَوْنَ فَاطِمَةَ بِنْتَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَرْسَلْنَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تَقُولُ: إِنَّ نِسَاءَكَ يَنْشُدْنَكَ اللَّهَ الْعَدْلَ فِي بِنْتِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ. فَكَلَّمَتْهُ. فَقَالَ: يَا بُنَيَّةُ، أَلاَ تُحِبِّينَ مَا أُحِبُّ. قَالَتْ: بَلَى. فَرَجَعَتْ إِلَيْهِنَّ، فَأَخْبَرَتْهُنَّ. فَقُلْنَ ارْجِعِي إِلَيْهِ. فَأَبَتْ أَنْ تَرْجِعَ، فَأَرْسَلْنَ زَيْنَبَ بِنْتَ جَحْشٍ، فَأَتَتْهُ فَأَغْلَظَتْ، وَقَالَتْ: إِنَّ نِسَاءَكَ يَنْشُدْنَكَ اللَّهَ الْعَدْلَ فِي بِنْتِ ابْنِ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ. فَرَفَعَتْ صَوْتَهَا، حَتَّى تَنَاوَلَتْ عَائِشَةَ. وَهْىَ قَاعِدَةٌ، فَسَبَّتْهَا، حَتَّى إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَيَنْظُرُ إِلَى عَائِشَةَ هَلْ تَكَلَّمُ؟ قَالَ: فَتَكَلَّمَتْ عَائِشَةُ تَرُدُّ عَلَى زَيْنَبَ، حَتَّى أَسْكَتَتْهَا. قَالَتْ: فَنَظَرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى عَائِشَةَ، وَقَالَ: إِنَّهَا بِنْتُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الهبة (2581) عن إسماعيل، قال حدثني أخي، عن سليمان، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب جواز حب الرجل بعض زوجاته أكثر من بعض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhari (2581).","chapter_en":"The Permissibility of a Man Loving Some of His Wives More Than Others","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿA’ishah said: The wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were two parties. One party included ʿA’ishah, Hafsah, Safiyyah, and Sawdah; and the other party was Umm Salamah and the rest of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Muslims knew of the Messenger of Allah’s love for ʿA’ishah, so if one of them had a gift he wanted to present to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would delay it until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the house of ʿA’ishah. Then the giver would send the gift to the Messenger of Allah while he was in the house of ʿA’ishah. The party of Umm Salamah spoke to her and said: Speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he may tell the people: Whoever wants to give a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ should give it to him wherever he may be among the houses of his wives. Umm Salamah spoke to him with what they had said, but he said nothing to her. They asked her, and she said: He said nothing to me. They said: Speak to him again. She said: So I spoke to him again when it was her turn, and he said nothing to me. They asked her, and she said: He said nothing to me. They said: Keep speaking to him until he answers you. So when it was again her turn, she spoke to him, and he said to her: “Do not hurt me concerning ʿA’ishah, for revelation has never come to me while I was under the covering of any woman except ʿA’ishah.” She said: So Umm Salamah said: I repent to Allah from hurting you, O Messenger of Allah. Then they called Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she sent word to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: Your wives ask you by Allah to be fair regarding the daughter of Abu Bakr. He said to her: “O my daughter, do you not love whom I love?” She said: Yes. Then she returned to them and informed them. They said to her: Go back to him. But she refused to return. Then they sent Zaynab bint Jahsh, who came and spoke harshly, saying: Your wives ask you by Allah to be fair regarding the daughter of Ibn Abi Quhafah. She raised her voice until she turned on ʿA’ishah while she was sitting and insulted her, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was looking at ʿA’ishah to see whether she would respond. Then ʿA’ishah answered Zaynab until she silenced her. The Prophet ﷺ looked at ʿA’ishah and said: “She is the daughter of Abu Bakr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[5977],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2581)."},{"num":6399,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: مَا عَلِمْتُ حَتَّى دَخَلَتْ عَلَىَّ زَيْنَبُ بِغَيْرِ إِذْنٍ، وَهِيَ غَضْبَى. ثُمَّ قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَحَسْبُكَ إِذَا قَلَبَتْ لَكَ بُنَيَّةُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ ذُرَيْعَتَيْهَا. ثُمَّ أَقْبَلَتْ عَلَىَّ. فَأَعْرَضْتُ عَنْهَا. حَتَّى قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: دُونَكِ فَانْتَصِرِي. فَأَقْبَلْتُ عَلَيْهَا حَتَّى رَأَيْتُهَا وَقَدْ يَبِسَ رِيقُهَا فِي فِيهَا، مَا تَرُدُّ عَلَىَّ شَيْئًا، فَرَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَتَهَلَّلُ وَجْهُهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجة (1981) والإمام أحمد (24620) والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (558) كلهم من طريق خالد بن سلمة، عن البهي، عن عروة بن الزبير، قال: قالت عائشة فذكرته. واللفظ لهما، واختصره البخاري بقوله: دونك فانتصري","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب جواز حب الرجل بعض زوجاته أكثر من بعض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب النكاح","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Majah (1981), Imam Ahmad (24620), and al-Bukhari in al-Adab al-Mufrad (558).","chapter_en":"The Permissibility of a Man Loving Some of His Wives More Than Others","part_en":"The Book of Marriage","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء عن حقوق المرأة المسلمة، وواجباتها، وحسن العشرة بها","group_en":"Collection of narrations regarding the rights of the Muslim woman, her duties, and kind treatment toward her","part_no":24,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿA’ishah said: Before I realized it, Zaynab entered upon me without permission while she was angry. Then she said: O Messenger of Allah, is it enough for you that the young daughter of Abu Bakr waves her hands in front of you? Then she turned against me. I ignored her until the Prophet ﷺ said: “Go ahead and defend yourself.” So I turned on her until I saw that the saliva in her mouth had dried up and she was unable to answer me at all. Then I saw the Prophet’s face light up with joy."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Her word “dhurayʿatayha” is the diminutive form of dhiraʿ (arm)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (1981)، والإمام أحمد (24620)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (558)."}]);